The following is a letter from the people: The project "Sustainability of Cambodia's landscape and eco-tourism" of the Ministry of Environment is moving the private sector to invest in ecotourism in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The "Sustainability of Cambodia's Sustainable Landscape and Ecotourism" project (CSLEP) has organized the first meeting with the private sector in order to present to all investors about opportunities for investment in sustainable ecotourism in the region. Protect nature of the Cardamom Mountains and Tonle Sap Lake landscape.
The event was presided over by Mr. Sao Sopheap, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Project Implementation Unit and Project Implementation Officer, with the participation of thousands of Ministries, Embassy Representatives, Private Sector Representatives and other key international guests at Waterside Restaurant. Phnom Penh on the evening of April 6, 2023.
Speaking at the event, Mr. Sao Sopheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Project Unit, said that CSLEP will create a favorable environment for the private sector to invest in ecotourism development and public-private partnerships, as well as with local communities.
The Secretary of State added: "The current meeting is to create an environment for the private sector to penetrate and participate in the protection and conservation of natural resources and improve the livelihood of local communities through the sustainable use of natural resources for sustainable development. "Especially by investing in the development of eco-tourism in our potential nature reserves."
These areas cover a total area of approximately 7.2 million hectares, accounting for 41% of the total land area of Cambodia. This vast area requires zoning, strengthening, managing and extracting the potential of those natural resources to serve a responsible socio-economic environment and ensure sustainability.
These protected areas have great potential for promoting and promoting tourism, especially ecotourism, including: beautiful natural landscapes, fresh air, biodiversity, forests, wildlife, birds, waterfalls, beaches and beautiful islands, natural heritage sites. And culture, which is an important and sustainable tourist destination to attract national and international tourists to visit.
It should be noted that in order to strengthen and facilitate the participation of the private sector in investing in the development of ecotourism, the Ministry of Environment has announced the implementation of guidelines for the implementation of small-scale ecotourism development projects with a lower land area. 10 hectares are in a protected area and a biodiversity conservation corridor. The book was also distributed to all participants in the program.
