(Pursat): Officials of the Ministry of Environment, civil society organizations and journalists, as well as Pursat Provincial Administration and more than 300 relevant departments march to open the second zero trap campaign in Pursat province on April 7, 2023.
The second Trap Zero Campaign in Pursat Province aims to reduce and prevent the number of traps in protected areas in Pursat Province as well as in other protected areas in Cambodia and to cultivate a greater sense of wildlife among the public. .
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment emphasized that the Zero Trap Campaign aims to further raise public awareness of the consequences of wildlife trapping, wildlife trafficking and wildlife consumption, including risks to public health and loss of resources. Nature, too. The campaign will also continue to spread the word about Cambodia's need for wildlife conservation and Cambodia's rich natural resources to support sustainable development.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that Pursat Province has 6 protected areas: South Cardamom Mountain National Park, Central Cardamom Mountain National Park, Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary, Phnom Oral Wildlife Sanctuary, Tonle Sap Lake and Conservation Corridor. Biodiversity Protected Area The total area is 689,297 hectares.
Family conflict! Man shoots wife and brother-in-law and then shoots himself in the morning in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Preliminary reports said that on the morning of April 7, 2023, a shooting incident occurred in Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province. In this incident, a man shot his wife and brother-in-law and then shot himself in the back, causing a great surprise.
Witnesses at the scene claimed that the gunman first shot his wife in the house and then went to shoot his brother-in-law, who was selling vegetables, then shot himself in the back of the head to end his life.
The source added that the gunman and his wife had just divorced and that the shooting was suspected to be a property dispute. However, the authorities have not yet confirmed the details of this incident.
The gunman's wife and brother-in-law were rushed to a nearby hospital, where they were pronounced dead at the scene.
