13. Singhasari The kingdom of Singhasari was founded by Hindu Javanese based in East Java. This empire existed from 1222-1292. Although short-lived, as it reached its zenith, the Sanskrit Empire conquered the major islands of present-day Indonesia, including Java, Sumatra, Kalimantan, Sulawesi, the Malay Peninsula, and many smaller islands.
25. Melaka The kingdom of Melaka, or Malacca, was founded by the Malay Muslims, who existed from 1400-1511. The empire used to extend to Malacca and other states of Malaysia as well as Singapore.
