Mr. Soeung Sotheany's reaction came after a senior official of the Candlelight Party, Mr. Sok Kimseng, Deputy Secretary General of the Candlelight Party and Chairman of the Siem Reap Candlelight Working Group, attacked the education system as weak.
For Soeung Sotheany, Sok Kimseng's statement does not reflect the reality of education in Cambodia. Mr. Soeung Sotheany said that compared to the post-liberation schools in 1979, the current education situation is better and the children have equal opportunities to study.
In addition, under the policy of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, efforts were made to deploy schools closer to people's homes, making the dropout rate lower.
According to a report by the Ministry of Education, in the 2021-2022 school year, there were 18,430 public and private general education institutions and more than 3.5 million students were studying. According to the data, many religions have been established and the majority of the population is receiving education under the auspices of the Royal Government.
