(Svay Rieng): Mr. Peng Pursa, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, on behalf of Mr. Men Vibol, Provincial Governor and Mr. Em Soth, Chairman of the Provincial CPP, on April 6, 2023, chaired a meeting with stakeholders on the start of the planning process. Election of the 7th National Assembly in 2023.
The meeting was also attended by the Vice President and members of the CPC Chairman and Vice Chairman of the CPC Svay Rieng, representatives of the three forces, the governors / deputy governors of the eight districts, representatives of the provincial information department, representatives of political parties. Representatives of NGOs and election officials of the Svay Rieng CPP.
He made some suggestions to the relevant parties to implement the following:
1. Political parties wishing to contest this election must be prepared and relevant documents in advance in order to apply for the registration of political parties and candidates for the NEC in a timely manner. Set.
2. The National Association of Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs) must also prepare the relevant documents to observe the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 in order to promote the success of this election by following the laws, regulations and procedures for Elections take effect and are based on the principles of multi-party liberal democracy.
3. The Provincial Police Commission, which is the staff of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, must prepare a clear plan to protect the election security in order to ensure a smooth election environment, security, safety, no threats, no intimidation and / or violence.
4. The district / municipal governor shall instruct the commune / sangkat authorities to facilitate and facilitate the issuance of various certificates to the candidates for the National Assembly election of a political party who are legally registered for use in the registration of political parties. And Candidates for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023.
5. The district / municipal governor shall instruct the commune / sangkat authorities to facilitate the issuance of a certificate of the name of a political party agent in the 2022 voter list to a legally registered political party agent for use in the registration process. Agents of political parties in the 7th National Assembly election in 2023.
6. All stakeholders must respect the laws, regulations and procedures for elections and the code of conduct for stakeholders properly and thoroughly in order to contribute to the betterment of the maturity of democracy in Cambodia.
"The president is grateful for the invitation of the British monarch and looks forward to his state visit," White House spokeswoman Karine Jean-Pierre told reporters. She did not specify a date for Biden's visit to the United Kingdom, but said it would take place in the near future.
King Charles of the United Kingdom invited Joe Biden during a telephone conversation on Tuesday. Meanwhile, Biden also told the King of England that his wife, Jill Biden, will be attending his wedding in May. As usual, US presidents do not attend the coronation of the King or Queen of England.
Last year, Biden and his wife visited London to attend the royal funeral of former British Queen Elizabeth. According to the White House, Biden will also begin a four-day visit to Northern Ireland, the United Kingdom and the Republic of Ireland on the occasion of the 25th anniversary of the Belfast Agreement.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Do not think of wild animals as medicine and tonic at all, but consider wild animals as good friends of people
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign, said that please do not think that the flesh and bones of wild animals, medicine is medicine and tonic, but consider wild animals as good friends because animals The forest is a part of everyone’s life.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this remark when he chaired a press conference on the second phase of the zero trap in Pursat province on the afternoon of April 6, 2023.
"Zero Trap Campaign is the object of providing wildlife sanctuaries, providing human safety, to change the attitude of the people around the wildlife, not to take wildlife as a medicine," he said. "Consider wildlife as our friend as a part of our lives because we can depend on nature."
In addition, Mr. Net Pheaktra said that wildlife plays an important role in balancing the ecosystem.
A senior official of the Ministry of Environment confirmed that the Ministry of Environment, together with its partner organizations, is heading to the Cardamom Mountains to launch the second Zero Trap Campaign because the area is rich in wildlife. According to previous studies, the Cardamom Mountains are an area with many traps.
Around this case, the traps in the Cardamom Mountains, Mr. Net Pheaktra said that for two years to collect 66,375 traps that were removed from the protected area. As a result, the Cardamom Mountains have become the largest trapping area and a high risk area for all types of wildlife.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment emphasized that the Zero Trap Campaign aims to further raise public awareness of the consequences of wildlife trapping, wildlife trafficking and wildlife consumption, including risks to public health and loss of resources. Nature, too. The campaign will also continue to spread the word about Cambodia's need for wildlife conservation and Cambodia's rich natural resources to support sustainable development.
