Labor Minister: A school in Vietnam plans to increase 45 scholarships for Cambodian students studying vocational skills
(Vietnam): A school in Vietnam called Thai Nguyen School will increase the number of scholarships for 45 bachelor of engineers for Cambodian students who want to study vocational skills by 2023. This is according to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
In the past, Thai Nguyen School of Vietnam has provided scholarships to 181 Cambodian students to study here, and now 108 more are studying for master's / associate's degrees.
During a visit to Thai Nguyen School on the morning of April 6, 2023, Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that providing scholarships to Cambodian students in the past has really helped and provided them with the opportunity to acquire specific skills and technical skills to To work in Cambodia, especially in factories, enterprises of Vietnamese investors in Cambodia.
In response to the request of Mr. Ith Sam Heng, the Ministry of Labor, Disability and Social Affairs of Vietnam, as well as the leaders of Thai Nguyen Province and Thai Nguyen School, will continue to provide scholarships to 45 more Cambodian students at the bachelor's / engineering level for 2023.
As a token of gratitude, Minister Ith Sam Heng requested the Royal Government of Cambodia to present the Thai Nguyen School Medal to encourage and honor the efforts to help train Cambodian human resources.
