Dr. Moeng Makara, Representative of Dr. Hun Manet, Meets with Pdao Chum Commune Leaders and Former Opposition Activists Who Join the CPP
(Kampong Cham): On Wednesday, April 05, 2023, Dr. Moeng Makara, Chairman of Kampong Cham Province, Cheung Prey District, organized a meeting with 37 former opposition party activists in Pdao Chum commune. Join the CPP at the party office in Pdao Chum commune, Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province.
The main reason for leaving the opposition party to join the CPP is because before the 2022 commune elections, the opposition commune chief candidate promised a lot to them when he was elected commune chief.
When the time came to win the election, the people did not see the opposition commune chief keep his promise, using all kinds of excuses and even blaming his members and the government while he was incompetent. Not at all, only promises the wind.
Instead, they see only the CPP working group continuing to help the people, regardless of party tendencies, building local achievements, even in areas where their party does not have a commune chief.
They came to join the life of the Cambodian People's Party one by one and up to 37 families and are committed to participate in all activities of the party, respect the principles and follow the policy of the Cambodian People's Party well, especially to continue the propaganda activities. Relatives and friends who still support the opposition to come back to live with the CPP in order to jointly protect the peace and national economic development to grow more sustainably.
In fact, on April 5, 2023, Dr. Moeng Makara participated in the inauguration of the incinerator in Hun Sen Pdao Chum High School and had a conversation with more than 500 teachers and students.
Dr. Moeng Makara brought greetings and memories from Dr. Hun Manet to the leaders of Pdao Chum commune, people and former opposition party activists who came to live with all the CPP who were present in the program.
