The handover ceremony was held at LOLC Headquarters by Mr. Sok Voeun, Executive Director of LOLC and Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot, Director of the Department of Legal Education and Rehabilitation of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs.
Mr. Sok Voeun said, "The fight against drugs is a joint task of all of us, not to be considered the exclusive work of any one person or group. The solution is to start with all of us, the elimination of drugs. "It is a major common problem that we must all work together to avoid danger and bring disaster to ourselves, our families and our society."
He urged all stakeholders and all citizens to work together to prevent the spread of the drug problem, which leads to the destruction of communities. He added that the LOLC will continue to fully support the National Anti-Drug Authority to join the fight against drugs.
Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot stated that the LOLC is a good partner who has always supported the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs on outreach, education, fight against drugs and helped social work such as providing wells. Clean water, hand washing facilities in schools, combating the spread of Kovid-19 epidemic, traffic and helping to rescue people affected by floods, etc.
He added that the participation of the Royal Government in implementing the multi-sectoral strategy to fight drugs and the plan to fight illegal drugs is needed from all sectors, especially the private sector, as the LOLC has been doing. Do it now and in the future to ensure the safety, security and order of all citizens, no drugs, no violence, no crime.
