Japanese Ambassador and Kratie Governor Inaugurate a New Bridge in Chit Borey District
(Kratie): Mr. Ou Nou Atsushi, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia, and Mr. Wathon, Governor of Kratie Province, on April 6, 2023, officially inaugurated a new concrete bridge. In Chrava village, Koulab commune, Chit Borei district, with the assistance of Japan through the Provincial Department of Rural Development.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Ou Nou Atsushi expressed his great pleasure that the project to build a concrete bridge in Koulab commune has been completed and ensured the safety and efficiency of daily travel to schools and hospitals. The nearby market will also improve the living standards of the community.
He added that the old wooden bridge was badly damaged and flooded every year. The floods made people wait until the water receded during the floods, and farmers could not transport their produce. Through the newly built concrete bridge, it will be a safe road for local people to travel to different places and get the necessary services for daily life.
"This year marks the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Japan and Cambodia, and bilateral relations between the two countries have been upgraded to a comprehensive strategic partnership from this year onwards," he said. "We value the friendly and historic relationship between our two countries and we believe that this bridge will further strengthen our relationship in the future."
