Kandal Governor Encourages People to Drink Clean Water to Avoid Diseases
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, urged all people throughout the province to use as well as drink clean water and maintain good hygiene to avoid any risk of various diseases.
Therefore, in the celebration of the 30th World Water Day under the theme "Accelerate the provision of clean water and sanitation services to solve the crisis of water and sanitation in rural areas" on April 5, 2023, organized by the Red Cross. Cambodia, Kandal province, in the area of Wat Peam Reang Leu, Leuk Dek district, Kandal province.
Kong Sophorn, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee and Provincial Governor, said that World Water Day aims to raise public awareness of the importance of water and sanitation and how to use water safely, safely and effectively. Good sanitation practices, especially in rural communities.
He added that the lack of clean water and sanitation affects all of us, especially the poor and the most vulnerable. On the other hand, most people in the area still drink unsafe water, which can make them sick on a regular basis, especially the elderly and children, making it impossible for them to go to work or school.
He claims that deaths from cholera and typhoid fever will be relentless due to unsafe drinking. Therefore, we need to address the water and sanitation crisis and promote safe drinking water in rural areas. At the same time, we also need to focus on environmental issues that can seriously affect water quality, both surface and groundwater.
