(Preah Sihanouk): The National Bank of Cambodia has continued to disseminate knowledge on the use of the riel, financial knowledge and the Bakong system to the people continuously. Sihanoukville.
This dissemination was made with the participation of Ms. Chea Serey, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia in the dissemination program on the riel, financial knowledge in Sihanoukville on April 5, 2023.
Ms. Chea Serey said that for the past 25 years, the Cambodian riel exchange rate has been very well maintained during the global financial crisis and the Kovid 19 crisis with an average rate of 4,036 riel per dollar. The United States since 1998, although the change is around 1% per year.
She stated that in 2022, banking and financial institutions in Sihanoukville paid in riel from the National Bank of Cambodia branch 41% of the total cash flow, which increased from about 26% compared to 2021 increase This shows that Sihanoukville is increasing the demand for riel more than before. Registration of Battambang Pomegranate as a collective brand will help expand cultivation and marketing, providing many benefits for producers-traders
(Battambang): The Ministry of Commerce plans to register "Battambang Paddy" as a collective brand, in order to set a common technical standard for coconut cultivation, determine the quality and determine the conditions for using this collective brand of Battambang Coconut Pan, especially to help expand cultivation. And the market provides many benefits for producers and traders.
It should be informed that the Ministry of Commerce plans to officially launch the collective brand "Doung Khtei Battambang" along with some other products in the near future.
He added that in order to promote the use of domestic products and promote the processing of export products as stated in the Trade Integration Strategy 2019-2023, the Ministry of Commerce has been speeding up the registration of geographical marks, goods and collective brands by "Battambang Coconut Pan" is also identified as a potential product for registration as a collective brand to enhance the competitiveness of Cambodian coconut in the national and international markets.
He said that one of the main goals of the Ministry of Commerce is to promote the processing and packaging of coconut pots in Battambang to meet the standards and requirements for export to foreign markets in line with the direction of diversification of Cambodia's exports as part. Support the local production chain to grow.
Mr. Suon Vichea, Advisor to the Ministry of Commerce, Chairman of the Secretariat of the National Committee for Intellectual Property Management and Director of the Department of Intellectual Property, said that Battambang Coconut Coconut is the first young coconut to be grown in three districts: Banan, Sangke and Srok. Ek Phnom.
This Battambang coconut has a thick, soft flesh, aroma, delicious taste in the mouth and can be used as a dessert, fruit, smoothie and provide many benefits to human health.
Seeing the potential and value of Battambang Pan Coconut and a rare coconut that requires very fertile soil and difficult to grow, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, initiated and supported the registration of Battambang Pan Coconut as a collective brand. Chapter 31 on Coconut Products at the Intellectual Property Department of the Ministry of Commerce.
Secretary of State Ouk Prachea also confirmed that after this meeting, the Ministry of Commerce will prepare to complete the application for registration of the collective trademark "Battambang Pan" at the Ministry of Commerce.
