Congratulations to Kampot Province, the 12th Mine Action Province under the Samdech Techo Project for Mine Action, Cambodia Remains 563 Square Kilometers to Be Cleared by 2025
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of April 6, 2023, Kampot Province was declared the 12th Demining Province under the chairmanship of Dr. Cham Prasidh, Senior Minister, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Which supports the Samdech Techo project for mine action under the theme "Provide safe land, create a smile".
Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the cooperation of Kampot Provincial Board of Governors, especially the Provincial Mine Action Committee (PMAC) and the Mine Action Planning Team (MAPO) for this brilliant achievement.
As of the first quarter of 2023, 2,579 square kilometers of landmines and explosive remnants of war have been cleared, of which about 76% is used for agricultural activities to contribute to poverty reduction and Development in Cambodia.
With this effort, Cambodia has 1,885 square kilometers of suspected mines and landmines, of which 563 square kilometers are mined, which Cambodia has ambitions to clear by 2025 and cluster munitions. 729 square kilometers and other unexploded ordnance 593 square kilometers will be resolved after 2025.
