Oknha Song Saran, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that Champey 70 will be a new commodity for Cambodia to compete in the market, especially in the fragrant rice market.
He said that the Rice Federation of Cambodia has gradually started to promote in some major markets, while he expects that 70 Champs grown from Rumduol rice will have a recognized quality that can capture new markets. Fast, currently some markets such as Europe, Hong Kong and Australia are waiting to be tested.
"I think this year or next we can taste it. "We have started advertising in Europe, including France, the Netherlands, Denmark, Germany, Singapore and Australia."
He added that the 70 varieties will make farmers' yields higher than today's rice varieties because the new rice varieties are resistant to diseases and weather, as well as short-term cultivation.
He added that next year he will start contracting with farmers to produce 70 Champis rice, which will be available from July and August. Then, the appearance (size of rice), taste and softness of the rice will be evaluated to determine whether high value-added can be obtained.
Also, this year, the Rice Federation will take 70 Champey rice to participate in the best rice competition in the world with two other types of rice: Phka Romduol and Sen Kraom.
It should be informed that 70 Champis rice varieties are officially present after spending 9 years in research and experimentation in 80 farmers' fields.
Champey 70 is the result of nearly a decade of collaboration between the Cambodian Agricultural Research and Development Institute (CARDI) and the Australian Government.
