(Banteay Meanchey): On April 5, 2023, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police and the Mongkul Borei District Police Inspectorate came out to clarify and completely reject a report posted on Facebook that a man was stoned and injured. Seriously, in fact, the victim fell on his own motorcycle.
Immediately after receiving this information, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Sithy Lod, assigned a specialized police officer in cooperation with the Mongkul Borei District Police Inspectorate to investigate and question whether the victim was actually stoned.
According to the victim, he said that on the day of the incident, he came from the funeral and returned home drunk. After that, he went to buy cucumbers in Ang Khmao village, Koy Meng commune (road to Sramoch village) and rode a motorbike about 400 meters east of the house. Cambodia-Japan Friendship Referral, Mongkul Borei District.
After investigating the scene, investigating and listening to the testimony of witnesses, the police considered that the case posted on social media was not true.
