Cambodia to set up vocational training schools on border with Vietnam
(Hanoi): Cambodia plans to set up vocational training schools on the border with Vietnam to serve the needs of the people of both countries and to exchange technical teachers and students.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, made this point during a courtesy call on Mr. TRAN HONG HA, Deputy Prime Minister of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on April 5, 2023 during his visit to Vietnam.
On that occasion, Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that "Cambodia plans to establish vocational training schools on the border with Vietnam to serve the needs of the people and the two countries and can exchange technical teachers and students." .
Mr. Ith Sam Heng also informed about the recent progress that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training of Cambodia and the Ministry of Labor, Disability and Social Affairs of Vietnam signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in the Field of Labor and Vocational Training in Cambodia last year. November 8, 2022 ago.
At the Cambodia-Vietnam Ministerial Meeting on Labor and recent related meetings, Minister Ith Sam Heng and Minister DAO NGUC DUNG, who co-chaired the joint meeting, also signed a five-year action plan (2023). 2027) To implement the Memorandum of Understanding and Joint Statement on Cooperation in the Field of Labor and Vocational Training.
Deputy Prime Minister TRAN HONG HA expressed full support for the two countries' cooperation on labor and vocational training, which the two ministries recently signed.
The Deputy Prime Minister also requested the Cambodian and Vietnamese Ministries of Labor to further prepare any necessary requirements related to the field of employment and vocational training to be included in the cooperation plan between the two countries.
