(Phnom Penh): Financial and economic experts believe that the rate hike of some banks at this time will add more burden to borrowers, as the current economic crisis has affected them to earn income if banks raise rates. That interest rate will affect the ability to repay and adversely affect the banking sector.
The comments by financial and economic experts come after a number of banks recently announced they were starting to raise interest rates in addition to the previous ones.
He said raising interest rates on existing customers would affect their livelihoods and their ability to repay. At the same time, the increase may reduce demand for loans, which could affect the banking sector.
"When the economy is less favorable and uncertain, it will make it harder for businesses to make a profit, and as banks begin to raise interest rates, it will hurt their customers," he said. "Their payback will be more difficult."
He said that although a 0.5% interest rate hike was not a bad sign, this was contrary to the National Bank's announcement that it would ban interest rates on existing customers or loans without them. No approval from the customer.
He added: "We do not know how things will change in the future. "Hopefully, the bank that issued the letter will consider compliance with the rules and regulations issued by the regulator as well as the government."
Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the current rate hike by some banks did not seem to respond to the circumstances, as people and borrowers were currently facing other problems such as inflation, unemployment. Make and decrease income from doing business. Raising interest rates is like adding a heavier burden to borrowers.
In the dissemination program on Riel, financial knowledge and Bakong system on the occasion of the 43rd anniversary of the re-circulation of the riel in Sihanoukville on April 5, 2023, Ms. Chea Serey, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia. Cambodia has stated that the announcement of interest rate hikes by some banks in Cambodia is due to the impact that Cambodia has received from the US Federal Reserve raising interest rates.
She added that the increase in interest rates was due to the high level of dollarization in Cambodia and the large number of loans in US dollars.
She said that since March 2022, the central bank has raised the benchmark interest rate to lower inflation, which has risen to an all-time high in recent decades, leading to higher international interest rates. Also in early 2023, this influence began in Cambodia, with some banking and financial institutions raising interest rates in US dollars.
She called on ministries, public institutions, institutions, banks and finance, factories, companies, enterprises, business owners and citizens and all stakeholders to continue to use the riel more. If the riel is used in large quantities, the National Bank of Cambodia will be able to control the market interest rate.
In Cambodia, there are more than 100 banks and microfinance institutions operating to provide loans to citizens, including 55 commercial banks, 10 specialized banks, 5 deposit-taking microfinance institutions, 79 non-deposit-taking microfinance institutions, as well as financial institutions. Others.
