Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged this at the 4th Summit of the Mekong River Commission to be held in Vientiane, Laos on the morning of April 5, 2023. In addition to the leaders of the four members of the Mekong River Commission, including Cambodia, Thailand, Laos and Vietnam, the meeting was attended by high-level delegates from Myanmar, China, as well as representatives of some of the Mekong River Commission's development partners.
The leaders of the four Mekong countries delivered keynote speeches on the Mekong River in line with the theme "Innovation and Cooperation for a Sustainable Water Basin."
The Prime Minister called the event of the Mekong River Commission Summit in Laos a special day in the history of Mekong cooperation.
In that keynote address, Samdech Techo stated that the Mekong River is a sustainable source of water that provides social, economic, environmental and cultural benefits for the countries along the river and the well-being of the people both inside and outside the basin. Sustainable growth for all Mekong countries. The cooperation we have made so far and in the future is to work together to ensure the sustainability of the Mekong River and the healthy Mekong River.
Samdech Techo also stated that the sustainable achievement of water, food and energy security is the highest priority in the agenda and objectives of sustainable development in the Mekong region and as well as for the countries along each river. Also.
"All of these factors, combined with climate change, as well as the risks and impacts, require us to pay more attention to working together more effectively." "Cooperate and be on time." This is Samdech Techo Hun Sen's push to respond to the challenges of the Mekong River.
Samdech Techo also encouraged and encouraged the Mekong River Commission to continue to pay attention and work more closely and cooperate better with the member countries of the Mekong River Commission and all cooperation partners for the effectiveness of Implement the 1995 Mekong Agreement in general and the Vientiane Joint Statement of the 4th Mekong River Commission Summit in particular.
However, Samdech Techo expressed the expectation that due to the continued efforts, cooperation and cooperation between each other, the Mekong countries will be able to achieve more major progress towards the common goal is to achieve Achieve a sustainable, prosperous and resilient Mekong River Basin by continuing to benefit each other and forever.
The Minister of Health calls on doctors to provide services to citizens in an ethical and non-discriminatory manner, in accordance with the proverb "Doctors are good patients of their mothers"
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, called on all civil servants to strengthen the technique of changing behavior from bad habits to service providers to the people with morality, dignity and non-discrimination of patients in accordance with the proverb. "The mother doctor has the good morals of the patient," he said.
