Cambodia, Vietnam agree to implement 5-year action plan to enhance cooperation in employment and vocational training
(Vietnam): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training of Cambodia and the Ministry of Labor, Disability and Social Affairs of Vietnam have agreed to implement a five-year action plan (2023-2027) to enhance cooperation in the field of labor and vocational training.
At the Cambodia-Vietnam Ministerial Meeting on April 4-5, 2023, the two sides signed a joint statement between the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training of Cambodia and the Ministry of Labor, Disability and Social Affairs of Vietnam. Focusing on a number of key points, including:
1. Promote cooperation between the two countries in the field of employment and vocational training.
2. Committed to achieving high results on the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding between the two Ministries signed in Cambodia on November 8, 2022.
3. Agree on mutual cooperation to address current trends and challenges, such as the Industrial Revolution 4.0 and labor market restructuring.
4. Exchange views on labor and employment management, development of labor markets and TVET sectors of the two countries, with both sides agreeing to launch a five-year action plan (2023-2027) for the implementation of the above MoU to further change Updates, data, research, skills and work visits, social security and vocational training.
Strengthening the immigration control of the two countries in coordinating the documents required by law and regulations and preventing the recruitment and use of illegal workers, as well as labor exploitation and human trafficking.
