Outcome for the 4th Mekong Summit on "Innovation and Cooperation for the Mekong Basin - Sustainable Water Security" in Vientiane, Laos
MRC leaders recognize that enhancing the opportunities for water, food and energy security available to all Mekong countries can only be achieved through regional cooperation and joint efforts if all countries work together. .
Afterwards, the leaders of the Mekong countries were invited to attend the 4th Plenary Summit of the Mekong River Commission. The summit was attended by the heads of government of Cambodia, Laos, Vietnam and high-level delegations from Thailand, Myanmar, China, as well as representatives of the Mekong River Commission's partner countries.
2. Appreciate the continued financial and technical support from development partners, international organizations, the private sector and other stakeholders provided to the MRC and its member countries, and the cooperation of the MRC dialogue partners and all stakeholders. Lead to the achievement of these and other achievements.
4. Recognize the many opportunities for sustainable development in all areas related to water, including hydropower, irrigation, navigation and other areas, and provide water security to protect society from water risks, especially floods. And drought is very important as an integral part of investment in other sectors and also as an opportunity for development.
11. Strengthen the management of the entire river basin in line with the mandate of the MRC through innovations in technology policies and mechanisms for cooperation and partnerships with other Mekong-related regional cooperation frameworks.
12. Maintain and seek innovative financing to support the above efforts, including through new public and private sources and global funding mechanisms.
14. We reaffirm our commitment to joint efforts to further strengthen the MRC's role in ensuring that the Mekong Basin is secure, water, food and energy and economically, socially and culturally sustainable. Environment.
15. Welcoming the strategic shift towards proactive regional planning and coordinated operational management, and called on all river countries, partners and stakeholders to continue working with the MRC to support the agreement. Mekong 1995 and procedures as well as to support the implementation of the Basin Development Strategy for 2021-2030 in accordance with this statement and the Mekong River in the same spirit.
And 16: Assign the MRC to coordinate and monitor the implementation of this statement.
