Committee on Digital Economy and Business Continues to Discuss Additional Inputs to Develop Financial Technology Development Policy
(Phnom Penh): The Committee on Economy and Digital Business has organized a workshop on the role of decentralized finance and data protection framework in the development of financial technology in Cambodia to discuss with stakeholders in identifying and collecting additional input on Decentralized financial development to lead the drafting of Cambodia's future financial technology development policy.
The workshop was held on April 4, 2023 at the Hyatt Regency Hotel Phnom Penh in order to identify and learn more about the development and impact of decentralized finance to the development of financial technology, components and Mechanisms of the data protection framework of the decentralized system and continue to collect additional input on decentralized finance and data protection framework to prepare a draft policy for the development of Cambodia's financial technology.
The workshop was attended by 130 leaders and representatives of ministries, institutions and regulators, educational institutions, banking and financial institutions, national and international private companies, associations, and relevant international organizations.
He added that decentralized finance could bring many benefits and potentials to the financial sector, but this form of finance has been the subject of much debate in recent years about the risks associated with it. The complexity of regulation, too.
"The continued use of digital technology in the financial sector has created more and more data that is still scattered, unregulated or unprotected," he said. "In this regard, considering the aspects of data protection and management in the development of financial technology is strategically important to increase trust and promote the safe and secure use of this technology."
Dr. Kong Mary, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Secretary-General of the General Secretariat of the Digital Economy and Business Committee, said that traditional management in the traditional financial industry had previously been subject to sector regulation. The two major financial sectors are banking and non-banking finance. But with the rise of finance, decentralization is changing the way financial transactions operate.
The day-long workshop also included a total of six presentations and two discussions on decentralized data and finance.
