This morning, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and Chinese Army Chief Closed the 2023 Golden Dragon Exercise between Cambodian and Chinese Armed Forces
(Phnom Penh): The 5th Golden Dragon Exercise between Cambodian and Chinese troops will end on April 5, 2023. The closing ceremony of the Golden Dragon exercise was presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, and Lt. Gen. Wuy Wenhui, Commander of the Southern Zone of the Chinese People's Liberation Army.
The 2023 Golden Dragon Exercise between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army took place on March 23, 2023. The Golden Dragon Exercise 2023 is held under the theme "Security Operations in Major Events and Humanitarian Relief of the Armed Forces of Cambodia and China." The exercise took place at the Gendarmerie Training Center (Phnom Chum Reak Reay) in Peam commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province.
The 5th Golden Dragon Exercise is designed to exchange experiences and enhance the capabilities of the Cambodian Armed Forces, not to intimidate anyone or any country.
The Cambodian side has 583 troops directly involved in the exercise, while the Chinese side has 257 troops. The exercise was planned a long time ago between the armies of the two countries, not by chance.
The exercise is a link between the two armies in promoting good relations, enhancing solidarity, friendship, training, exchange of knowledge, coordination, living and working together with many nations during joint operations. Each also responds to non-traditional challenges.
