TOKYO: Japan says it has discovered a way to use a laser weapon capable of firing at enemy drones. The discovery of the advanced weapons system comes amid growing tensions in the Indo-Pacific region.
Two Japanese defense companies have unveiled prototypes of their high-powered laser weapons to shoot down enemy drones. The weapon was unveiled during the recently concluded International Defense and Security Equipment Exhibition (DSEI) in Tokyo.
According to the company, the anti-drone system will be able to detect enemy drones using an infrared camera that can track and lock the drone out of the tracking circle and then fire a micrometer laser. Put on goals.
Japan has contributed $ 21 million to research on the laser weapon system. Japan's search for advanced weapons comes amid tensions in the Indo-Pacific region, particularly concerns over Chinese influence, which the United States and Japan consider a regional threat.
At the same time, reports indicate that China has released a new free drone that can fly at high altitudes, and India has also unveiled its new drone. The question is, why have so many countries recently increased their focus on drone production?
