(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works has issued a supplementary instruction on the content of Decision No. 5453/22 dated 15 November 2022 on Procedures for the Management of Printing, Validation and Use of Civil Servants' Identity Cards. Civil. This is according to the instruction of the Ministry of Public Function, which was received by Fresh news on April 4, 2023.
The issuance of these additional guidelines is to facilitate the process of managing the printing and issuance of ID cards for civil servants to be easier, faster and more efficient. The Ministry has made the following recommendations:
1: Preparation of new framework for civil servants
- Ministries and institutions shall prepare the application for the ID card of the new civil servants for the new framework of civil servants together with the application for ID number to the Ministry of Public Function, with the number of units, the number of officials, the list of officials and other necessary data that the relevant ministries and institutions have entered. In the information technology system of the Ministry of Public Works.
Capital, Province, Municipality, District, Khan, Departments and Units at the Sub-National Level shall prepare the application for the ID card of civil servants for the new civil servants in conjunction with the request for ID number to the Department of Public Function of the Capital / Province with the number of units, the number of officers, the list of officers And other necessary data that the relevant entity has entered into the information system of the Ministry of Public Works.
After receiving the request from the Capital, Province, Municipality, District, Khan, Departments and Units at the sub-national level, the Department of Public Function of the Capital and Provinces shall review the request for data and related documents and send it to the Ministry of Public Function for approval.
2: Issuance and activation of cards
A. After verifying the printed card, the bank must contact the cardholder to accept the card and activate the card at any nearest bank branch.
B. The bank must provide a list of officers, ID numbers and card numbers of the officers who have received the card and submit it to the Ministry of Public Works every month to be kept as a document.
3: Reprinting of cards
