President of the National Blood Transfusion Center: Cambodia needs about 500 people a day to donate blood
(Phnom Penh): The President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, Dr. Sok Po, said that Cambodia uses about 250 to 300 units of blood per day, which requires about 500 people per day to donate blood.
He said this at the Ariana International Hospital on Monday, April 3, 2023, when Duke Kuon Thida, Chairman of the Board of Ariana International Hospital, led a number of volunteers to join the National Blood Transfusion Center to save your life. Diseases that are in short supply and need blood to meet the urgent needs of the current blood supply.
Dr. Sok Po said that the blood that was pumped was not sure to be used at all. In general, the pumped blood can not be used 10% after considering both technical problems and considering high blood fat. This means that in order to get about 250 to 300 units of blood, about 500 people are needed, which is why only the National Blood Transfusion Center is looking for volunteers to donate blood to save lives.
According to the doctor in Cambodian policy, the law states that whoever needs a block of blood from the National Blood Transfusion Center must give it back by one person. He said that due to the high demand for blood today, it is also necessary for compatriots to donate more blood because the law also prohibits the sale of blood.
The President of the National Blood Transfusion Center encouraged the public to donate blood without waiting for the right time to donate. In general, he sees that some families need 5 to 6 units of blood at a time, which makes it difficult to find blood to supply.
According to the World Health Organization, Cambodia requires at least 150,000 people, or 1% of its population, to donate blood each year.
The Blood Donation Program on Monday, April 3, 2023 is part of the Ariana International Hospital Humanitarian Program, which is born out of true love and shows the utmost care for the people of Cambodia. . The humanitarian activities that the management and staff of Ariana International Hospital aim to contribute to the National Blood Transfusion Center to meet the urgent needs of the current blood supply.
"Giving blood equals saving lives!" This is the statement of Duke Kuon Thida. Duke Kuon Thida added, "As a highly responsible private institution, we must participate in activities that value the society as well as the general public, so we have established a blood donation program on This.
