A huge fire engulfed a clothing market in the capital of Bangladesh (Video inside) (Dhaka): On Tuesday, a huge fire broke out at a popular clothing market in the capital of Bangladesh, but no There were no reports of injuries or deaths. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, April 4, 2023.
The Bangabazar market, famous for its light clothing, caught fire at 6am. Firefighters from 50 units, including members of the military, joined forces in the firefighting effort. Firefighters said most of the 3,000 or so stalls were reduced to ashes as the fire spread rapidly.
No one was killed or injured in the blaze, according to Bangladeshi authorities, as most of the stalls were closed in the early hours of the morning. Fires often occur at commercial locations in the South Asian country due to lax safety standards.
