Three Chinese Suspects Arrested for Smashing Valuables in Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): On April 3, 2023, at Sihanoukville Port Special Economic Zone, located in Village 3, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, there was a case of aggravated theft (beating a car window, stealing money and valuables). One was caused by an unidentified Chinese suspect who smashed a car window and stole people's wallets.
After receiving the victim's complaint, the light criminal police force, in cooperation with the Sihanoukville Police Inspectorate, conducted a thorough search until April 4, 2023 at 8:30 am. Pointing out Major General Chuon Narin, Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner, the police cracked down completely, arresting three Chinese suspects at Village 2, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville.
After interrogation, the suspects confessed that they had smashed car windows, stolen wallets, equipment and stolen license plates a total of five times, including:
* Hit the windshield of a car and stole wallets and materials 3 times: the first time on March 19, 2023 at the point of Independence Beach Road in Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, the second time on April 2, 2023 2023 at Otres Beach at Village 6, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville and the third time on April 3, 2023 in front of the Port Special Economic Zone in Village 3, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville.
For the above suspects, the Office of Minor Criminal Police is building a case to be sent to the Sihanoukville Provincial Court for legal action. Ratanakkiri Province Prepares Nearly 1,400 Hectares of Land in Lumphat District for Airport (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Nearly 1,400 hectares of land in Ratanakkiri province's Lumphat district is being set aside by the provincial administration for development as a new airport, while the existing old airport in Banlung is being developed as a location for people to relax or park A large garden for the province.
This was said by Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province this morning, April 4, 2023, in the press conference of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on "Five years of success of the administration of Ratanakkiri."
According to Nhem Sam Oeun, the site for the new airport is located between Mondulkiri, Stung Treng, Kratie and Ratanakkiri provinces. The new airport location is a high potential location, about 100 km from Ratanakkiri provincial town.
However, the company that has been awarded the right to invest in the construction of the new airport in Ratanakkiri is not yet available, pending a formal decision from the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC). This is according to the additional emphasis of the provincial governor.
The governor of Ratanakkiri province expressed the expectation that when his province has a new airport, it will attract more investors and be part of helping to boost the economic, social and economic development of local people. He claims that many investors often ask him, when will this northeastern province have a new airport? Because if there is an airport, they will be easier to do business.
