(Kampong Speu): The Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia called on all citizens to use the riel daily as the riel circulation and payment became more digital, all local banks.
Ms. Chea Serey, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, made this call on the 43rd riel day of the introduction of the riel organized by the National Bank of Cambodia on the morning of April 3, 2023 in Kampong Speu province.
Ms. Chea Sereymean said that after the liberation on January 7, 1979, the government strived for national unity to ensure complete peace and rebuilt society and economy from scratch in all areas, and one of the main priorities. At that time, the riel was reissued to facilitate the exchange of goods and services in the economy, especially to build and strengthen national sovereignty.
She said that on March 20, 1980, the riel was officially re-circulated and received great acclaim from all citizens and began to play a number of roles in the transaction, along with the use of assets. Some other prices, especially gold and rice, were the main means of payment in 1979 and in the 1980s.
The Deputy Governor said that due to the prolongation of the civil war until the end of 1998, the trust in the riel was low, while the circulation of the riel was not widespread throughout the country, especially in the border areas.
She encourages the people and all stakeholders in Kampong Speu to continue to use the riel more and more.
She added that under the vision of promoting the use of the riel, the Royal Government and the National Bank of Cambodia have been working closely with stakeholders to support the demand for the riel and make the riel easier to use in daily life as well as for business.
She stressed that the electronic payment system is constantly being upgraded to make the use of the riel easier, no matter how small or large. Bakong payment system using the latest technology "Blockchain and KHQR Code standard facilitates diversion and cross-institutional payments."
