Please be informed that the national anthem "Nokor Reach" written by Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipady Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath has a lot of meaning for the Khmer nation.
An expert on Khmer civilization and author of a book on the history of the national anthem of Nakhon Ratchasima, Mr. Rath Sandab said that according to the content and meaning in the above Nakhon Ratchasima song, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath, he inspired and embed two meanings. For example:
* Second: the metaphor (metaphor) of the rock means that Cambodia has been invaded by plants, neighboring countries, invaded and occupied many places, as well as dominated the power of relentless persecution. .
Mr. Rath Sandab continued that in this sense, Samdech Sangkhareach Chuon Nath, the Lord, did not just bring our hearts to remember the glorious past of the Khmer people. However, he also instilled the spirit of hope in the hearts of the Cambodian people, especially he highlighted that "one day, the fortunes of the past and return to Cambodia."
If this is the case, the Khmer will not perish. The Khmer nation is still strong Khmer. Although the Khmer people have to face dangers at times, the Khmer people are still Khmer people, the Khmer people do not want to submit to anyone, but the opportunity has not been passed yet, they just hold on and keep their mouths shut.
As for the new temples, such as schools, hospitals, small and large buildings, roads, bridges, flyovers, labyrinthine irrigation systems have sprung up all over the country and are moving fast. This means that "the fortune of the great hero" returned to Cambodia, the time of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
