Tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Inaugurates Krouch Chhmar District Referral Hospital, the First Modern District Hospital in Cambodia
On April 3, 2023, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, will inaugurate two large buildings of Krouch Chhmar District Referral Hospital in Tbong Khmum Province with many modern medical facilities.
Under the wise initiative and support of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kat Prith Bundith, the Kroch Chhmar District Referral Hospital Development Project, one of the seven referral hospitals in Tbong Khmum Province, started in July 2020. Krouch Chhmar District Referral Hospital, which covers an area of 12,647 square meters, purchased an additional 6,755 square meters of land, bringing the total area to 19,402 square meters.
The project has started construction of two new buildings and renovation of one old building. The first new building is 18 meters by 62 meters, 4 floors high, construction started on July 27, 2020 and completed on February 11, 2022. There is a general examination room, emergency room, room. Surgery, treatment room, medical laboratory, ultrasound room, X-Ray room and 200 beds.
With the construction of the infrastructure, Krouch Chhmar District Referral Hospital received 17 types of medical equipment, a grant from the KUSANONE (Kusanone) Fund of the Government of Japan, equal to 37 units, totaling approximately 263,760 USD, and turned into A hospital with good infrastructure and equipped with modern equipment.
Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, told Fresh News that, seeing the need to provide health care services to the people, the Krouch Chhmar District Referral Hospital has been developed and upgraded to a level 2 complementary hospital. CPA2) on September 14, 2022.
Ms. Youk Sambath also pointed out that Krouch Chhmar District Referral Hospital is the first district hospital with high capacity to treat patients and equipped with modern medical equipment.
Notably, in recent years, many Cambodian hospitals have been modernized with modern facilities, such as the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Tbong Khmum, and the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Preah Kosomak. And Calmette Hospital. Modernization of treatment with modern medical equipment will make the treatment of patients more effective.
