Khmer Civilization Expert: How important is the decoration of Angkor Sankranti with "art" works for Khmer society?
How important is the decoration of Angkor Sankranti with "art" works for Cambodian society?
When it comes to "art", whether it is our Cambodian nation or the nations of the world, art has the potential to influence culture, politics, the economy and the nation as a powerful force in human society. In creative design to be aesthetically pleasing, transmitted to others with the intention of being attractive and energetic on society, culture and nation.
Because art: expressing cultures from around the world in different forms and aspects to create a culture of thought in thought and action, plays an important role in the fight against racism and other forms of Divide the caste: society to change the way of life to be beautiful.
"In this context, art is a part of the culture that, despite being transmitted and incorporated into different parts of the world, the arts still retain their original identity," he said. Because it is an important ingredient in strengthening the hearts of people who pull the heart and lead to social freedom and influence to make a positive change.
Therefore, art is very important to human society, such as:
First, to promote human education, to create an understanding of what is in the world, to be more equitable in society. Second, to promote cultural values from one generation to another to be more creative. Smart for art, history, culture and traditions of the nation. Third: Promote the speech and expression of people in society better in other areas of knowledge and social dignity.
Mr. Rath Sandab stated that therefore, art is a beauty created to show the emotional response to design, harmony, unity, richness of glorious civilization. At the same time, if any imaginative art form expresses the baseless ideas or feelings of a self-created culture, it also disappears spontaneously at the same time.
