Understand Business: Securities Regulator of Cambodia encourages SME owners to raise funds to expand their business through the securities market in addition to bank loans
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sou Socheat, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, encouraged the owners of small and medium enterprises (SMEs) to raise capital to expand their business by issuing additional securities. Choice of bank loan.
He said that raising funds through the stock market can not only provide capital for SMEs to expand their business, but also help improve business standards, transparency, good governance, the company's reputation, which will strengthen the trust of publishers.
Mr. Sou Socheat made his remarks at the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on "Cooperation on Raising Awareness and Promoting the Participation of Small and Medium Enterprises in the Securities Sector in Cambodia" between the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia. Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association, organized at the Business Development Center on March 31, 2023.
"The securities market is a source of financing for SMEs to expand their growth potential with access to capital by gaining public trust, and it is also an investment channel that provides opportunities for the public and entrepreneurs to become shareholders of the company," he added. "Listing securities in Cambodia is easy and uncomplicated."
Oknha Pech Bolen, President of the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association, said that as of now, the membership of the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association has grown to more than 600 and has branches in six provincial capitals: Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Tbong Khmum and Sihanoukville. In addition, the association will expand its branches to all provinces by 2026, increasing its membership to 1,500.
The tycoon explained to his members how to promote their business by entering the legal system, registering properly without fear or fear of paying taxes.
