Cambodian workers visiting the New Year must enter through international gates, not allowed to enter the corridor or walk through the forest
(Banteay Meanchey): A senior official of the Central Border Police Department has announced that Cambodian workers wishing to leave Thailand for the New Year to return to their hometowns must enter through the international border gates. Do not corridor or walk through the forest because it can be dangerous.
The same senior official also ordered border guards to be ready to protect workers crossing from Thailand into Cambodia and to implement the order properly.
This statement was made during a meeting with the standing forces along the border line in the 5th Zone of Poipet City on March 31, 2023.
Lt. Gen. Leang Phearum, Director of the Central Department of Border Police, instructed and took measures against the forces stationed along the border to prevent Cambodian workers from illegally entering the corridors and crossing the border, as they could be in danger at any time. .
Lt. Gen. Leang Phearum continued, "Forces stationed along the border must guide workers through the international border gates on the occasion of their traditional Khmer New Year visit."
Major General Sim Sam Ath, Director of the 5th Border Police Department, also reminded of the efforts and achievements of the Border Troops along the border.
At the same time, Major General Kheng Sophine, Deputy Director of the Central Department of Border Police, instructed the Border Guard Force to protect the territorial integrity of neighboring countries from invasion and prevent cross-border crime of right-hand drive vehicles, motorcycles and goods. Damage to the quality that smugglers illegally import from neighboring countries must be prevented.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh: SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games will be held in 5 capitals and 17 locations
The statement of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh was made on the occasion that Samdech, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presented $ 411,200 in incentives to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit. The coaches and athletes who won medals from the 31st Southeast Asian Games in Vietnam this morning, March 13, 2023 at the Ministry of National Defense.
On that occasion, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh said that based on the action plan and the special time frame, according to the final inspection and evaluation, we still have some urgent work to be done, such as equipping equipment, technical equipment and decoration. The venue as well as some other related work.
Please be informed that as of April 1, 2023, there are only 34 days left to go to host the 32nd SEA Games, which will be held on May 5. 2023. The hosting of the SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games is a source of pride and prestige for the country and the people of Cambodia, who have been waiting for 64 years.
