The 2023 Hong Kong Policy Report released by the US State Department states that Chinese and Hong Kong authorities continue to use national security as a basis to further undermine the rule of law and freedoms in Hong Kong. The report claims that Hong Kong authorities continue to arrest and prosecute people for expressing peaceful political views against local administrations, including the central government.
China passed the National Security Law for Hong Kong in June 2020. Hong Kong authorities claim the law helped restore order after a riot in 2019. However, since 2020, a total of more than 230 people have been arrested on suspicion of activities that threaten national security.
