The new strategic document underscores the deep Cold War rift between Russia and the West over Moscow's offensive in Ukraine.
"The Russian Federation intends to prioritize the elimination of the influence of US and other unfriendly countries in world politics," the document said.
Russia uses the term "unfriendly countries" to refer to countries, especially in Europe and North America, that have condemned Moscow's military campaign in Ukraine and imposed sanctions on it.
A 42-page document posted on the Kremlin website says Russia intends to "create conditions for countries to reject the goal of new colonialism and hegemony."
At the Security Council meeting, when announcing the policy, Putin said that an update on Russia's strategy for global engagement was necessary as the world was changing dramatically.
The strategy reflects Russia's growing anti-Western stance in the face of Western sanctions and military aid to Ukraine.
