During 2017, two companies that have invested in the production of bags, clothes and well-known brands have trained Cambodian workers who do not have the skills and experience in production to gain experience and techniques on these skills. At the same time, the owner of the company also thanked the governor for supporting and facilitating the company to run better, which can be considered as the tail of the company.
So far, 10 Hong Kong companies have decided to invest in Kampong Speu in the near future due to the belief in the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, especially clear politics. On the national stage and on the international stage.
Of these 10 companies, 1 company focuses on recycling plastic waste, waste for processing into tiles, boards, etc. For building decoration, construction materials and consumables as well. The company has already invested in a number of countries, especially the United States. Mr. Hun Manet encourages the private sector to create new tourism products to restore the sector to grow.
