NEC Chairman: From now until election day, the NEC has a lot of work to do with stakeholders.
(Phnom Penh): According to Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), from now until election day, the NEC has a lot of work to do with all stakeholders. The work must be done in stages and have a clear start and end date.
During the meeting, Mr. Prach Chan said that the NEC has prepared and prepared the master plan, the work calendar and updated the rules and regulations of the election-related legal framework. Procedures, including other legal documents, to ensure the smooth and successful conduct of parliamentary elections.
Mr. Prach Chan added, "From now until the day of the election, the NEC has a lot of work to do with all stakeholders, and that work has to be done in stages and has a clear start and end date." "
Regarding the Calendar of the 7th National Assembly Election, the Chairman of the NEC stated the procedures for the date of registration of national and international observers, national and international journalists, the registration of political parties and the list of candidates. Standing for election campaigns, voting and counting ballots, reviewing and summarizing election results and announcing election results.
Regarding the official election results, the NEC Chairman stated that after resolving the complaints related to the provisional results of the election, the NEC will announce the official election results. Distribute seats and announce elected candidates to the public and all stakeholders.
The NEC answered questions and explained to all stakeholders one by one to understand and confirm that in relation to the National Assembly election, the NEC will have meetings with stakeholders. The stages and themes of each follow-up. Today is the first day of the announcement of the start of the process of preparing for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023.
As a result of the visit to the French Republic, the NEC saw that the electoral system in France was different from Cambodia, and that few countries held elections like France. France made the law and held the election long before the Cambodian election. Overall, at some point, Cambodia is better and easier.
The President of the NEC emphasized that the NEC is an arbitrator who complies with the election law and follows the rules and procedures of the election from the active participation of stakeholders. He hopes that all stakeholders will strengthen cooperation with the NEC in accordance with the election law, regulations, procedures, ethics and other guidelines to ensure a smooth and efficient process. Success.
