Samdech Techo Hun Sen Pays Tribute to the Late Man
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of March 31, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, paid his last respects to the late Grandfather Di Bo, his uncle, who held a traditional Buddhist ceremony at House No. 41. -43, Street 265, Sangkat Teuk Laok 3, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
In front of the photo of the coffin, Samdech Techo bowed his head with the deepest gratitude to the body of the late Dibo, who passed away at the age of 102. By old age.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister dedicated his life to the body of Grandpa Di Bo, referring to the inauguration in heaven without any hesitation.
According to the biography, Mr. Di Bo was born on April 8, 1921 in a farmer family in Peam Krao village, Peam Koh Sna commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province. He has a father named Ouch Di and a mother named Uy Mop.
As a child, Di Bo received a little education at the pagoda and worked as a farmer and trader. He is survived by his wife, Tin Seng, who died in 1987, and 12 children, including three daughters and nine sons, and a total of 43 grandchildren, 62 great-grandchildren and four great-great-grandchildren.
Mr. Di Bo went through many periods from the French colonial period to the present Kingdom of Cambodia, which proves that he was very intelligent and highly resilient. Especially during the era of Democratic Kampuchea (Pol Pot genocidal regime 3 years, 8 months and 20 days), he was forced to work hard, breaking up his family and children like the general population in the whole country.
At that time, he lost his two sons, Mr. Dy Kimsour and Mr. Dy Saron, and has been missing until now. Layman Dibo is known by his relatives as a person who adheres to good deeds, has compassion, and lives in the path of the Buddha, Dharma, and Sangha.
He always helps relatives in times of need and educates his children to walk the path of righteousness no matter what the circumstances. Grandpa Di Bo always leads his children to perform meritorious deeds in the Buddhist way by contributing to the construction of pagodas to support the religion by holding alms-giving ceremonies and other religious ceremonies.
With the careful care of his children, he regained his strength. For more than 2 months, he was in good health, but unfortunately he passed away immediately on Thursday, the 9th day of the month of Chet, the year of Karl Chatva Sak, Buddhist era 2566, which is on March 30, 2023 at 11:45 At noon, at the age of 102, due to old age, there are only 9 days left to reach the age of 103.
The death of the layman Dibo is a great loss to the rich, to be the father, grandfather, great-grandfather, great-grandfather and the most pious relatives to the children.
The body of Grandpa De Bo was buried by his children, grandchildren, great-grandchildren, close relatives and close friends for 3 nights and 4 days, scheduled to be cremated on Sunday, April 2, 2023 at Wat Han Chey, Stung Trang District, Kampong Cham Province.
