Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority calls on business owners in Phnom Penh to use water sparingly to share water shortage in the suburbs
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA) has called on industry and handicraft owners to save water to share clean water to people living in the suburbs of Phnom Penh who are short of water. This is according to the announcement of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, which was received by Fresh News on March 31, 2023.
Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has confirmed that according to the situation of water supply throughout Phnom Penh and Takhmao in the dry season of 2023, there is a severe shortage, causing some suburbs in Phnom Penh and Takhmao do not have access to clean water. Daily.
To solve this water shortage problem before the new water treatment plant is put into operation in early May, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority asks all industrial and handicraft customers to save water in order to share clean water to the people. Living in Khan Sangkat, Cheay Phnom Penh, which is short of water in accordance with the policy of "clean water for all" of the Royal Government through:
1. Save water by reducing daily water consumption
2. Suspend the use of water directly from the state water supply and replace it with water in a reservoir or tank before resuming use.
3. Avoid using the motor to pump water directly from the water supply, which causes the water pressure in the distribution network to drop water to the suburbs.
4. Examine the possibility of changing or adjusting the production time or water consumption during rush hour.
5. For car wash locations, reduce water consumption and ask car owners to reduce or suspend car wash for March and April 2023. Minister of Commerce addresses opening ceremony of China-India Economic Outlook 2023
The Minister praised the important event, which will provide an update on the global economic recovery following the outbreak of Kovid-19 and increase awareness of the economic, trade, investment and tourism aspects of the invited guests.
Why is Beijing angry with the Taiwanese leader's trip to the United States?
BEIJING (Reuters) - Beijing was outraged during a visit by Taiwanese leader Sai Yingluck to the United States. In fact, Sai Ing Wen's visit was aimed at Latin American countries, but required a stopover in the United States, as reports indicate that Sai Ing Wen was planning to meet with the new Speaker of the US House of Representatives. Kevin McCarthy.
Taiwanese leader Sai Ing-wen is stopping in the United States on an overseas trip to Latin America, but her trip appears to be showing other intentions, angering Beijing. Beijing has said that because Taiwan is part of China's territory, state visits to Taiwan are not eligible.
The dispute between China and the United States over Taiwan has raised concerns about the possibility of a new war in the Indo-Pacific, as many countries around the world are suffering from the effects of the Russian-Ukrainian war that dragged on. It has been more than a year now.
"We are calm and confident that it will not yield or provoke," said Sai Eng Wen. Taiwan will firmly walk the path of freedom and democracy and enter the world. "Although the road is difficult, Taiwan is not alone."
There were no immediate reports of injuries or severe damage in the United States. A Taiwanese ambassador to the United States has said all of her events in the United States will not be released to the media.
Zhu Fenglian warned that "if the Taiwanese leader deals with the Speaker of the US Congress during his visit to the United States, it will be a new provocation that seriously violates Chinese policy." One is to undermine China's national sovereignty and to undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan peninsula. "We oppose this meeting and take decisive action to retaliate."
A Chinese spokeswoman said the stop in the United States was a "fake cause" created by the Taiwanese leader. The real reason is to find a way out and want to bring independent Taiwan out of China. "China is not just overreacting to the United States, which is ignoring the conspiracy and continuing to support Taiwanese forces seeking independence," she said.
