Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom urges all enterprises to use foreign labor legally
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Ly Veth, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, urged all enterprises and establishments to cooperate with local authorities in the clear use of foreign labor.
The Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province said this at a ceremony to promote the management of foreign labor in Cambodia to factories, enterprises and establishments throughout Kampong Thom Province on March 31, 2023, organized by the Provincial Department of Labor and Vocational Training.
He said that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, has created favorable conditions for the promotion of socio-economic development, attracting investment both in the country and abroad, as well as the influx of one million foreign tourists visiting Cambodia. The years that have driven Cambodia to achieve high economic growth over the last decade.
Mr. Ieng Sopheap, Director of the Provincial Department of Labor and Vocational Training, stated that the current outreach meeting has the following main objectives:
1. Promote the management of foreigners, stay, do business and work in Cambodia.
2. Strictly enforce the labor law and the immigration law as well as the relevant legal documents.
3. Disseminate foreign labor inspection related policies and measures to owners or directors of enterprises and establishments to support operational plans to increase employment, combat all forms of human trafficking, labor trafficking, sex trafficking, crimes related to illegal gambling or online fraud or Money laundering or other offenses to take legal action.
It should be noted that Kampong Thom province has a total of 407 enterprises with 14,320 workers, 5,428 of whom are women, of which 35 enterprises using foreign labor have a total of 684 foreign workers, 133 females of 19 nationalities. .
