It should be noted that the chairmanship of the UN Security Council is changed every month among the member countries and in the order of the initials of the members' English names. The last time Russia took over the presidency was in February 2022, the month in which Russia began its war of aggression in Ukraine.
"Russia is a permanent member of the UN Security Council," she said. "Russia should not have this position because of what it is doing in Ukraine." However, the US ambassador said that the UN charter does not allow for a change in the status of a permanent member of Russia's Security Council.
The UN Security Council is one of the top international peacekeeping bodies in the world. The UN Security Council votes and makes decisions on security issues that all UN members are obliged to comply with. It has 10 rotating members and 5 permanent members: the United States, Russia, China, the United Kingdom and France, all with veto power.
