The Taiwanese Defense Ministry said in a statement that the nine Chinese military aircraft flew over the northern, southern and central points of the Taiwan Strait, which serves as the unofficial border between the two sides. The Taiwanese military also responded by mobilizing its aircraft and ships to monitor the situation.
Taiwan's Defense Ministry said the move of Chinese military aircraft was a deliberate act of tension in the Taiwan Strait and not only affected peace and stability, but also had a negative impact on security and economic development in Taiwan. Area as well. Taiwan's Defense Ministry has condemned China's actions as "completely unreasonable."
Although Beijing has never officially recognized the median line in the Taiwan Strait, the Chinese military has just begun moving ships and military aircraft to pass through it after a controversial visit to Taiwan in August last year. Nancy Pelosi, who was then Speaker of the US House of Representatives. At that time, tensions escalated in the Taiwan Strait.
Egypt considers opening embassy in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, led a Cambodian delegation to pay an official visit to the Arab Republic of Egypt from March 29 to 30, 2023 at the invitation of Mr. Sameh. SHOUKRY Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Arab Republic of Egypt.
The two Ministers highlighted the significance of the visit, which coincided with the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Arab Republic of Egypt, and discussed the potential for strengthening and expanding cooperation in various fields. More.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Foreign Minister Sameh SHOUKRY also agreed to consider establishing a bilateral consultation between the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs as a mechanism to explore ways and means to strengthen and expand cooperation on all fronts. Sector. In this regard, the two Foreign Ministers agreed to push for the signing of a memorandum of understanding in the near future.
In response to the development of relations, Minister Sameh SHOUKRY informed Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon that Egypt would consider opening its embassy in Phnom Penh. The two Foreign Ministers noted that the volume of bilateral trade is still limited and stressed the need to boost trade and economic cooperation, as well as to promote communication between relevant ministries. Of both countries.
