Officer: Understanding the obligations of restaurant business registration is important for entrepreneurs or those who want to open a restaurant
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kim Serey, Deputy Secretary General of the National Committee for Clean City Assessment and Director of the Department of Accommodation, Tourism and Food Services of the Ministry of Tourism, highlighted the importance of entrepreneurs or restaurant business owners who have just started a restaurant or are looking to take a step. To enter the restaurant sector, it is necessary to understand the obligation to register a restaurant business.
He added that in order to facilitate quick and easy registration, the Cambodian Restaurant Association has published a book entitled Restaurant Business Registration for 8 Days, which is the most important book for restaurant business owners.
The Cambodian Restaurant Association has organized the official launch of the book on the obligation to register a restaurant business in Cambodia with the participation of officials from various ministries, including: Ministry of Tourism, Ministry of Environment, Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, Ministry of Interior, Ministry of Health , Ministry of Environment on March 30, 2023.
This book on the obligation to register a restaurant business in Cambodia is very important for entrepreneurs and restaurant business owners, small, medium, large or those who are planning to open a restaurant business.
The book on the obligation to register a restaurant business in Cambodia was prepared by the team of the Cambodian Restaurant Association in 2023 in order to mainstream knowledge related to restaurant business registration in Cambodia for the convenience of readers, this book is prepared in two parts. The languages are Khmer and English.
Mr. Kim Sereyroth said, "This book is very important for all restaurant businesses operating in Cambodia, providing knowledge to entrepreneurs in the restaurant business, both small and medium. "This book highlights the importance that entrepreneurs or restaurant business owners need to understand the obligations of registering a restaurant business and explains in detail the information that business owners need to have and understand."
He added that he appreciated the launch of the book on the obligation to register a restaurant business in Cambodia and requested that it be widely disseminated so that the public could better understand it.
The Restaurant Association believes that this work will contribute to the promotion of legal compliance, especially the business registration culture in Cambodian society, to ensure a fair business environment, which is an indispensable part of implementing the in-depth reform of the government's Rectangular Strategy.
