(Phnom Penh): With the move towards the CPP's prime ministerial candidate for the future, Dr. Hun Manet is a busy politician who regularly engages in important public activities. In fact, in June 2022, Dr. Hun Manet also had seven important public missions.
Below is a video summarizing the mission of Dr. HUN Manet in June 2022: This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen handed over certificates and diplomas to more than 6,000 trainees and students of the National Institute of Business.
(Phnom Penh): This morning, Thursday, March 30, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the handing over ceremony of certificates and diplomas to more than 6,000 trainees and students of the National Institute of Business after their graduation. Successfully. The event will be held at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the total number of trainees and students who received this certificate and degree was 6,051, 3,895 females.
According to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Samdech Techo has already presented certificates and diplomas to the trainees and students of this institute twice. The first was held on May 08, 2002 and the second on December 25, 2006.
According to the Minister, the National Institute of Commerce was established in 1979 as the "Central Technical School of Commerce" under the auspices of the Ministry of Commerce. In 1985, it was renamed the Commercial Secondary School. In 1994, it was transferred to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and in 2001 it was renamed the National Institute of Commerce.
Since 2004, the National Institute of Business has been transferred under the auspices of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. The institute is responsible for training students and business students in the field of business and services from short to long term, both public scholarship students and students paying tuition fees.
The institute has a management team of 145 contracted Khmer-foreign professors and staff, 37 females, including 3 doctoral students, 1 female, 90 senior bachelors, 17 females, 22 bachelor / engineers. 6 females and 30 undergraduates, 13 females.
According to the Minister, trainees, graduates get 99.36% of the jobs.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that the National Institute of Business is an educational institution that has received the accreditation of technical and vocational education and training institutions through the accreditation from the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia (ACC). ), Quality Assurance Certificate of Technical and Vocational Education and Training Institutions from the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and ISO 9001: 2015 Certificate.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng also highlighted that technical and vocational education and training is one of the priority areas of the Royal Government's political program to invest in human resource development. The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is promoting the education, technical and vocational training sector in collaboration with ministries, institutions, development partners, NGOs and the private sector to achieve remarkable results.
The ministry has continued to promote the training of about 130,000 apprentices and test the recognition of 1,350 previous learners.
On March 21, 2023, the Royal Fire Extinguishing Ceremony for the 32nd Southeast Asian Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023 officially started and will continue to run through the 10 countries of Southeast Asia. Before returning to Cambodia to officially celebrate the 32nd SEA Games, China will increase lending to countries along the "Belt and Road" project.
China has provided $ 240 billion in loans to 22 developing countries facing bankruptcy risk over the past two decades, a trend that has escalated in recent years. . According to the AFP news agency.
The AFP news agency quoted a new study as saying that almost all of the funding was given to countries along the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI), such as Sri Lanka, Pakistan and Turkey, most of which are nationals. Low- and middle-income earners receive loans from China for infrastructure development.
Around the world, countries on the BRI initiative have been struggling as rising inflation and interest rates, coupled with the chronic effects of the Kovid-19 pandemic, have hampered the ability to repay. Its debt.
According to the report, the bailout allows countries to continue their loans and still be able to repay their debts.
China says more than 150 countries have signed up to the BRI Initiative, a $ 1 trillion global infrastructure promotion project launched by President Xi Jinping a decade ago. Beijing said the initiative aims to deepen friendly trade ties with other countries, especially in the developing world.
But critics have long accused China of luring low-income countries into a debt trap by offering too many unfavorable loans.
"China has established a bailout system for belt and road projects that will help bailers avoid bankruptcy and continue to provide their BRI debt service for at least the next term," the report added. Short time.
Compared to the International Monetary Fund and the large amount of liquidity support provided by the US Federal Reserve, China's bailout is still small but growing rapidly, the report said.
"Beijing has targeted a number of potential borrower recipients, as almost all of China's bailout loans have been provided to low- and middle-income BRI countries with Chinese bank debt," the report's authors wrote. A lot.
US, Japan reach mining trade agreement for electric car batteries
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States and Japan this week announced a trade agreement on ores for the production of electric car batteries, a key step in strengthening their countries' battery supply chains. According to the Reuters news agency.
The Reuters news agency quoted a senior US government official, President Joe Biden, as saying that the swift agreement barred the two countries from restricting bilateral exports of the most important minerals. For electric car batteries.
These minerals include lithium, nickel, cobalt, graphite, and manganese.
The agreement also aims to reduce US and Japanese reliance on Chinese ores by requiring cooperation to combat other countries' "non-market policies and practices". More in this area and cooperation on overseeing foreign investment in their key mineral supply chains.
