(Tbong Khmum): Tbong Khmum Provincial Police Commissioner held a meeting on March 29, 2023 to review the situation and the results of operations in 2022 and disseminate the direction of the Ministry of Interior and the General Commission of National Police 2023 in the presence of Lt. Gen. Chea Pov, Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police, representing General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, and Mr. Nop Lundy, Deputy Governor.
The meeting was held at Tbong Khmum Provincial Police with the participation of Generals, Colonels, Deputy Commissioners, Chiefs of Special Offices, 7 Municipal Inspectors, Commanders, Chiefs of Commune / Sangkat Administrative Police Stations.
On this occasion, Lieutenant Colonel Lay Lay, Deputy Commissioner for Planning, read the report summarizing the work achieved by the police in 2022. Identifying strengths, weaknesses, monitoring and evaluation to set out a plan for implementation next year.
Addressing the forces, Major General Mon Mekar reminded all police forces in all provinces, especially at the commune / sangkat administrative posts, to be gentle in gestures and words when providing public services to the people.
He added that the traffic police must implement the law well and continue to disseminate the law and traffic accidents widely to reduce accidents and deaths.
In addition, in each district, the complex goal is to encourage people to install security cameras to make it easier to investigate, prevent and crack down on crime, in order to ensure 100% security for local people.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Chea Pov said that for 2022, crime in Tbong Khmum has decreased due to the efforts of all police forces.
The Deputy Chief of the National Police also said that before the New Year, there is a risk of crime because most people go to their hometowns to face theft, burglary and fire, so all police forces must There will be more vigilance and tightening, especially to be ready to intervene at all times, waiting for the order of the leadership when any necessary situation arises.
On that occasion, the delegation also handed over certificates of appreciation to the Chiefs of the 7 Special Offices of the Municipal / District Inspectors, Chiefs of the Commune / Sangkat Administrative Police Stations.
