Iran's foreign minister says Tehran and Moscow are in the final stages of signing a long-term cooperation agreement (Video inside) (Tehran) Tehran and Moscow are taking the final step towards signing a long-term cooperation agreement. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, March 29, 2023.
He said the high-level Iranian and Russian delegations exchanged views at different levels and that the presidents of the two countries have always been in touch.
The senior Iranian diplomat noted that relations between Tehran and Moscow are on the "right path" and are improving, expressing hope that bilateral cooperation in regional and international organizations will continue. Positive.
Speaking to reporters during a visit to Moscow on Tuesday night, Amir Abdollahian said Russia had played an active role in months of negotiations in Vienna over the resumption of the nuclear deal. Signed between Iran and the superpower in July 2015 and was withdrawn unilaterally by the United States in 2018.
Referring to US concerns about Iran's defense cooperation with Russia, he said that defense cooperation was on the agenda of Tehran and Moscow, but such cooperation Will not focus on any third party.
