The Bar Association of Cambodia filed a lawsuit against Mr. David Chhay Nava with the Phnom Penh Municipal Court
(Phnom Penh): The Bar Association has decided to file a lawsuit against David Chhay Naiva with the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for misrepresenting his legal status as a lawyer and publicly insulting the Bar Association.
In a statement issued by the Bar Association, in May 2021, David Chanaywa, a Facebook user, claimed to be a lawyer involved in interpreting a case. At that time, the Bar Association issued a press release denying that David Chanayva was not a lawyer.
On May 21, 2021, the Bar Association received a letter of explanation from David Chanayva, publicly apologizing and appealing to the public not to be confused again because he did not have the name of a lawyer in the Bar Association. Of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
(Riyadh): Saudi Arabia's cabinet on Wednesday approved a decision to join the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) as Riyadh continues to build long-term ties with China despite the revelations. Concerns about the United States over security issues. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, March 29, 2023.
Originally founded in 2001 by China, Russia, along with former Soviet states in Central Asia, the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) has now expanded to include India and Pakistan with the aim of playing a bigger role. More to resist Western influence in the region. Iran also just signed a document to become a full member of the organization last year.
However, Riyadh's growing ties with Beijing have alarmed Washington, its longtime security ally. Washington has argued that China's attempts to sow influence around the world will not change US policy toward the Middle East.
In the past, Saudi Arabia and other Arab states bordering the Persian Gulf have expressed concern over what they see as the withdrawal from the region by the United States, the main security guarantor. They also began to diversify partners. However, Washington says it will remain an active partner in the region.
