(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, called on the people living in Siem Reap Province not to believe in the incitement of some brokers, which led to falling into committing illegal acts without realizing it, especially related to land issues.
In the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit on "Five Years of Success of the Siem Reap Provincial Administration" on the morning of March 29, 2023, the provincial governor claimed that as Cambodia nears the election, the broker They often incite people to protest over land issues while the authorities are continuing to try to mediate.
Mr. Tea Seiha's call came after residents of Balang commune, Prasat Bakong district, recently filed a petition with the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and the Ministry of Interior, claiming that the authorities did not register the land. Give them. Of those who submitted the petition, about six were incited by the authorities.
Mr. Tea Seiha said, "During the election season, the protesting community, together with some brokers, has provoked the movement, sometimes the people live in harmony, even though the land is not registered according to various legal standards, but when the election is approaching, the brokers will Go to them. I call on the people not to trust brokers who push them to act illegally.
The provincial governor pointed out that in the case of people living on the border of Banteay Srei and Prasat Bakong districts, they often protested in connection with land registration when the land was in trouble and the provincial authorities tried to mediate. This case of conflict is between the people and the people, not the people and the state.
In addition, Mr. Tea Seiha also called on people not to worry about losing their land, even though it has not been registered in accordance with the law. While Hean said that people should not worry about the loss of land because the local authorities and the competent forces have prevented the encroachment and removal of the border posts of each party.
It should be informed that in relation to the systematic land registration work for 5 years, Siem Reap province has issued a total of 48,476 title deeds, which are implemented in 6 cities and districts in 12 cities and districts throughout the province.
Since the beginning of 2004, the province has registered 152,291 plots of land in 167 villages, issued 81,644 land titles in 87 villages, and the remaining 70,647 plots due to the demarcation of 1 and Two areas of the Tonle Sap Lake Authority are not clear and some because after posting there are complaints and have not been resolved.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Chea Van Det's participation in the closing ceremony of the National Day "Science, Technology and Innovation" on the evening of March 28, 2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Chea Vandeth stated, "In the three years that I have been the Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, we have undergone a lot of reform work, and as a result, state revenue has quadrupled in three years. This year compared to three years ago when I joined the ministry.
Mr. Chea Vandeth said that this is a great achievement that makes the civil servants in the Ministry enthusiastic and happy, and he recently conducted a survey of officials in some departments, officials support 100 percent of the correction. Ministry form.
In addition, Minister Chea Vandeth stated that the result was that all officials received a decent salary in addition to their salaries, which could make his life easier and make him turn from the private sector to work in the state. Some officials working in the private sector have come to work at the ministry to help develop the ministry.
The minister also said that in the reform, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has focused on three areas: the postal sector, e-commerce and technology and telecommunications.
He said that the postal sector is working with private companies that are preparing to implement technology nurseries to support e-commerce. In addition, the ministry is also developing a technology system that tracks the count of all goods from one destination to another to make the postal sector grow.
Minister Chea Van Det said that in the next 5 to 10 years, according to some economists, e-commerce will be a major sector in each country's national economy, as well as in In the world, too.
In the field of information technology and telecommunications, the Ministry has set out a vision to do the next 5 to 15 years, Cambodia, both public and private sectors are transformed into a sector that uses technology in In public affairs as well as private affairs. This is the confirmation of Minister Chea Van Det.
