(Siem Reap): General Meas Savon, Director General of the General Department of Military Service of the Ministry of National Defense, called on the Cambodian people to unite to protect the peace and achievements that have been built as at present, at all costs, to be absolutely protected so as not to Let our children suffer like the people of the past.
This was stated by General during the ceremony of conferring ranks on officers on behalf of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense at the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Kulen 317 Siem Reap Disability Military Development Center on the afternoon of March 28, 2023 at District Administration.
He stated that Samdech Techo set a win-win policy for national unity on December 29, 1998, so we consider December 29, 1998 as the day of full peace and national unity. We must thank peace, thank politics, win-win and be grateful to the founders, guides and win-win political operators who have brought peace and complete national unity.
Mr. Meas Savon stated that Cambodia only achieved full peace in 1998, but we must not forget that we must work hard to protect peace, protect our children so that they do not go to the guns and bullets through the fields and forests like our generation, it is very difficult Until we achieve peace, we must work together to protect the achievements we have sacrificed, some lost our lives, some lost our eyes, some lost our limbs, and some of our bodies returned to peace today.
Therefore, the sacrifice of some of our limbs is not in vain, we have returned to peace for our descendants, and our role is to maintain peace, national unity for the future of our descendants.
He also commended Lt. Gen. Pov Sea, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Military Service, Ministry of National Defense and Director of the Center for the Development of Disabled Soldiers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Kulen 317 Siem Reap, for strengthening the base of Prasat Commune, Varin District, Siem Reap Province. Willingness to join hands to lead the team to strengthen at the grassroots level.
He urged the working group to continue this work to achieve the goal of long-term peacekeeping, and he also instructed the soldiers in the center that we need to protect the local area from gambling. Theft, sex trafficking, drug trafficking, and other illegal activities are not allowed in the center, and the policy of safe villages and communes is to be implemented.
On that occasion, Mr. Meas Savon also called on all soldiers, families, soldiers and people to be ready to participate in the election.
Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications Releases $ 20 Million to Promote Digital Technology Education in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) Deposit $ 20 million plus $ 3 million a year to promote digital technology education.
Mr. Chea Van Det made the remarks during the closing ceremony of the National Day "Science, Technology and Innovation" on the evening of March 29, 2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
Mr. Chea Van Det said that the field of digital technology is very important and soon all universities will have a digital management system with a data provided to the Ministry of Education to know and manage information well.
He said that the digital technology sector in Vietnam has up to 150,000 graduates per year, but in Cambodia we have only more than 1,000 graduates, this is an inaccurate figure that can be below or above. Only a little.
"These are the factors that make the Ministry strive to provide digital technology scholarships to more than 1,000 students, and in addition, the Ministry has organized a program that requires students to come and receive funding to study at school or university. "As long as they pass the exam, the ministry will set aside $ 20 million plus $ 3 million a year to support digital technology education."
He said that the budget program, the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation can also request some funds to research and train other technologies.
