General knowledge: The oldest flag in the world
Today, the Nordic countries use the cross on their flags, such as Denmark, Norway, Finland, Sweden, Iceland. The use of crosses to mark the flags dates back to the 13th century.
However, the world considers the Danish flag to be the oldest, as it has been in use since the 13th century, dating back to the Battle of Lindenice in 1219.
