The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SET) has confirmed that it has agreed in principle on the application to examine the feasibility of listing on the Stock Exchange of Cambodia (BCG) on March 29, 2023.
In order to be officially listed and traded on the Cambodia Securities Exchange, Cellcard must be licensed to issue IPOs and must meet certain other conditions related to listing on the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
Please be informed that Cellcard is the second company that has been approved in principle on the application to examine the feasibility of listing on the Cambodia Securities Exchange in 2023 and is also the ninth company that plans to list on the Stock Exchange of Cambodia. Cambodia Securities Exchange as well.
It should also be noted that Cellcard was established in 1996 to provide one of the leading telecommunications services in Cambodia, including the installation and operation of all devices and equipment used in connection with the operation of the GSM mobile network.
BEIJING (Xinhua) - China's first Honduras-based media agency, jointly licensed by the two Ministries of China and Honduras, the Tegucigalpa Journalist Station of the Central Radio and Television of China, held a grand opening ceremony. To be held at the Honduran President's Office on March 28, local time. This is the 191st foreign correspondent station of China Central Radio and Television.
Also at the ceremony, the Central Radio and Television of China and the Honduran National Radio and Television Station signed a letter of intent on exchange and cooperation. The two sides will cooperate in many areas, such as institutional establishment, cooperation mechanisms, program content, people-to-people exchanges and industrial cooperation.
"Please join us in congratulating this historic event that will lead to a brighter future between the two countries," the Honduran President's Office said in a statement.
Nearly one hundred members of the Honduran media, culture and arts media attended the opening ceremony, and many major Honduran media outlets covered the event.
