Senior officials of the Ministry of Commerce continue to encourage Chinese investors to invest more, Cambodia ensures a favorable environment
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhuon Dara, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, continued to encourage and welcome Chinese investors to invest in Cambodia with more investment with confidence.
Mr. Chuon Dara made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the Cambodia-China Entrepreneurship, Economic, Trade and Investment Cooperation Summit held on March 28, 2023, with the participation of a large number of Chinese and Cambodian investors.
"We welcome the return of more Chinese businessmen and investors to do business in Cambodia than during the pre-Kovid-19 outbreak," he said. In Cambodia, we would like to ensure that all investors have a conducive environment for investment, especially Cambodia is peaceful, secure and politically stable, as well as macroeconomic stability, legal framework and institutions that are effective, transparent and accountable.
He said, "I would like to encourage you to find out how to do business, invest and do business in Cambodia is not wrong, because Cambodia is in a strong situation from day to day from year to year and Cambodia is in the country. Which also receives tax incentives. ”
He added that Cambodia has great potential through the introduction of the Royal Government's policy on trade facilitation, which makes it easier for businesses to do business in Cambodia through tax incentives for investors and secondary factors. Others. Cambodia also has important economic poles for business investment, such as Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville, Siem Reap and many other major poles that are favorable in the field of both agriculture.
"I would like to call on all traders and investors to decide to invest in time to take advantage of the markets that Cambodia receives from developed and developing countries in a favorable environment."
Bilateral trade between Cambodia and China in 2021 will reach 11,194 million US dollars, of which Cambodia exported more than 1,510 million US dollars to China and imported more than 9,684 million US dollars from China. With an increase of about 38% compared to 2020.
In addition, Cambodia has continued to cooperate with China on a wide range of trade-related issues, including the establishment of nine Cambodian private business centers in several major cities in China to promote potential Cambodian products. From Cambodia's culture, tourism and trade and investment policy, as well as boost exports to the Chinese market.
