The ceremony at Wat "Ponleu Pich Kiriram Phnom Kralanh" in Prek Prosop district, Kratie province enters the second day and there are a series of benefactors
(Kratie): The wedding ceremony of 109 Buddha statues, holding the 9 Po crosses and other achievements in the pagoda "Ponleu Pe 1, Chiri Kiriram, Phnom Kralanh" in Sop Leu village, Sop Leu commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province. Entering the second day, with Buddhists and philanthropists from near and far invited to participate in the festival and entered the suffix for the construction of the pagoda directly and indirectly according to their respective generosity.
On March 28, 2023, the second day of the festival, Major General Lor Meng Huot, Deputy Director of the Traffic Department of the Ministry of Interior, and his wife were invited to participate in the festival. On that occasion, the lieutenant general and his wife donated 2 million Riels for the construction of the pagoda and supported 4 police officers and 19 police officers, each of whom received 2 sets of clothes and 20,000 Riels. Well.
The abbot of the pagoda, Sachchak Kalyana Sennara, said that he, together with the committee of abbots and Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda, had agreed to celebrate the Buddha's wedding and pass on this achievement to be kept as a sacred object in the pagoda. It is a place of worship for Buddhists of all generations.
It also refers to the dissemination to the Buddhist philanthropists, both inside and outside the country, know that a pagoda is poor and suffixed to continue to build many other achievements in the pagoda, which does not currently exist, such as Kod Temple, Chan School, Dharma School. And so on, which must be built as a necessity.
On that occasion, he also thanked and blessed all Buddhists, especially Major General Lor Meng Huot and his wife. Major General Heng Lalin and his wife, Brigadier General Yim Saran and his wife, as well as all local and foreign philanthropists who are generously involved in the construction of the pagoda.
Please note that Wat Ponleu Pich Kiriram Phnom Kralanh was built more than 20 years ago, located on a mountain in a remote area far from the town and the village is the poorest temple in Kratie province. Until now, there are no temples, halls, or synagogues, only small wooden huts built for monks to live in.
