Minister of Health inspects the construction process of Calmette Hospital Techo Development Building, which is scheduled to be officially opened soon
(Phnom Penh): The Techo Development Building of Calmette Hospital is currently accelerating the construction and equipping of modern medical equipment imported from abroad and is scheduled to be completed soon. The building is also scheduled to be officially inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in the near future.
In order to expedite the construction process, on the morning of March 28, 2023, Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, inspected the construction process of the Techo Development Building of Calmette Hospital to make sure that it is completed as planned.
On that occasion, the Minister said that in accordance with the decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to make Calmette Hospital more modern and basic to treat people more effectively. Reduce people from going abroad for treatment.
Prof. Mam Bunheng said that the Techo Development Building of Calmette Hospital is not just built to build the infrastructure, but to be equipped with modern medical equipment imported from Germany and the United States to meet. The needs as well as the expectations of the Cambodian people on public health services in line with effective and efficient globalization.
The Calmette Hospital Techo Development Building has 10 operating rooms equipped with the latest medical equipment. Built in line with state-of-the-art construction engineering techniques, it is easy to use, interconnected, high quality and durable, suitable for state-of-the-art medical equipment. Famous brands with a team of doctors specializing in all specialties.
It should be reminded that Techo Aphivath Building, a multi-specialized center, was inaugurated in early March 2018. The new 465-bed facility will be equipped with state-of-the-art medical technology that brings together all the major medical and surgical specialties, including the emergency department of modern multidisciplinary care. While on the top floor of the Techo Development Building of Calmette Hospital, there is also a helicopter landing pad.
