Ma Ying-jeou was the first former Taiwanese leader to visit China since Zhang Kai-hek's nationalist government fled to Taiwan in 1949 after losing the civil war under the Communist Party. His visit comes amid rising tensions as Beijing continues to use political and military tactics to try to pressure Taiwan to accept Chinese sovereignty.
Taiwan's ruling party has questioned why he is still visiting China, as Beijing has just recaptured another of Taiwan's diplomatic allies, Honduras, on Sunday. This leaves Taiwan with only 13 diplomatic countries.
