The Ministry of Tourism recommends that all capital-provincial departments continue to strengthen the management of informal economy staff in the tourism sector.
(Phnom Penh): Pursuant to the policy of the Royal Government and the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Ministry of Tourism has instructed all capital-provincial tourism departments to continue to strengthen the management of informal economy staff in the tourism sector. Efficiency.
This introduction was made in the meeting to review the results of women's work and informal economy in the first quarter of 2023 in the morning of March 28, 2023 at the Ministry of Tourism, chaired by Ms. Hun Dany, Secretary of State and Representative Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism.
The purpose of the meeting is to review the progress of women's work and the informal economy in tourism at both the national and sub-national levels, study the challenges and set out the implementation direction for the second quarter of 2023 to strengthen management mechanisms. Businesses and female employees working in the informal economy in tourism, as well as empowering women in the tourism industry.
At the meeting, the Secretary of State said that women play an important role in tourism, with nearly 60% of the 320,000 workers (2022 tourism indicators). In particular, in the field of tourism services, women account for more than 70%.
In order to implement the policy of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Tourism has always paid attention to the group of women working in the tourism sector by launching programs and strategic plans aimed at promoting the status, role and values of women in the partnership. Employment framework and increase economic resilience.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Soeung Sotheany, President of the Khmer Kampuchea Krom Charitable Association, claimed that the arrest of three Siamese ivory party members involved in the case of forgery of documents to form the National Heart Party in the past is not political.
