Samdech Techo Hun Sen Calls on Agricultural Farm Owners to Provide Complete, Accurate and Honest Data to Agricultural Census Officers
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has called on agricultural farm owners and families of all types of agriculture to provide complete, accurate and honest information and interview information to agricultural census officials. This is according to the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the agricultural census in Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on March 28, 2023.
According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the agricultural census in Cambodia will be conducted from April 1 to April 30, 2023. This is the second agricultural census in Cambodia in accordance with the Law on Statistics which defines the obligations of All agricultural unit owners, including agricultural enterprises and agricultural households, must cooperate in providing information and data to agricultural census officers.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the agricultural census aims to obtain important information on the agricultural sector on the agricultural situation to serve as a basic database for the formulation of policies, strategies, action plans and program projects to promote the development of agriculture, economy and society. And the welfare of the people.
The Agricultural Census is a historically important and important work for the nation and also the National Statistical Work of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which provides information on all types of agricultural enterprises and agricultural households of all types and sizes.
Many countries in the world are in need of an agricultural census, in which a peaceful, politically stable country can function and function properly. The data from the agricultural census will be widely used in the public and private sectors.
