The agricultural census in Cambodia will be conducted from April 1 to April 30, 2023. This is the second agricultural census in Cambodia in accordance with the Law on Statistics, which defines the obligations of all agricultural unit owners. First, each farm enterprise and agricultural family must cooperate in providing information and data to the agricultural census officer.
The following is the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's appeal:
Chinese delegation reaffirms support for Samdech Techo, CPP and next generation leaders to continue to lead Cambodia for a long time
I would also like to commend the leadership of Samdech Techo, which has led Cambodia to progress in all areas, strengthening and expanding Cambodia's role in the international arena, as well as gaining the trust of the people, and the Chinese side believes that the CPP Cambodia will lead the country to achieve prosperity, people, peace and further development.
Such an assessment by Mr. Xu Chi Ming was made on the occasion of his meeting and discussion with the Honorable Dr. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly on March 28, 2023. The ceremony was accompanied by Mr. Wang. Win Thien, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to the Kingdom of Cambodia, on the occasion of leading a delegation on a working visit to Cambodia.
During the meeting, Mr. Xu said that the current visit of the Chinese delegation was for the first purpose: to implement the main ideas between Samdech Techo and President Xi Jinping; Introduction on the Outcome of the 20th and Third Congresses of the Communist Party of China: Sharing New Experiences and Ideas of Party and State Leadership
He said that under the leadership of President Xi Jinping and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia-China relations have been enhanced and the bilateral cooperation has been bilateral and multilateral, as well as a model relationship between countries with political regimes. Different. Expressed gratitude to Samdech Techo and highly appreciated the open Cambodia that supported China based on the accuracy of history and justice.
On behalf of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly and Honorary President of the Cambodian People's Party, as well as on her own behalf, expressed his pleasure and warm welcome to Mr. Su Chi Ming and the visiting delegation. In Cambodia and take the opportunity to come to the National Assembly now.
Ms. Kittisangbandit expressed her gratitude to the Chinese side for its contribution and support to the cause of the motherland by transforming Cambodia from a war-torn country to a land of peace, security and development as it is today. Taking this opportunity, she congratulated the Communist Party of China on its success in the General Assembly in October 2022, which is a world event, including Cambodia with high attention.
She said Cambodia adheres to the "one China" principle and the "one country, two systems" policy and considers the issues in Hong Kong, Taiwan and Xinjiang as China's internal affairs.
Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary expressed the hope that the Chinese side will continue to firmly adhere to Cambodia's sovereignty, especially to support and defend the constitution of the National Assembly election this July.
Ms. Khuon Sodary highlighted the importance of the "Youth House for Cambodia-China Friendship" initiative, which was established to link the two party leaders from one generation to the next in order to ensure a mechanism for working with Each.
Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary also made a proposal to the Chinese side through Mr. Xu Chiming and Mr. Wang Winthean to support the initiative to establish the "Academy of Leadership of Techo Academy" to promote sharing, exchange of experiences and learning from Mutual as well as linking relations at the senior leadership level of the two countries.
Ms. Khuon Sodary also continued to promote the sharing of technological development, science and innovation, as well as the promotion of civil and cultural cooperation and cooperation to achieve the agreement reached by the leaders of the two countries. Already agreed to come out as a practical action.
The announcement of the provincial governor was made through a press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit this morning, March 28, 2023, on "The five-year success of the Banteay Meanchey provincial administration."
Mr. Oum Rath said, "Banteay Meanchey lost some months, but Sihanoukville is the number one in earning revenue for the nation, we strive to prevent corridors from entering the official gateway to pay taxes to the state, which we consider An average of $ 1 million to 1.5 million per day.
Through what Banteay Meanchey has achieved, the provincial governor also expressed his pride, especially to earn revenue for the nation with the customs authorities and prevent the illegal import of goods through the channels that lead to loss of revenue to the nation.
In addition to earning customs revenue, Mr. Oum Rath also confirmed the collection of tax revenue, with each year the revenue never decreases. In fact, in 2022, the tax revenue in the province was 25 billion riels.
At the same time, he also thanked the traders and investors who respect the law and pay taxes, and in case the people and investors do not contribute, Banteay Meanchey can not earn as much as now.
The province is bordered by the Kingdom of Thailand, which facilitates the exchange of goods, trade, travel, tourism, cooperation and has helped boost the province's economic growth. Banteay Meanchey's exports to Thailand are mostly agricultural products such as cassava, dried peppers, sugar cane, red corn, cashews, rice and so on.
Four institutions jointly organize training courses to improve knowledge of banking, finance and insurance for journalists in Cambodia
The training course for journalists is divided into two sessions. The first session is for about 58 news writers and the second session is for about 20 editors, all from 40 different local and international institutions.
This training is designed to contribute to building the resilience of the banking, microfinance and insurance sectors by providing additional basic knowledge related to the banking and financial sector as well as the insurance sector to journalists in Cambodia and networking and maintaining relationships with journalists and bankers, as well as contributing to the development of the media in Cambodia.
He added that these challenges have limited the production of information content in the financial sector, and that access to financial information and knowledge among the Cambodian people is not yet widespread.
After completing the course in the class, both groups will visit the provinces to learn about the use of financial services in the community. In addition to basic knowledge training for journalists, the three associations will develop a number of programs to link journalists and bankers to insurance.
