Takeo National Authority Holds a Meeting to Strengthen Drug-Free Villages in Kirivong District, Takeo Province
(Takeo): On March 28, 2023, in accordance with the multi-sectoral plan of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and the plan of the 8th Anti-Illicit Campaign Campaign, the Takeo Provincial Drug Control Secretariat cooperated with the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs. Drugs held a meeting to strengthen the mechanism of drug-free villages in Kirivong district, Takeo province.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Yong Sovathana, Deputy Governor and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Takeo Provincial Drug Control Committee, and Lt. Gen. Nak Yuthea, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs.
Mr. Nguon Dina, Governor of Kirivong District, reported on the situation of security and order, in which the fight against drugs is a priority that the district strives to prevent and suppress for the peace and security of the people.
Speaking on behalf of General Meas Virith, Secretary-General on that occasion, Lt. Gen. Nak Yuthea, Deputy Secretary-General, expressed his appreciation and informed about the general situation of the drug problem, which has no signs of abating and that unscrupulous traders are always trying to hide drugs and chemicals. The combination of drugs is an attempt to use Cambodian territory as a place to process and produce more drugs, which the authorities are cracking down on.
On that occasion, General Nak Yuthea presented the policy of the village without drugs, which is an effective mechanism to prevent, suppress, treat, rehabilitate and solve drug problems.
On behalf of Mr. Ouch Phea, Provincial Governor, Dr. Yong Sovathana said that the Takeo Provincial Drug Control Committee has struggled to implement the Royal Government's policy of safe villages, communes and communes and the plan to fight against illegal drugs by the Royal Government. At the same time, the drug-free commune village mechanism has been strengthened and it is planned to expand some border villages to strengthen the anti-drug mechanism to bring safety to the people.
It should be noted that Kirivong district is a border district with Vietnam, with a length of 36 kilometers, 5 border communes and 24 border villages.
