(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Malaysia, Dato 'Seri Ann Wabin Ibrahim, led a delegation to leave Cambodia on the night of March 27, 2023, after concluding a one-day official visit to Cambodia.
The Prime Minister of Malaysia arrived at Phnom Penh International Airport at more than 9 am on March 27, 2023 to pay an official visit at the invitation of Samdech Techo. At the airport, he was warmly welcomed by Cambodian officials, led by Senior Missionary Osman Hassan.
During his visit, he met with His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia at the Royal Palace, and paid a separate courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei. Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia. He also met bilaterally with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed strengthening bilateral cooperation and exchanged views on regional and global issues.
