(Banteay Meanchey): A five-room school building built with a budget of more than $ 50,000 with the help of the Cambodian Children's Dream Organization was inaugurated on March 27, 2023 at Koh Primary School in Slor Kram commune, Svay Chek district.
Svay Chek district governor Loeung Sopheak said the Koh Primary School was built in 1993, initially as a wooden building for students to study. In 2000, it received 1 stone school building with 2 rooms, in 2005 it received 2 buildings with 12 rooms, until now it has received 3 buildings with 17 rooms, now it has received 1 building with 5 rooms as an aid to the Cambodian Children's Dream Organization to be inaugurated. Launched.
Mr. Lauren Hadmas, a donor of Samrech Soben Komar Cambodia, said that Samrech Soben Komar Cambodia has built 500 school buildings, including 200 in Cambodia, in collaboration with the Royal Government of Cambodia. Education to help children gain practical education and knowledge.
Mr. Ngor Mengchruon, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, praised the donors of Samrech Soben Komar Cambodia for building a school building at Koh Primary School, Slor Kram Commune, Svay Chek District, which has just been inaugurated. On behalf of the Governor of Banteay Meanchey, he requested donors and organizations to continue to support the education sector in Banteay Meanchey.
Authorities launch water distribution campaign in some communes facing water shortage, in early May the water supply can meet almost 100%
(Phnom Penh): During the current period and until the beginning of May 2023, people in some communes, especially on the outskirts of Phnom Penh, will face water shortage due to the water supply station is not fully supplied in both Phnom Penh and Takhmao. Kandal Province. Faced with this real problem and to solve this problem for the people, the authorities in the districts have started a campaign to distribute water to the people.
For the past few days, in some localities in Prek Pnov district, Mr. Theam Sam An, the district governor, and his subordinates have been distributing clean water to people who are short of water in Kork Roka commune.
According to the district governor, the reason for the lack of clean water is because the Phnom Penh Autonomous Region is building a new network for distribution to the people, while the increase in the number of people living in the dry season, there may be a shortage of clean water. .
On that occasion, the district governor also recommended the delivery of clean water to the people from early morning until all homes where people lack water.
Separately, Po Sen Chey District Authority, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Sangkat Sangkat Samrong Krom and Sangkat Trapeang Krasang also cooperated with Phnom Penh Capital Hall to supply water to the people in some villages and communities who are facing water shortages this dry season. Well.
Officials said that for Po Sen Chey district, the communes that are experiencing water shortages include: Sangkat Choam Chao III, Sangkat Samrong Krom and Sangkat Trapeang Krasang.
Mr. Va Savoeun, Chief of Sangkat Choam Chao III, said that three villages in Sangkat Choam Chao III had been without running water for the past week and were not open day and night. In the other 11 villages, at night, the water can be stored in a tank or other container for normal use.
Mr. Hay Sokhim, Chief of Samrong Krom Commune, confirmed that in his commune, there are two villages that are facing a shortage of water, not open at all, in addition, nine other villages can be used at night. After encountering this problem, the commune team has already installed water storage tanks in the two villages to store water for the people to drain and use.
According to the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, at the beginning of May, the water supply will be another 20 cubic meters, and by the beginning of 2024, the water supply will be another 200,000 cubic meters, so water use will no longer be a problem.
Armenia, Russia's historic ally, and relations have deteriorated sharply since Putin ordered the invasion of Ukraine, are on the verge of becoming parties to the Rome Statute, a measure under the jurisdiction of the ICC. According to a source from the Russian Foreign Ministry, the RIA, the state news agency reported that Moscow considered Armenia's plan on the ICC "unacceptable".
Russia has warned of "serious negative consequences" for bilateral relations if Yerevan continues its plan, which will be ratified by the Armenian parliament after the Constitutional Court approves it to become a member of the ICC. However, Armenia has not yet commented on the news.
The ICC order would complicate Putin's global travel plans if the country he wants to visit is an official party to the Rome Statute. The countries Putin may visit in 2023 include South Africa and Turkey, and in the past the Russian leader has traveled through the former Soviet Union, including to Armenia, where Russia has a military presence. Peace and military bases are there.
The following is a letter from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport: Citizens' views: "Are the opposition politicians all dirty like this?"
