Cambodian insurance regulator strives to promote benefits of life insurance products that help ease financial burden at risk
(Siem Reap): The Insurance Regulator of Cambodia on March 27, 2023 organized a seminar on "Benefits of Life Insurance Products" held in Siem Reap.
As a mechanism for promoting the benefits of life insurance products more widely, the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia has organized this workshop in order to mainstream knowledge and contribute to the protection of the interests, rights and obligations of insurance users, focusing on: the basics of Life Insurance Types of Life Insurance Benefits of Life Insurance The Role and Duties of the Cambodian Insurance Regulator.
Participants showed great interest and appreciation of the benefits of life insurance, which can facilitate or transfer a financial burden to a certain extent when any risk arises by providing insurance compensation to the recipient. The effect.
In addition, the workshop actively exchanged ideas to increase public confidence and develop the insurance sector in Cambodia. In addition, participants expressed interest in the role of the Cambodian Insurance Regulator in resolving disputes and insurance claims between clients and insurance operators to protect customers who use insurance services, as well as the growth of the insurance sector in Cambodia as a whole.
Participants applauded the efforts of the Cambodian Insurance Regulator and highlighted the importance of using life insurance services to respond appropriately to the risks that affect the financial burden due to the loss of life of a family head or individual. Which provides a source of income for the family.
According to the Ministry of Mines and Energy, the master plan studies and forecasts the growth of Cambodia's electricity demand from 2021 to 2040, modeled on the increase in electricity demand in line with the development of neighboring countries, including Thailand and Vietnam. To calculate and analyze the consistency of the forecast with the growth of Cambodia's gross domestic product by sector.
Each power source development scenario is evaluated to ensure that during this plan period the power supply will be adequate, reliable and have a reserve of at least 20% of the maximum power supply forecast for the season. Dry. The reserve power conditions are set to ensure that it will withstand any eventual changes during the master plan period from 2022 to 2040.
Interior Ministry spokesman: 46 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on March 27
(Phnom Penh): At least 46 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on March 27, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on March 28, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 46 suspects, 25 were arrested in 16 criminal cases and 21 were arrested in 13 drug cases.
(Banteay Meanchey): People, young and old, men and women, young men and women living in the northwestern part of the country will have the opportunity to enjoy the event "Family reunion New Year Banteay Chhmar under the shadow of peace." This event will be held at Banteay Chhmar temple in Banteay Chhmar commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province from 13 to 16 April 2023.
Banteay Chhmar New Year is organized by the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Youth Development Working Group, supported by the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration and the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Youth Federation. HE Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister, Chairman of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Government Working Group and Lok Chumteav will preside over the opening ceremony and religious ceremonies as well as entertainment programs.
Entertainment activities at the Banteay Chhmar New Year event include drumming, folk games, floating lanterns and lanterns, martial arts competitions, trade shows, celebrity concerts, sand-climbing ceremonies, Banteay Chhmar Puppet show. This is according to the Banteay Chhmar New Year event management team.
It should be noted that on the way to organize the Banteay Chhmar New Year event, HE Ke Suon Pheap, Chairman of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Youth Development Working Group and Chairman of the Banteay Chhmar New Year Committee, chaired the meeting and inspected the venue every week, especially after Krong Pali Ceremony for Peace was organized on February 17, 2023.
On March 25, 2023, the Banteay Chhmar New Year Organizing Committee held another meeting with the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration under the chairmanship of HE Oum Rath, Governor of the Provincial Board of Governors to review the progress of the work. After the meeting, Lok Chumteav Ke Suon Sophis Sokha, Deputy Chief of Event Management, together with the team, continued to inspect the process of organizing the venue, both day and night.
(Stung Treng): The specialized force of the Anti-Drug Department in cooperation with the Stung Treng Provincial Police launched an operation to crack down on cross-border drug trafficking by arresting two Lao suspects with 13 kilograms of drugs. G.
The two suspects are Nok Sovannasan, male, and Sai Songkham, Keo Kong Moeung, male, Lao nationals. The seized items include: 13 drugs, about 13 kilograms, a black CARENS car with license plate Laos 1811 Sovann, and an old motorcycle without a license plate. At present, the suspects and exhibits are being prepared by the competent authorities to build a case and send it to the court according to the procedure.
Please be informed that the specialized force of the Department of Anti-Drug Crime led by Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, Director of the Department, has actively worked hard to crack down on major drug trafficking cases in accordance with the recommendations of General Dr. Neth Savoeun. Which encourages professional forces to work hard to crack down on drug crimes, especially major crimes.
