(Tbong Khmum): On March 27, 2023, the General Commission of the National Police held a meeting on exchanging information, experience and strengthening cooperation to prevent and suppress all kinds of crimes between four border provinces, including Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham. Kratie and Prey Veng provinces.
The meeting was held at Tbong Khmum Provincial Police under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Muong Sothea, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, on behalf of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner. This was also attended by the heads of specialized departments, 4 provincial police commissioners / deputy commissioners, 7 district / municipal inspectors and many other stakeholders.
Speaking on that occasion, Lt. Gen. Muong Sothea said that the goal of this meeting is to continue to implement the prevention and suppression of all crimes in order to reduce crime and in accordance with the action plan. 2023: Encourage provincial commissions to cooperate with the working groups of specialized departments to make a list, manage and monitor crime updates regularly.
Encourage the struggle to report criminal cases and search for and arrest the remaining suspects and strengthen the preparation of technical and scientific documents to be included in the case to be sent to the judiciary in cooperation with the relevant specialized offices (Serious-light crime, drugs and Trafficking) National background and archives of arrests related to theft and so on.
Tbong Khmum Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Mon Meakrea said that Tbong Khmum Provincial Police has cooperated with the border provinces of Kampong Cham, Kratie and Prey Veng by fulfilling the roles and responsibilities of the leaders. Come with a high sense of responsibility.
