Concerns of imminent nuclear war (Video inside) (Kiev): The world has expressed concern over the deployment of Russia's nuclear weapons abroad for the first time as preparations for its spring strike strike. Ukraine plans to use US and Western weapons to defeat Russia.
Russian President Vladimir Putin has said that Russia will deploy strategic nuclear weapons in Belarus, which is a warning to NATO and a message of escalating confrontation. Between Russia and the West. Russian leader Putin said on Saturday that the deployment would not violate its promise of non-proliferation.
The report confirms where in Belarus that Russia's nuclear weapons will be stored. The transfer of nuclear weapons is an expansion of Russia's nuclear strike capabilities along the eastern border of NATO member states.
The report said that although the Kremlin has never publicly confirmed the location of tactical nuclear weapons, Western groups have said Russia has long maintained nuclear-capable missiles in the coastal region of Kaliningrad. Its Baltic Sea, which stretches between NATO and Poland and Lithuania.
The International Campaign for the Elimination of Nuclear Weapons has called Putin's announcement the most dangerous increase. "In the context of the war in Ukraine, the possibility of miscalculations or misinterpretations is very high," the international campaign wrote on its Twitter account. "The sharing of nuclear weapons has exacerbated the situation and posed a catastrophic threat to humanity."
Putin added that Russia would not hand over nuclear weapons to Belarus and that the United States would not hand over its nuclear weapons to its allies. "They have allies in some countries and they have helped train them to use weapons, and we will do the same," Putin said.
Putin said Russia had deployed 10 aircraft in Belarus capable of launching nuclear tactical weapons. He added that Russia has already transferred to Belarus an Iskander tactical missile system capable of launching nuclear weapons.
