(Phnom Penh): On Monday evening, March 27, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Anwar Ibrahim, Prime Minister of Malaysia, presided over the 7th Ramadan Ramadan of Cambodian Islam. The event was held at the Chroy Changvar Convention and Exhibition Center.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech on the occasion of presiding over the vegetarian dinner:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen would like to express his appreciation for the efforts and attention of the Committee for the Preparation of the Ramadan Food Program of Islamic Cambodia, which has co-organized an important ceremony for Muslims to 1). Feel close to God 2). Spend time with family and loved ones 3) Participate in charitable activities and 4). Reminiscent of people with bad luck.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that the Royal Government of Cambodia provides full freedom of religion without discrimination. In fact, the Royal Government has opened its doors to Cambodian Muslims through 1) allowing Muslim students to wear traditional clothing in educational institutions at all levels, 2) arranging places of worship in public places.
* Under the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and during subsequent wars, religious beliefs, especially Islam, were completely abolished. This is the result of internal conflicts and divisions and also the result of power struggles and attempts to change the government by force, lack of internal unity and national unity.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia, formerly known as the Killing Fields, was an insecure area, a minefield that everyone feared, has now become a "Peace Island" and a popular tourist destination. Cambodia, formerly an economically impoverished country dominated by poverty and food insecurity, has now become a food exporter and achieved high economic growth.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia, formerly a country under siege and political and economic isolation, has now become a country that is actively integrating itself into its global structure and structure. Who are playing an active role with equal rights and equality in all regional affairs and on the international stage.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen would like to take this opportunity to encourage and offer the following four views:
First. The Royal Government of Cambodia promotes freedom of religion and belief, promotes the harmony of religious harmony and peace, which is an important and indispensable factor for all national development and economic and social prosperity of Cambodia.
Second. The Ministry of Cults and Religions and the competent authorities at all levels must work together to facilitate religious observance, work closely with religious leaders and communities, based on the principles of religious harmony, and facilitate the construction of mosques in Villages with large numbers of Muslims live according to actual needs.
Third. The Cambodian Islamic Council must strengthen and expand national and international cooperation to mobilize both technical and financial assistance to contribute to improving the lives of the Khmer Muslim community through the development of human capital for technology access and transfer; Innovation for the Khmer Muslim community.
Fourth. Highly encourage Muslims to adhere to the sacred principles of Ramadan and to contribute to the promotion of racial and religious harmony in Cambodia through the establishment of good relations, solidarity and non-discrimination, and Other religions.
