Through the interest of the representatives of the Kratie Provincial Network of Civil Society Organizations and the active feedback from the forum participants. A concrete bridge donated by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit in Batachi village, Sangkat Prek Hoor has been opened for construction.
(Kandal): A 55-by-8-meter-long American concrete bridge donated by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the people of Sangkat Prek Hoor was opened in Batachi Village, Sangkat Prek Hoor, Takhmao City, Kandal Province on March 27, 2023
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Mao Phirun, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Kong Sophoan, Provincial Governor, with the participation of more than 500 people.
Mr. Kong Sophoan said that the project to build the concrete bridge of the main bridge will alleviate the hardships of 381 families, equal to 1685 people living in Batachi village, as well as Prek Long and Prek Kat villages, Takdol commune and other people who pass through In the past, it was very difficult to travel through and transport agricultural products to sell in the market to solve daily life.
He pointed out that the construction of the old bridge began in 1992 with the proceeds from the sale of village land to build a wooden bridge under the assistance of Mr. Yin Yat, former director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province.
By 2001, the bridge was badly damaged and Samdech Techo Hun Sen donated $ 5,000 through Kun Kim to renovate the site. Later, the bridge began to deteriorate until 2015, Mr. Chhun Sirun, former governor of Kandal province, ordered Mr. Moeng Youleng, director of the Kandal Provincial Department of Public Works, to remove the bridge and build a new bridge made of the same wood.
He added that until January 23, 2023, unfortunately, the condition is very dilapidated, people have gradually repaired this place with the participation of the Royal Government to help Prek Hoor, but due to flooding in the dry season. Coming hard and there was a lot of water flowing under the bridge, it completely collapsed.
At the same time, Dr. Mao Phirun said that the 55-meter-long, 8-meter-wide, 8-meter-wide and 8-meter-wide concrete bridge in Batachi village, Sangkat Prek Ho, Takhmao city, Kandal province, is now a new great achievement for Kandal province. This emerges from the Rectangular Strategic Policy of the Royal Government under the wise and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Meeting to review the work results for 2022 and work direction for 2023 of Prey Veng Provincial Administration
(Prey Veng): On March 27, 2023, Prey Veng Provincial Administration held a meeting to review the work results of 2022 and raise the work direction of 2023 of the provincial administration under the chairmanship of Mr. Sbong Sarath, Chairman of Prey Veng Provincial Council and Mr. Chea Somethy, Governor of Prey Veng Province. Including departments and units around the province, the three forces, the governors of the 13 districts are crowded.
The provincial governor continued that in the context of the reform of the Royal Government, the main directions of the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly are as follows:
* First, to ensure the normalization of national institutions, public administration, the process of liberal democracy, pluralism and the rule of law * Second: to maintain peace, political stability, security, public order and promote the participation of the people, especially the implementation of the principles Village, commune safety policy and the reform policy of the Royal Government and thirdly - to promote economic growth and reduce poverty of the people.
Mr. Chea Somethy, Provincial Governor, continued that the meeting was held for three purposes:
* First: Review, comment, supplement the draft report on the results of 2022. * Second: Evaluate the strengths, weaknesses and related factors to gain experience in leadership and implementation * Third: Raise challenges, solutions All sectors, as well as the results of solving problems and responding to those challenges, to set out additional activities to be included in the 2023 work direction effectively.
The provincial governor hopes that through this meeting, the provincial administration will receive lessons, experiences and other important points to help guide and implement the work successfully for 2023 with quality and efficiency in accordance with the guidelines. Rectangular Strategic Policy, Phase 4 of the Royal Government, 6th Legislature of the National Assembly.
Cambodian, Malaysian leaders agree to strengthen cross-border crime cooperation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian and Malaysian leaders agree to strengthen cross-border crime cooperation.
The agreement was reached during a bilateral meeting between Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Malaysian Prime Minister Datuk Seri Anwar bin Ibrahim on March 27 at the Peace Palace.
Speaking at a joint press conference after the bilateral talks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen outlined the results of talks on a number of issues between the two leaders, both bilateral, regional and international.
"Regarding defense and security, the two sides agreed to strengthen cooperation between relevant institutions, exchange professional delegations to experiment with anti-trafficking and human trafficking and money laundering, and consider establishing money," he said. "To have a memorandum of understanding between the General Commission of the National Police of Cambodia and the Royal Police of Malaysia on cooperation in the fight against transnational crime."
Samdech stated that this is what was proposed to the Prime Minister of Malaysia.
Please be informed that Mr. Anwar Bin Ibrahim led a delegation to arrive in Cambodia on the morning of March 27, 2023 for a one-day official visit at the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Meeting between the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Malaysia to enhance bilateral relations, increase trade and investment by Malaysian businesses in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Meeting between the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Malaysia will enhance bilateral relations And expand the scope of trade and investment operations of the two countries even more.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized: "In expanding the scope of trade and investment between the two countries, I have proposed to increase the purchase of goods that meet the needs of each other. I encourage Malaysian investors and companies to come. "Do more business and invest."
On that occasion, Samdech Techo expressed his happiness that the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Malaysia in 2022 reached 620 million US dollars, an increase of 24% compared to 2021, which reached only 500 million US dollars.
"I would like to reaffirm my commitment to work closely with His Excellency Minister Ibrahim to further strengthen and expand bilateral relations and cooperation to be stronger and more prosperous," he added.
Malaysian Prime Minister Datuk Seri Anwar bin Ibrahim said a wide-ranging discussion on trade and investment was a priority for the two countries in bilateral relations and discussions on Malaysia's halal industry. That will provide an opportunity for Malaysia and Cambodia to use the sector to encourage and facilitate exports.
At the same time, to increase trade between the two countries, he will encourage Malaysian companies to consider importing rice and cashew nuts from Cambodia.
