The UN Water Conference 2023 aims to review the mid-term mandate of water sustainability practices for sustainable development 2018-2028 related to (1) knowledge sharing, experience of water use management and Improved sanitation (2) Taking joint action to achieve clean water and sanitation goals for all.
The conference is also a forum for member countries to reaffirm their commitment, plans and best practices in water and sanitation management.
The conference was opened by the Secretary-General of the United Nations, the President of the United Nations General Assembly, the President of the Economic and Social Council, the Secretary-General of the Conference and the Co-Chairs of Tajikistan and the Netherlands.
The Lecturer, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, briefed the conference on Cambodia's position on the topic, its performance and challenges, and its strategic direction for sustainable water and sanitation management for all.
The conference concluded successfully on the afternoon of March 24, 2023, approving the summary report of the entire conference as a basis for the implementation of effective water use and management. Senior Minister Cham Prasidh: The Ministry is committed to cooperating with relevant ministries and institutions to address challenges in science, technology and innovation.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cham Prasidh, Senior Minister and Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, on March 26, 2023, stated that although the field of Science, Technology and Innovation is a new sector and one of the first missions of the Ministry of Industry. Despite science, technology and innovation, the Ministry is committed to cooperating with relevant ministries and institutions to address challenges in this area.
This confirmation was made by Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cham Prasidh at the first National Forum on Science, Technology and Innovation under the theme "Building a Foundation for All" under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The forum will be held at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center on Sunday morning, March 26, 2023.
Senior Minister Cham Prasidh continued that we together promote the development of science, technology and innovation to move forward with the guidance and guidance of Samdech Techo Prime Minister as the Honorary President of the National Council for Science, Technology and Innovation. A number of important achievements have been made and are bearing fruit positively for contributing to the national economic growth.
In addition, the Ministry is preparing a draft law on technology transfer and a number of draft sub-decrees, such as the draft sub-decree on the establishment and management of the Science, Technology and Innovation Park, and the draft sub-decree on research and development management. This is the additional emphasis of Senior Minister Cham Prasidh.
Of course, the field of science, technology and innovation is not the responsibility of any separate ministry, it must be inter-sectoral, which requires close and sincere cooperation within the inter-ministerial framework, including The private sector, too, must take into account the common interests of the nation as a whole, not take a pro-ministerial position or work separately.
Senior Minister Cham Prasidh said, "I understand that at this stage, good cooperation is necessary for a national harmony that can push science, technology and innovation forward more than ever before."
The five points of view of Samdech Techo Hun Sen are as follows:
* First, the Royal Government gives high priority to the development of human capital in the fields of science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) by encouraging the younger generation to choose to study agriculture, improving the quality of education and training at all levels. Implement strategies to attract and retain outstanding individuals, strengthen research and development, and establish a national research fund for science, technology, and innovation.
* Second, the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and the National Council for Science, Technology and Innovation must promote the development of legal frameworks, in particular the issuance of legal documents, policies, strategic plans and roadmaps in priority areas to accelerate system development. National innovation to fully respond to the needs of Cambodia's development, changes in regional and global trends.
* Third: The Royal Government encourages to increase and strengthen cooperation between the public sector, the private sector, the education sector and development partners in promoting the Cambodian innovation system.
* Fourth, Samdech highly encouraged higher education institutions to continue to establish new business and business support centers to contribute to the promotion of entrepreneurship and innovation in Cambodia.
This was stated by Samdech Techo on Sunday morning, March 26, 2023, when he presided over the opening of the National Forum on "Science, Technology and Innovation" at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia stated, "In the context of the Kovid 19 pandemic, global warming, geopolitical competition, trade wars and climate change, I see an increasingly important role for science, technology and innovation in sustaining growth." "Economy and promote the fruits of socio-economic development in an environmentally friendly manner."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out the Science, Technology and Innovation Policy 2020-2030 in order to build the foundation for the capture of science and technology products, as well as to participate in the process of creating new technologies in the future.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that the Royal Government has launched the "Roadmap on Skills Development in Cambodia 2022-2035" and the National Research Agenda 2025 in order to address the challenges and create opportunities for the public, private sector and the people of Cambodia. .
This confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on the morning of Sunday, March 26, 2023, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the opening of the National Forum "Science, Technology and Innovation".
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and the National Council for Science, Technology and Innovation must prepare a legal framework, especially the issuance of legal documents, policies, strategic plans and roadmaps in priority areas. To accelerate the development of the national innovation system to fully meet the needs of Cambodia's development, changes in regional and global trends.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia added that it encourages and encourages the enhancement and strengthening of cooperation between the public and private sectors, the education sector and development partners in promoting the Cambodian innovation system.
