(Phnom Penh): This morning, Sunday, March 26, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening of the National Forum on "Science, Technology and Innovation". The forum is being held at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
National Day "Science, Technology and Innovation" organized by the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation. This is the first time in Cambodia that this has never happened before.
National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation is a contribution to the joint implementation of the Royal Government's policies and roadmaps in accordance with the Cambodian Digital Economic and Social Policy Framework 2021-2035 and for Cambodia to be ready to become a country that High middle income by 2030
The National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation will be held for three days from March 26 to 28, 2023. The day will be attended by more than 200 relevant institutions, including relevant ministries, higher education and research institutions, national and international development partners, businesses and business associations.
Highlights of the national event include the launch of the Science Caravan, the first ever mobile science lab. The lab exhibit is designed to engage children in science, technology and innovation, as well as encourage a positive attitude toward STEM education.
The event is expected to attract many children and parents to introduce their children to science and technology.
The national program also features keynote presentations by experts and researchers in the field of science and technology, with a focus on promoting the field of stem cells for children and especially for girls.
In addition, there will be a Talk Show, a platform to bring together intellectuals, entrepreneurs and government experts to discuss various challenges, as well as find solutions and future cooperation in these two areas. This is a unique opportunity to promote unity and accept ideas from different angles to lead to better decisions in their respective institutions.
"Science, technology and innovation are the backbone of national development," he added. The Royal Government of Cambodia has made important decisions to promote science, technology and innovation to push Cambodia into a new era of vibrant civilization.
The three-day national event is expected to attract more than 50,000 visitors, with interactive and fun science-related learning to boost interest in science among Cambodian children and youth.
