(Phnom Penh): Trud Dance is a traditional Khmer dance that people often play on the occasion of the New Year, the national tradition, the end of the old year, the New Year and the opportunity to celebrate the eviction of evil from home or office or during Where wild animals run into the village and so on. This dance is also mentioned in the royal ceremony called "Trasat Sankran".
* Sources from various documents claim that this traditional dance originated from the indigenous people in the mountainous areas, such as the Samre Sui Por, as well as our Khmer people in Srey Slaket, Surin Kork, Khan Ubon, Siem Reap, Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom, Pursat. Battambang and so on. The natives call the word "trud" to refer to the end of the old year and the beginning of the new year.
