Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks while presiding over the opening of the first National Forum on "Science, Technology and Innovation" this morning, March 26, 2023. The National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation is organized by the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, which is the first time in Cambodia that has never been seen before.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also praised and appreciated the attention of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, which initiated this event in connection with the 1st Cambodia-International Science, Technology and Innovation Exhibition, 2023.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister called on the national and international community to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in all stages of the digital revolution, as clearly stated in the framework of the Cambodian Digital Economy and Society 2021-2035 and the Digital Government Policy 2022- 2035.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in the context of the Kovid 19 pandemic, global warming, geopolitical competition, trade wars and climate change, Samdech sees an increasingly important role of science, technology and innovation in maintaining sustainable economic growth and development. Promote the fruits of environmentally-friendly socio-economic development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further affirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out the Science, Technology and Innovation Policy 2020-2030 in order to build the foundation for the capture of science and technology products as well as to participate in the process of creating new technologies in the future. The future.
This announcement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen presiding over the opening of the National Forum on "Science, Technology and Innovation" at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center on the morning of March 26, 2023.
