On March 24, 2023, Mr. Thong Rathsak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation, led a delegation from the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia to visit and sign a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Human Resource Development in Tourism, Shanghai Tourism Institute of the People's Republic of China. China is represented by Kang Nian, director of the institute.
The memorandum focuses on the following six points:
1. Promote exchange programs for Chinese and Khmer language training in tourism.
2. Promote and increase short-term Chinese language exchange programs.
3. Promote the exchange of tourism students between China and Cambodia.
4. Exchange experiences and management courses in tourism skills training.
5. Organizing workshops on tourism focused on development, investment, culture, heritage, education and management.
6. Encourage study visits of tourism officials.
During the visit, the representative of the Ministry of Tourism also gave a presentation on Cambodian tourism to the professors and students of the Shanghai Institute to show the attractiveness of tourism in Cambodia and start to implement the cooperation as stated in the memorandum.
Cambodia, Dominican Republic vow to seek bilateral cooperation
At the bilateral meeting on March 23, 2023, Mr. Ouch Borith, Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, and Dr. Win Henderson reaffirmed their commitment to strengthening relations. Between the two countries in a bilateral and multilateral framework.
The Acting Minister briefed on the political and economic situation, as well as Cambodia's efforts to achieve and maintain peace and stability, which are hard to find, democracy and human rights. He also mentioned some potential commodities for trade between the two countries, as well as many incentives for investors under Cambodia's new investment law.
Minister Henderson praised the level of development of Cambodia and the improvement of people's lives due to the peace and stability that Cambodia has maintained. The Minister agreed on the key to development: peace and stability and the challenges that small states face in the context of competition between superpowers.
The two sides discussed ways and means to explore potentials in areas of common interest, such as trade and investment, agriculture, technical and vocational training, eco-tourism and hospitality. The two sides agreed in principle on the possibility of establishing a bilateral consultation mechanism between the Foreign Ministries of the two countries and agreed to support each other in multilateral forums, especially the UN system.
After the talks, Mr. Ouch Borith and Dr. Win Henderson signed an agreement between the Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Commonwealth of Dominican Republic on a visa waiver for holders of diplomatic and official passports.
On March 24, 2023, Dr. Win Henderson paid a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. This is a good start to seek mutually beneficial cooperation after the two countries established diplomatic ties 13 years ago.
The Prime Minister welcomed the signing of the Agreement on Visa Waivers for Holders of Diplomatic and Official Passports, which will pave the way for further dialogue, and highlighted some key areas of potential cooperation. Includes: agriculture, fishing and tourism, where the two countries can exchange experiences with each other.
Admiring Cambodia's progress, Dr. Win Henderson praised Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his simplicity but firmness in bringing peace, stability and development to Cambodia, and stressed that Samdech Techo had a lot of experience to share. Share to the world.
The Foreign Minister agreed on the vision of cooperation in the above fields and was ready to strengthen relations between the two countries, and volunteered to serve as a gateway for Cambodia to other countries in the Caribbean.
Minister of Information: To neutralize false information, journalists must find the real source from all parties to verify thoroughly before publishing information (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, emphasized that for the neutralization of false information, journalists must find Real sources or find sources from all parties involved in the information to interpret and must verify thoroughly before publishing any information.
This statement was made by the Minister of Information on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results in 2022 and set the work direction for 2023 of the Independent Media Alliance under the theme: "Together to disseminate real information, do not fabricate information. There are fakes for society and humanity as a whole "on the afternoon of March 24, 2023 yesterday.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith continued, "False information means a lot because some information is distorted and some information is not distorted, but they expand from small to large. The important thing is that journalists must eliminate this false information." .
The Minister said that the upcoming 7th legislative election in 2023 may spread false information affecting the election, and called on all media to help spread the word. Just in time.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith also further urged all media outlets to publish factual information "Do not abuse others, do not distort the truth" and Cambodia has the right to remove the authority of the media in Cambodia that publishes unprofessional and unethical.
Meanwhile, the Minister of Information said that in Cambodia there are more than 50 media associations, in which there are only one or two press associations. He added that professional and professional journalists must join the fight against fake news.
He said that only in Cambodia, the Prime Minister eats with journalists. At the outbreak of Kovid 19, the government gave priority to journalists getting vaccinated, as did doctors and soldiers on the front lines.
Please note that disseminating false or misleading information can lead to wrong decisions on any matter. If the false information is more divisive, it will increase the risk of social unrest, which could lead to unrest in the country and even war.
