(Tbong Khmum): 48 young people (35 females) from Choam and Chan Moul communes, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province participated in a class forum on the history of Democratic Kampuchea, especially the security system in Democratic Kampuchea 1975-1979 at the Documentation Center. Koh Thmor, Tbong Khmum Province.
This class forum was held on March 24, 2023, led by Mr. Long Dany, Director of Koh Thmor Documentation Center.
According to the director of the Koh Thmor Documentation Center, during the Democratic Kampuchea regime (1975-1979), the Khmer Rouge organized the Security Department at the following levels:
1. The first three levels of security are at the commune level, the district level, and the regional level, most of which house detainees of Lon Nol regime veterans and civil servants, and other prisoners who are civilians charged with stealing or fleeing or fleeing. Work or say bad things about the organization.
2. The Regional Security Department is a place of detention, torture and killing of Khmer Rouge fighters and their families and those accused of committing crimes in the region.
Mr. Long Dany screened a documentary on Tuol Sleng Prison (S-21) for the young people who attended the forum to watch. He also gave additional presentations on the prevention of genocide, the use of violence, discrimination and its consequences.
