The Cambodian Pharmacists' Council officially launches an online registration system, all pharmacists must register before applying for a work license.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Pharmacists Association has officially launched the Online Pharmacist Registration System (RMS), which facilitates pharmacists across the country to register and participate in preventing those who pretend to be pharmacists. Affect public health.
The announcement of the RMS Online Pharmacy Registration System was held at the Online Registration Dissemination Workshop on the morning of March 24, 2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
Mr. Ban Botta, President of the National Council of Pharmacists of Cambodia, said that this workshop is to promote the launch of the RMS online registration system of the Board of Pharmacists of Cambodia from 2023 onwards and for officials to better understand the implementation. This online registration system will disseminate to all pharmaceutical professionals to register before applying for a license to work.
Mr. Ban Botta continued that this online pharmacy registration system is to facilitate pharmacists across the country to get convenience, save time and money and be faster than before. Cambodian Pharmacist, Phnom Penh.
The President of the National Association of Medicines of Cambodia stated that in order to be able to register as a Cambodian pharmacist, pharmaceutical professionals must have some important qualifications, such as:
Pharmacists must have a medical degree from a college and have a valid certificate from the Ministry of Health or the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, or an overseas college.
* Pharmacists must have sufficient ability or qualifications to practice pharmacy.
* Pharmacists must be healthy, that is, be physically fit and free of disease.
* Pharmacists must not be convicted or have been convicted.
"Before applying for a license from the Ministry of Health, pharmacists must first register with pharmacists to avoid harm to public health, especially to improve the quality, safety and efficiency of providing services to the people," he said. "This is a condition set by law."
Prak Manila, USAID-EQHA Project Manager, said that through this work will also strengthen the capacity of health professionals to be more quality and safe for people across the country.
Kampong Speu Province Organizes the 1st Sui Indigenous Song Festival
(Kampong Speu): With the permission of Kampong Speu Provincial Administration, the Provincial Department of Culture and Fine Arts, in cooperation with the Provincial Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, organized the 1st Sui Indigenous Song Festival 2023 on March 23, 2023 at the Library. Kampong Speu.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Son, Provincial Councilor, Representative of the Chairman of the Provincial Council and Ms. Long Bonareth, Deputy Governor and Representative of the Provincial Governor, and was attended by the Deputy Governor of Kang District. The three types of forces: the director, the deputy director of the department around the province, civil servants, students, and youth of the CPPCC. Red Cross Youth, Scout Youth, a total of about 300 people.
Addressing the ceremony, the representative of the provincial governor stated the purpose of organizing the festival by urging the people, especially the youth, who are the pillars of the nation and the successors to:
* Increase love, inspire, participate in the transfer and acquisition of knowledge, skills, techniques, arts and culture to promote the preservation and development of national culture, as well as multiculturalism in Cambodia to be stable and stable, which is the basis of unity, national unity, harmony and Peace of the society.
* Promote a better understanding of the values of the Sui indigenous culture and more actively participate in the conservation and development.
* Increase participation in the cultivation of education, research, and understanding of the knowledge, arts, and culture of the Sui indigenous people so that their youth can understand the important benefits of transferring and embracing knowledge, skills and compilation. Maintain all documents in its locality as well as disseminate more widely.
* Inspire the youth who take turns to participate in creating new works of quality, maintain the basics, rules and promote the use of its cultural potential to participate in the development of the national economy in order to increase employment and opportunities to reduce Poverty and reduce the relentless influx of negative culture from the currents of globalization.
* Encourage the participation of Sui indigenous youth in the conservation and sustainable development and peace, regardless of political affiliation. The main purpose is to inspire the mass movement to support and promote Motivation to contribute to the preservation, protection and promotion of the values, arts, culture and traditions of the Sui people.
She also requested the department to make efforts to organize this festival regularly and also requested the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts to organize indigenous arts festivals throughout the country.
Please be informed that the above festival has the participation of 6 Sui indigenous art groups, a total of 72 people from Trapeang Cho and Sangke commune, Oral district, each group received a certificate of appreciation and accompanied by flowers. Some budget.
Senior official of the Ministry of Interior: Development in Police School Zone 2 in Kampong Cham Province to enhance the professional capacity of the police force
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Santibandit Chan An, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, stated that the development of infrastructure and study materials at the Police School Zone 2 in Prey Chhor District, Kampong Cham Province is aimed at enhancing the professional capacity of the police force to maintain law and order. To the people.
He said this on the occasion of his visit on behalf of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, to inspect the progress of the construction of various infrastructures and to meet and greet the 17th generation police students at the 2nd Police School this morning. March 24, 2023
Dr. Chan An took the opportunity to commend and thank the management team of the National Police School, Zone 2 and the police teachers for their hard work, responsibility and good training, as well as to appreciate all the police students who Has worked hard to learn, train and respect discipline well to become a police officer who is qualified to serve the nation and the people.
(Banteay Meanchey): On March 23, 2023, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department held a handover ceremony for the emergency department building after the renovation, expansion and delivery of ambulances by the Thai side under the Cambodia International Cooperation Project. Thailand of the Thai International Cooperation Agency (TICA) project.
The handover ceremony was held with great honor, full of atmosphere, happiness, friendship, solidarity, cooperation between the two countries in general and in particular for the health sector between Banteay Meanchey and Sa Kaeo.
On that occasion, Mr. Tpe Chansangvat, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department, thanked the Thai side for always paying attention to the health sector in Banteay Meanchey. This afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen closed the meeting of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
(Phnom Penh): This afternoon, Friday, March 24, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries held a meeting to review the work of the old year and set the direction of the new year on March 21, 2023. The four-day conference was attended by leaders of the Ministry of Agriculture, leaders of relevant units, directors of the 25 Departments of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the capital-province, the private sector, community development partners and farmers.
The conference opened a lively discussion, reviewing the achievements of the previous year, raising challenges and setting out plans for the new year. In particular, promote better work efficiency.
Speaking on the opening day of the conference, Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the conference was a collective participation of private sector leaders, development partners, farmers' communities together to set the direction of agriculture, not just a summary. The conclusion is to be heard, understood and remembered by letting the public know the achievements of the Ministry and join in the celebration.
Agriculture is an important sector to support the livelihood and economic growth of Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the leader who transformed Cambodia from a food-deprived country after the liberation from the Khmer Rouge regime into a rice-rich country today, often presides over the annual work review of the ministry.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister always takes this opportunity to remind and make some recommendations to promote agricultural work.
According to the report of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in 2022, the Ministry has achieved a lot of proud work for the benefit of the people and the nation.
At the same time, the Ministry has also strengthened the conservation of fishery resources in the sea area. In Kep province, the Fisheries Authority and the Provincial Unity Command cracked down on the use of trawl nets in many cases, and others who used this equipment voluntarily handed over to the authorities. At present, in Kep province, there is no use of trawl nets, which makes the presence of flocks of sea dolphins and pigs come to visit our sea often.
Separately, the Ministry has prepared a draft law to amend the current forest law to allow people, especially true animal lovers, to raise some wild animals as a family in accordance with the highest recommendation of the Prime Minister.
For international cooperation, the Ministry has also been reviewing existing agreements and documents on agricultural cooperation in both bilateral and multilateral fields to increase ownership of project design and implementation and ensure efficiency. Economy and sustainability after the project is completed.
Minister Dit Tina emphasized that the agricultural sector continues to play an active role in ensuring food security, raising people's living standards, reducing poverty, increasing exports and sustaining national economic growth despite the effects of natural disasters and crises. Global.
