(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Honorary President of the Independent Media Coalition Association, advised all journalists to publish true information with clear, accurate and impartial sources and to eliminate false information for the benefit of society.
Mr. Sar Sokha made this instruction on the morning of March 24, 2023, when he chaired the opening of the conference on the work results for 2022 and the work direction for 2023 of the Independent Press Alliance at the hotel. Sokha Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Mr. Sar Sokha said that currently Cambodia is also affected by a lot of false information, including other countries. At this point, all journalists need to understand how to write news.
Mr. Sar Sokha continued that for Cambodia, the Royal Government has not blocked the right to freedom of expression and dissemination of information, as alleged by some individuals, compared to other countries, while there are now associations and organizations. There are no less than 5,000 registered civil society organizations in the Ministry of Interior.
At the same time, Mr. Sar Sokha said that the slogan "Together to spread true information, do not invent fake news for society and humanity as a whole," which further reflects the will of the leaders as well as journalists in Effective and timely crackdown on fake information.
(Banteay Meanchey): Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Government Working Group, further instructed the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Authority to strictly implement the policy of safe villages, communes and combat plans. Fight illegal drugs more vigorously.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan made this instruction on the morning of March 24, 2023, when he presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results for 2022 and the work direction for 2023 of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration. This was held at Banteay Meanchey Provincial Hall.
Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, reported on the results of the management, leadership, administration and development in all areas, maintaining security, public order, implementing policies, villages, communes, sangkats, work safety, fight drugs and provide public services to the people. People in Banteay Meanchey province in 2022.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan stated that the achievements and results of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration have really contributed to the maintenance of peace, political stability, and the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration also strives to maintain security, public order and social security to raise The height of democracy and pluralism.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan said that under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Cambodia has been able to manage and respond effectively and timely to the global epidemic of Kovid 19, as well as the introduction of measures to mitigate the effects caused. Due to Kovid 19 disease, floods, floods and global crises, the national economy is recovering rapidly at a growth rate of 5.2 percent in 2022.
At the same time, on behalf of the Royal Government, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the authorities, law enforcement forces and the people of Banteay Meanchey province for their cooperation in maintaining security, public order and ensuring better security. Also praised the authorities at all levels who have participated in maintaining peace and order better.
Along with the above achievements, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan also noted the remaining challenges, including many other important tasks: the strict implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, plans, combat campaigns. Illegal drugs, etc.
