Brigadier General Van Havari, Deputy Director of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department and Chairman of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway Traffic Police Working Group, told Fresh News this morning, March 24, 2023, that from From March 1 to 21, the traffic police on the expressway inspected a total of 56 vehicles, of which 38 were fined and 18 cases were educated.
Brigadier General Van Havari added that the most fined case was driving in the opposite direction, 31 vehicles were fined and points deducted. According to the police, the reason for them to turn in the opposite direction is because they do not know the geography of the road, and some people drive beyond the bend.
