This case happened on March 21-22, the police arrested 6 perpetrators out of 10 factions. They admitted that the attack was not resentful, but a massacre.
In the second case, at 12:30 pm on March 20, a 21-year-old woman named Khun Srey Khouch was riding a motorbike in front of the gate of Hour Khieu School on National Road 5 in Damnak Popoul village, Kampong Chhnang commune. In this case, the police immediately investigated and arrested a perpetrator named Thun Chandoeun, a resident of Trapeang Kor village, Chrey Bak commune, Rolea Bier district, confiscated a mobile phone and 100,000 Riels and returned it to the victim.
The third case of murder, stabbing to death, robbery of motorcycles and two mobile phones occurred at 8:40 pm on March 21, 2023 in Taing Poun village, Peam commune, Samaki Meanchey district, causing the victim named Nuth Saroeun, 52 years old The paralyzed man was stabbed and stabbed to death with 15 knives on the house.
In this case, the provincial police, in cooperation with the Criminal Police Department, arrested the perpetrator, Vun Rith, residing in Khyang village, Svay commune, Samaki Meanchey district, on March 22 in Kampong Speu province, confiscating a motorcycle and two mobile phones of the victim.
Authorities confirmed that in this case, the perpetrator was initially sent by his mother to study with monks in Phnom Chum Reay, Kampong Speu province. But later, they left Wat Lok to ask for monks at another pagoda in Samaki Meanchey district, but the monks did not know him well, so he did not allow them to stay.
After eating and drinking together with 3 people, at night, the perpetrator used a brown knife to stab the victim, the owner of the house, who was asleep on the house with 15 knives, causing the perpetrator to die. He also hijacked a motorcycle and two mobile phones and escaped during the night. In this case, after being arrested, he was charged with murder and robbery.
The eight perpetrators who committed the three different crimes above were sent to court this morning, March 23, for legal action.
