Please be informed that the conditional release is in accordance with the spirit of the Prakas on the Procedures for Monitoring, Supervision and Reintegration of Prisoners Released with the Conditions of the Ministry of Justice dated 14 July 2021.
According to the Code of Criminal Procedure, prisoners can be released before the end of their sentence, subject to the following two conditions:
1: Conditions related to behavior: Prisoners must show that they have good manners during detention and have the ability to return to society. This means that inmates have to take various actions, such as remorse, guilt, expression of remorse for their actions, etc., to show that they really have the will and qualifications to be able to get out of prison by knowing their mistakes and correcting them. Re-body.
