Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for continued cooperation in the eradication of tuberculosis (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Through a message on the occasion of World TB Day, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, called on all Ministries, institutions, stakeholders, the private sector, national and international organizations, development partners and all citizens to understand and understand, and must continue to contribute and support the promotion of TB eradication.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued, "I am confident that Cambodia will continue to move forward on a stronger, broader and more autonomous basis, and achieve the set goals."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cambodia still has a high rate of morbidity and mortality due to tuberculosis compared to some other countries and there are still many people who have not yet received services. This requires us to step up our efforts to further reduce the incidence and mortality of TB in line with the Sustainable Development Goals of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the world.
