On Friday, March 17, 2023, the ICC announced the arrest of Putin on charges of war crimes in Ukraine. The Kremlin immediately dismissed the order, declaring it null and void, as Russia is not a party to the ICC.
The ICC verdict and the completion of a surprise visit to Mariupol, the territory of Ukraine under Russian occupation on March 19, 2023, were considered by Dr. Yong Pov Overlap between the United States (and its allies) with Russia. It is this insult that makes Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen worried about nuclear war.
Dr. Yong Pov stated that "this aggression is dangerous, as Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen said that could lead to more nuclear war or weapons of mass destruction."
The expert argues that power struggles between the superpowers in the geopolitical game have seen that since the Cold War, the three main polar powers, the United States, the Russian Federation and China, have always played a key role in both political and military power. The most in world order. He added that the three countries always change their attitude when big problems occur.
According to Dr. Yong Pov, in order to reflect the current reality, one should look at the important role of US-led NATO, with the main goal being to counter the former Soviet Union. Now NATO, like creating another object, is also resisting China. That is why China has joined hands with Russia to counter each other, which they both understand are strategic enemies in world order.
On March 20, 2023, Chinese President Xi Jinping arrived in Moscow, Russia for a three-day state visit and met with Putin to discuss peace plans.
On March 22, 2023, the United States said it did not see China as acting as a neutral mediator between Moscow and Kiev in the Russia-Ukraine war. The United States' first direct criticism of China for trying to enhance its role as a peace seeker to end the war.
For Dr. Yong Pov, he saw Chinese values in the Russia-Ukraine conflict, especially the 12-point proposal initiated by the Chinese president.
"Like it or not, I see China playing a key role in the Russia-Ukraine war," he said. If China is not recognized, the world will lose because the United States and the West cannot talk to Putin. So the one who can talk to Putin and weigh in is China, led by Xi Jinping. "So we should try to accept China's 12-point plan where it is acceptable."
He added that if the United States alleges that China's 12-point proposal is not independent by joining hands with Putin in the war, it can also be questioned that in the case of NATO, the West and the United States, which has always provided a lot of weapons to Ukraine. Raising a war or to end a war. In his opinion, this is a protracted war and the real victims are the people of Ukraine.
