(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on March 22, 2023 announced the expansion of the Public Financial Management Reform Program (FMIS) in the remaining national and sub-national institutions.
He said the Ministry of Economy and Finance continues to have ambitions to expand the use of FMIS to include budget implementation units and state budget expenditures throughout the country, especially to further integrate the new digital revolution. To existing and new functions to be developed by FMIS, including the transformation of current and paper-based manual procedures into fully digital procedures.
He added that "civil servants must be ready to learn more and embrace changes in the way they work, increase immunity quickly, and keep pace with social and economic developments." "Digital."
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth also said that the Ministry of Economy and Finance, through the FMIS Project Management Team, has achieved a number of major goals in response to the 2023 plan. The fourth phase of the Public Financial Management Reform Program and the FMIS Expansion Plan includes:
1. Completed the preparation and development of the system to fully implement the FMIS for all 5 additional ministries and institutions
2. Complete the preparation and development of the system to implement the procedures for payment of debt service in Chapters 50 and 66 by FMIS in full at the Ministry of Economy and Finance
4. Completed the design and development of the system to deploy the core functions of FMIS to the budget of 10 new delegates. Completed the preparation and development of the system to deploy the budget planning function to 12 ministries-institutions, 17 central level full-fledged delegated budget units, and 25 Departments of Economy and Finance
6. Completed the preparation and development of the system to deploy the full procurement functions to the 20 central delegated delegated budget units and the 25 Departments of Economy and Finance.
At the same time, General Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth announced the implementation of the state property management function project in FMIS with 5 ministries and institutions: 1. Ministry of Economy and Finance 2. Ministry of Environment 3. Ministry of Health 4. Ministry of Interior and 5. Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries from now on.
Please be informed that the Public Financial Management Reform Program (FMIS) is one of the priority policy programs of the Royal Government of Cambodia with the vision of transforming the Cambodian public financial system towards a public financial system that focuses on results or achievements and decentralization. In accordance with international standards and practices.
