Banteay Srei district in Siem Reap province is the third district to be officially recognized as a district to end open defecation.
(Siem Reap): On March 21, 2023, Banteay Srei district in Siem Reap province is the third district to be officially recognized as a district to end open defecation with the participation of Mr. Thong Poch, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Rural Development. And leaders of departments, units, district authorities, commune chiefs, partner organizations, government officials, students and more than 200 people participated in the Banteay Srei district hall, Siem Reap province.
Mr. Thong Poch said that in order to achieve this goal, the Ministry has been implementing the National Action Plan on Rural Water Supply, Sanitation and Sanitation Phase II 2019-2023, with a target of 90% coverage. On access to rural water and sanitation services by 2023 to achieve 100% vision.
He also called on all stakeholders to continue to participate and cooperate for better rural sanitation activities through the implementation of the National Action Plan on Water Supply, Rural Sanitation and Sanitation to achieve its policies. The Royal Government of Cambodia pays regular attention to people's health and public health to improve people's lives, reduce poverty and achieve the vision of 2030 and 2050.
He added that the rural water supply and sanitation sector is an important part of the Royal Government in improving the living conditions of rural communities by improving access to clean water and sanitation services. The Royal Government's vision is that by 2025, all people in rural communities will have access to adequate water and sanitation services and live in a hygienic environment.
He said that in order to achieve the policy on improving the quality and value of people's lives in an economic, social and cultural environment, the Ministry has set four priority strategies. According to the report of the relevant partner organizations and the report of Siem Reap on the progress of the province, the sanitation coverage rate reached 84.53%, of which 350 villages in 30 communes of 3 districts have completed open defecation. (ODF).
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has continued to mediate joint labor disputes at NagaWorld in accordance with the roles set out in the law, as well as in accordance with the wishes of workers' representatives who wish to negotiate with the company.
On the afternoon of March 22, 2023, the Ministry continued to invite the parties to the dispute to the 25th meeting to resolve the dispute with His Excellency Tes Rukhaphal, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the CEC. As the facilitator and chair of the meeting, the representatives of the workers 'side included Ms. Ry Sovandy, Ms. Hay Sopheap and the representatives of the employers' party, including Ms. Dy Seiha and Ms. Ros Bunleng.
Through lively discussions, both sides have yet to find a mutually acceptable solution, as workers 'representatives continue to demand reinstatement and employers' representatives cannot be reinstated. No.
Therefore, both sides agreed to set the next meeting date on Wednesday, April 26, 2023 at 14:30 to have the opportunity to reconsider the possibility of mutual concessions that could lead to the conclusion of this dispute.
Once again, the Ministry requested the two sides to have a high level of understanding in resolving this labor dispute, to continue to work closely with the competent authorities and relevant parties peacefully, to maintain security and public order, and to remain calm.
