Cambodian Minister of Commerce asks Indonesia to help buy rice, cassava, cashew nuts and mangoes
Mr. Pan Sosak urged the Indonesian side to import agricultural products from Cambodia, such as rice, cassava, noodles, cashew nuts and mangoes, which are potential products of Cambodia and are being promoted for export to international markets. In particular, Cambodian rice, which has won the World's Best Rice Award five times, and the last time it received the World's Best Rice Award was in 2022 in Thailand.
He added that Indonesian investors could invest in agriculture, such as setting up rice mills, processing cassava into medicinal products and packaging for domestic consumption, and exporting mangoes and fruits. At the same time, the Minister urged Indonesia Airlines to connect direct flights from Indonesia to Cambodia as soon as possible to facilitate investment and tourism flows between the two countries.
In addition, Mr. Enggartiasto congratulated Cambodia for its success in fulfilling its chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022 and expressed its intention to strengthen cooperation with the Ministry of Commerce to boost bilateral trade, investment flows and tourism. Between the two countries.
Mr. Enggartiasto Lukita also noted that Cambodia has experienced strong economic development and strong growth under the wise leadership of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who is committed to maintaining political stability, prosperity and economic stability. He especially praised the Ministry of Commerce's efforts to boost agricultural exports and attract investment.
