Banteay Meanchey Provincial Armed Forces Send 3 Thai Suspects to Provincial Court for Proceedings in Case of Cutting Two Chinese Nationals
(Banteay Meanchey): Poipet City Gendarmerie arrested three Thai nationals according to the complaint of a Chinese victim in a case of intentional violence at 11:30 on March 20, 2023 at In front of Phsar Kandal Pagoda, Phsar Kandal Village, Sangkat Phsar Kandal, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
After receiving the above complaint, the Poipet City Gendarmerie Police arrived at the scene and arrested the suspect and seized evidence to bring about the incident at the Municipal Gendarmerie. .
After being arrested and interrogated, the three suspects confessed that they had hacked into the Chinese victim. Based on the confession and the evidence, the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent the suspect to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Currently, the suspect and the exhibits were sent by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Office to the Provincial Court on Wednesday morning, March 22, 2023 to follow the procedure. Senior official of the Ministry of Labor: Over the past 30 years, until now, Cambodia has sufficient human resources, both among students, intellectuals and civil servants at all levels
This statement was made by Mr. Pech Sophoan, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, during the inauguration ceremony and graduation ceremony for students of Techo Sen Regional Polytechnic Institute at Techo Sen Regional Polytechnic Institute Svay Rieng on March 21, 2023.
The event was attended by Mr. Ros Pharith, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, a representative of the Provincial Governor, and a delegation accompanying the private sector, factory owners, enterprises, students of the Institute and many relevant officials.
According to Mr. Muth Chenda, Director of Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute, today's program is aimed at encouraging the successful graduates and to launch. Officially the new achievements of the infrastructure of Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute.
Mr. Muth Chenda said that at present, the institute has a total area of 7095 square meters, with a total of 5 buildings, which are divided into 2 school buildings, 1 workshop building, 1 dormitory building, 1 administrative building and 1 car repair workshop. And the new achievements launched today are 3 buildings, a workshop building and an administrative building renovation.
According to the statistics of trainees, the number of trainees who completed the training at the certification level from 2014-2022 was 6521, of whom 3182 were female. And the employment rate is 90% student employment rate in the private sector and 10% self-employment and public service.
At the same time, Dr. Pech Sophoan said that the fruitful achievements that we have achieved today is another new testimony that confirms the high attention of the Royal Government in strengthening and expanding the field of technical training. And human resource development in Cambodia in the new phase as we are integrating into the region and globalization.
At the same time, the employment and vocational training sector is also considered by the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly as a priority sector in promoting economic growth, job creation, ensuring equity and efficiency as stated in the Rectangular Strategy.
In addition, the Royal Government, through the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, has been preparing and submitting for approval the Roadmap on Skills Development 2022-2035 to strengthen human resources to have real skills and capabilities to meet the needs. Of the private sector in accordance with the Cambodian Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 and the Investment Law 2021.
Dr. Pech Sophoan calls on the management, staff, professors of all institutes to redouble their efforts to improve the quality and efficiency of education as a valuable contribution to the rehabilitation and development of human resources, including the development of information technology. And telecommunications, which is a priority expression of the education, technical and vocational training and is at the core of the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy.
He praised the management, leadership, teachers of the institute who have worked hard and trained a total of 2,116 students to graduate successfully today. Two men electrocuted by fish in Chhlong district, Kratie province
