Senior officials of the Ministry of Labor: We now have sufficient human resources, both among students, intellectuals and government officials at all levels.
(Svay Rieng): Dr. Pech Sophoan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that over the past 30 years, until now, we have enough human resources in both students and intellectuals. Civil servants at all levels, especially we have many public and private educational institutions have actively contributed to the development of human resources to participate in the process of building and developing the country.
Mr. Pech Sophoan made this statement during the inauguration ceremony of the building and graduation ceremony for the students of Techo Sen Regional Polytechnic Institute at Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute on March 21, 2023 with the participation of Mr. Ros Pharith, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, represented the Governor and Mr. and Mrs. are the delegates accompanying the private sector, factory owners, enterprises, students of the Institute and many relevant officials.
Mr. Muth Chenda, Director of Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute, said that today's program is aimed at encouraging the successful graduates and to officially launch. The new achievements of the infrastructure of Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute.
Mr. Muth Chenda said that at present, the institute has a total area of 7,095 square meters, with a total of 5 buildings, which are divided into 2 school buildings, 1 workshop building, 1 dormitory building, 1 administrative building and a car repair workshop. One and the new achievements put into operation today are 3 buildings, a workshop building and an administrative building renovation.
According to the statistics of trainees, the number of trainees who completed the training course from 2014-2022 was a total of 6,521, 31.82 females. Employment rate 90% of students are employed in the private sector and 10% are self-employed and in the public sector.
At the same time, Dr. Pech Sophoan said that the fruitful achievements that we have achieved today is another new testament to the high attention of the Royal Government in strengthening and expanding the field of technical training. And human resource development in Cambodia in the new phase as we are integrating into the region and globalization.
Dr. Pech Sophoan called on the management, staff, professors of all institutes to redouble their efforts to improve the quality and efficiency of education as a valuable contribution to the rehabilitation and development of human resources, including the development of information technology. And telecommunications, which is a priority expression of the education, technical and vocational training and is at the core of the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy.
He praised the management, leadership, teachers of the institute who have worked hard and trained a total of 2,116 students to graduate successfully today.
