The following is the decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Prey Veng Provincial Commissioner sets the priority direction to implement the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats to ensure high security and social order (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Prey Veng Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chhoeun Bunchorn has set a priority direction to continue to implement the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats to be more effective among some important work directions to ensure security and public order in the province. Prey Veng.
The confirmation of Major General Chhoeun Bunchon was made this morning, March 22, 2023, in the press conference of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on "Five Years of Success of Prey Veng Provincial Administration".
Lt. Gen. Chhoeun Bunchon, who recently took over as Prey Veng Provincial Police Commissioner, recently claimed that in implementing the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats, the main direction is related to traffic, drugs, gambling. Law and gangsters.
"At this point, I will work with all colleagues, police officers, administrators, inspectors and specialized offices, together with the military, to work together to implement this policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats as a high priority," he said.
According to Major General Chhoeun Bunchon, more than 300 criminal cases were cracked, equal to 91%, 116 cases of gambling were suppressed, 27 cases of law enforcement and 89 cases of education. 596 drug crimes were cracked, 1,179 people were arrested and 43 economic crimes were suppressed.
Overall, the security, public order and social security in the jurisdiction of Prey Veng province are well maintained. At the same time, the implementation of the safe village-commune policy has been expanded in all localities to create good conditions and harmony for the living and working life of the people in their daily lives.
At the same time, the province also pays attention to taking measures to prevent crimes and some inactive activities in the local area, ensuring better order.
