(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training of Family Health Care of Cambodia (RHAC) and UNFPA have jointly organized an orientation workshop on cooperation in improving access to sexual and reproductive health services among workers. Garment factory worker.
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Huy Hansong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of the Tripartite Coordinating Committee on AIDS and Drugs at the Phnom Penh Hotel on the morning of March 22, 2023. Funded by the Japan People's Fund JTF through the IPPF.
Mr. Huy Hansong emphasized that the provision of occupational health services is an important part of preventing and combating any risks that occur during the work, such as occupational accidents and occupational diseases in the workplace requires the need for procedures or Clear guidelines for the implementation and monitoring of occupational diseases aimed at developing a quality occupational risk insurance system.
On behalf of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, Mr. Huy Hansong requested the employers to increase the implementation of the guidelines on the organization of hospitals to be more efficient by providing services that are the needs of workers in the hospitals of their enterprises to Towards ensuring health and well-being in the workplace.
Ms. Saphan Somolysmey, Deputy Executive Director of Family Health Care Cambodia (RHAC), said that RHAC has been a non-governmental organization working to promote sexual health, reproductive health and rights in Cambodia since 1996. RHAC is committed to supporting all people in Cambodia with full access to sex and access to sexual and reproductive health.
She highlighted some of the challenges that hinder access to information and sexual health services and reproductive health, such as the context of climate change, the effects of the Kovid epidemic and the post-epidemic, and some negative social norms and norms. Original.
However, health promotion continues to be active under the favorable environment of the Royal Government of Cambodia's policies, trends and pragmatic management through the close cooperation of stakeholders, urging Cambodia to achieve this. In line with the commitment to meet the Sustainable Development Goals 2030 and the 25th International Conference on People and ICPD Development.
Lt. Gen. Heng Lalin and his wife join in the construction of Ponleu Pich Kiriram Phnom Kralanh pagoda in Prek Prosop district, Kratie province for 2 million Riels after the appeal of the pagoda's chief priest
Please note that the pagoda "Ponleu Pe 1 Chrkiriram Phnom Kralanh" is located in Sop Leu village, Sop Leu commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province, which is a very sacred pagoda and is far from the village. This pagoda has existed for more than 20 years, but there is a complete shortage. Today, there is no temple for monks to live in, no chan hall or synagogue, not even spoons, plates and pots to keep in the pagoda.
Since the establishment of the pagoda until now, there have been 5 abbots, but the previous 4 abbots have not been able to build a pagoda to achieve great results and have left to live in another pagoda. Continuously because of all kinds of resistance.
When it comes to the teacher named Sachak Kalyana Sennara, the chief abbot of the 5th pagoda seems to have the most outstanding ability because he knows strong magic. He knew how to look after various diseases, how to get rid of deeds, etc., which made the people near and far have faith and participated in building a pagoda with him in their respective generosity.
He built a concrete road to the pagoda, built 109 Buddha statues and other statues, and also continued to build a synagogue from the previous chief priest, but due to lack, he asked for God's help. Monks in pagodas and philanthropists all over the country and abroad, especially the head of government.
The pagoda committee said that on March 27-29, 2023, the Chief Inspector, together with the pagoda committee and the pagoda's followers, have agreed to hold the wedding ceremony of 109 Buddha statues. Cross the 9 Po trees and other achievements in the pagoda.
