Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth Closes a Meeting to Summarize the Achievements for 5 Years and Raise the Continuing Orientation of the Ministry of Public Function
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and High Representative of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, attended the Closing Ceremony of the Conference. 5 years and the direction of the Ministry of Public Function.
On this basis, in order to participate in determining the direction of further work in accordance with the strategic plan of the Ministry and the results of the meeting, Mr. General also gave some recommendations to the Ministry of Public Works and Public Administration Reform Committee as follows:
First, to amend or re-draft the Law on the General Statute of Civil Servants, which has been implemented since 1994, in order to be consistent with other legal documents and to strengthen the management of public functions more effectively.
Second: Prepare the draft National Public Administration Reform Program 2023-2035 to submit to the Head of the Royal Government for approval and promote the implementation of the National Public Administration Reform Program in stages with high efficiency.
Third, to promote the consultation and preparation of the Royal Decree on the Recruitment of Civil Servants of the Kingdom of Cambodia to ensure transparency, accountability and accountability.
Fifth, strengthen the efficiency of the performance of public officials, especially the inspection of public functions in accordance with the strategic and policy framework that the Royal Government has been preparing for the new legislature.
Sixth, increase the efficiency of administrative control, salary and management of civil servants, and continue to provide support for the management and development of human resources, especially at the sub-national level.
Seventh, continue to participate in building digital government by enhancing the capacity of the information technology human resource management system (HRMIS) to better support the management and development of human resources in public administration.
Eighth: Continue to pay attention to the living conditions of civil servants by building a safety net to strengthen the protection of the welfare of civil servants.
Ninth: Promote the study, analysis, function and structure and staffing of public institutions, and on this basis, set out the policy framework and guidelines for all ministries and institutions to develop a vision and development plan for their respective institutions to ensure Effective in - fulfilling its mission in accordance with the provisions of the provisions in force.
10th: Promote the organization and gradual implementation of performance-based management systems to have a sufficient basis for evaluating the performance of officials and to provide appropriate and equitable incentives.
After the remarks of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, High Representative of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the General Secretary also presented medals to civil servants of the Ministry of Public Works. Siem Reap Chamber of Commerce - Oddar Meanchey Discusses Investment and Business with Japanese and Korean Consulates in Siem Reap
