This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Graduation Ceremony of Nearly 5,000 Vanda Institute Students
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of March 22, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the graduation ceremony for nearly 5,000 students of Vanda Institute. The event takes place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
Dr. Heng Vanda, Director of Vanda Institute, said that the winning students include 4,705 associate and bachelor degrees, 4,221 females who graduated in the 2021-2022 academic year at the base. Phnom Penh and Siem Reap branch. Among them, there are 50 bachelor students of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, 42 females.
Vanda Institute is a private higher education institution that currently has three operating locations. One in Phnom Penh and two in Siem Reap and Battambang.
