(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, has issued nine important guidelines to the National Authority for Combating Drugs, Ministries, Institutions, Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committees and all relevant departments. Carefully organize and implement work in their respective fields and skills to increase the efficiency of the fight against drugs in 2023.
The introduction of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, made on the afternoon of March 21, 2023, on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the results of drug control in 2022 and the direction of further work in 2023 of the National Authority for Combating Drugs include:
* Second: All ministries-institutions, units of the Armed Forces of all kinds, especially the Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committee, must continue to pay attention to the implementation of anti-drug activities more rigorously and more vigorously in accordance with the master plan. The government's anti-drug strategy, strategy and campaign against illegal drugs.
* Fourth, the relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and the Ministry of Health, must strengthen and increase the control of all activities of importing and using chemicals and chemical compounds in companies, factories and promote The use of sub-national longitudinal mechanism as a staff to monitor and control the use of this chemical compound.
* Fifth: The Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committee, the Governor of the Capital-Provincial Board of Governors shall lead, promote and enhance the effective implementation of the Village / Commune / Sangkat Safety Policy, the Village / Commune / Sangkat Free Drug Policy and be assigned to participate in the implementation. Breaking news program, which is a program of the Ministry of Interior with FM 012 on a regular and effective basis.
Organize and assign the implementation of the duties and responsibilities of the Border Liaison Office (BLO) and drug-free villages, communes / sangkats of the border provinces correctly and clearly, by incorporating the mechanism of implementing the policy of drug-free villages and communes into the mechanism Of implementing the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
Seventh: All Ministries, Institutions, Relevant Units, Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committees, especially border provinces, must promote international cooperation on drug control in the bilateral, tripartite and multilateral frameworks with neighboring countries, regions and Globally, the aim is to cooperate in preventing and combating the trafficking, trafficking and illegal use of drugs and chemical compounds across border areas and within the country.
Hun Many Shares Tips for Continuing Leadership
(Siem Reap): In a meeting with the management team, professors and students of the Siem Reap Teacher Training College on the afternoon of March 21, 2023, Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia shared the key in leadership.
Mr. Hun Many highlighted what should the leaders of the next shift should understand? He stated that as a successor, one must understand three points: first: learn from one's own history, second: know the system of governing the country, and third: understand the economic situation to ensure national sustainability and development.
According to Hun Many, every stage of social development or social leadership is necessary for leaders to know the country's leadership system, which is divided into different powers. In this sense, no matter what context we are in, we should be careful about the methods and modes of use of roles to avoid misusing power in roles. Our goal is for the benefit of the nation and its people.
Another is to participate in the development and to accelerate the resilience, leaders should take turns to practice skills in addition to existing skills. That capacity is an understanding of the macroeconomic situation that is a necessary driver for livelihoods in a sectoral society, as well as the resilience of the Cambodian economy in an environment where we are at peace.
Leaders take turns to learn to train themselves while the leadership is leading. He wants to see leaders take turns with clarity and certainty.
