(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ouk Prachea, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, said that the Ministry of Commerce will register the geographical indication of Kampot-Kep salt in the near future after the association and the geographical indication book of Kampot-Kep salt. Approved and registered with the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. Ouk Prachea made the remarks at the first congress of the Kampot-Kep Salt Brand Association on March 21, 2023.
Mr. Ouk Prachea said that the meeting of the Association of Producers of Geographical Marks of Salt Products was held to prepare the Board of Directors, Executive Vice President and Auditors of the Association to register with the Ministry of Interior after meeting with the producers of salt. Several times after this meeting, the association will organize the leadership structure and the charge book has already been approved by the salt producers, traders and producers.
He added that after the coordination, the association was allowed to register with the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry will continue to organize other related work to register the geographical mark of Kampot-Kep salt in the near future.
Mr. Suon Vichea, Advisor to the Ministry of Commerce and Chairman of the Secretariat of the National Intellectual Property Management Commission, stated that the purpose of establishing the Kampot-Kep Salt Brand Traders Association is to protect and promote the talents, producers and reputation of Kampot salt quality. Kep for the benefit of producers or processors, operators and consumers.
He continued, "We expect that the registration of geographical indications will help the salt to have a more expensive export market, Kampot salt gained fame and show the potential of Kampot province and the history of the people of Cambodia." The international stage as well.
Please be informed that currently, the Ministry of Commerce has registered the protection of 4 geographical marks, including: Kampot pepper, Kampong Speu palm sugar, grapefruit, Koh Trong and Mondulkiri wild honey.
Currently, the Ministry has been implementing the project to register 4 more geographical marks, including Kampot and Kampot salt and flowers in Kampot and Kep provinces, Takeo lobster in Takeo province, Kampot fish sauce in Kampot and Kep provinces, and Koh Kong crab. .
