(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, a coal-fired power plant in Trapeang Prasat district is scheduled to open soon, while the transmission line from Oddar Meanchey to the eastern substation of Siem Reap has been built. Ready.
Speaking at a press conference on "Success in the past 5 years of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on March 21, 2023, Mr. Pen Kosal said that the provincial working group and National work is pushing for Oddar Meanchey to have electricity for all villages and communes, as expected during June or July.
He confirmed that the coal-fired power plant in Trapeang Prasat district is planned to operate in the near future, but the supply will be to Siem Reap and then to the substation in Samrong to supply in Oddar Meanchey. .
He added that many questions have been asked as to why the coal-fired power supply goes to Siem Reap. He explained that before the 19 Kovid disease in Siem Reap, the power supply was insufficient, so the coal-fired power plant was connected to Siem Reap and continued to the Samrong substation.
Please be informed that the construction of a coal-fired power plant will supply 263 kilowatts of energy, located in O'Svay commune, Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province, with an area of 212 hectares.
