Arriving in Spain, the unscrupulous Sebastian also gained the reputation of being the first person to sail around the world on a one-time adventure. Sebastian was awarded a coat of arms by the emperor of Spain, with the inscription "You are the first person to take us around the world."
However, Aka Henry de Blake, or Enrique, was the only Southeast Asian hero to travel around the world for the first time since he was captured by Sumatra pirates in the Philippines, from the Philippines to Malacca. It continued from Malacca to Portugal, from Portugal to the Pacific Ocean, and returned to the Philippines in 1521 before fleeing from the Sebastians.
