(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism, in collaboration with Chinese volunteer teachers, offers free basic Chinese language and other knowledge classes at the Ministry of Tourism (new building, 6th floor) every Monday to Sunday. Friday from 6:00 to 7:30.
It should be informed that this Chinese language study is done directly with a native teacher who has more than 15 years of teaching experience in China.
Guoyang said that the Chinese language teaching was held at the Ministry of Tourism (new building, 6th floor) every Monday to Friday from 6:00 to 7:30, including a number of teachers. Three by Kuoyang are trainers and two assistant teachers.
This voluntary participation is also because Kuoyang and his colleagues like Khmer culture, love the Cambodian people, want the Cambodian people to know Chinese, know Chinese culture, especially easy with Chinese people who come to visit or invest in Cambodia. In addition, teachers also want to contribute to the Ministry of Tourism in promoting tourism services, hospitality to Chinese tourists and attract more tourists from China.
The volunteer teacher added that in addition to knowing the alphabet, words and basic Chinese language, students will also gain knowledge related to Chinese culture, art and lifestyle.
According to the teacher, Kuoyang wants more Chinese tourists to visit Cambodia, and also wants the Cambodian people to know the Chinese language and culture. Therefore, in the future, teachers will teach Chinese related to tourism, with teachers having techniques that make it easy for students to understand and remember in a short time, and students will be able to introduce themselves about Khmer culture to tourists. China.
Ms. Chhun Sok Jing Jing, a student of Chinese language with her teacher, confirmed that she had been learning Chinese for about a month, that she could read vowels, Chinese characters and gain other knowledge. Ms. Jing Jing's goal is to speak Chinese well to use in future business, especially communication with Chinese tourists.
Nal Udom, a student from Phnom Penh Primary School, confirmed that he had been studying Chinese at the Ministry of Tourism for about two weeks and was working hard to learn to read Chinese vowels and consonants. Studying with Kuoyang is not stressful, it is easy to understand, quick to grasp and create a happy atmosphere.
At the age of only 11 years old, Udom tried to stay away from home in Teuk Thla to learn Chinese at the Ministry of Tourism without hesitation, because he wanted to know Chinese well as a bridge to continue his studies to the next level.
Please be informed that according to the announcement of the Ministry of Tourism, this Chinese language training course is to participate in improving the quality of tourism services and to promote the development of skills and human resources in the tourism sector, especially to prepare to receive Chinese tourists.
