(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), who led a high-level delegation from Cambodia to pay an official visit to study, understand and exchange experiences related to the election in Paris. The Republic of France from March 13 to 19, 2023 returned home on March 19, 2023 safely and with fruitful results.
Speaking at a press conference on his return from Phnom Penh International Airport (VIP Port), Mr. Tep Nytha, Secretary General of the National Election Committee (NEC), said that during the mission in the Republic of France, the Cambodian delegation received Well coordinated by the Ministry of Interior of France, as well as the Ambassador and officials of the Embassy of the Kingdom of Cambodia in France.
During the visit, most of the Cambodian delegates met with the French Electoral Commission and other institutions related to the French elections. Unlike the Cambodian electoral system, France has held elections since the 19th century and has continuously improved its electoral system, and France is still using modern technology.
The Cambodian delegation was warmly welcomed and exchanged experiences and information with each other. At the same time, the delegation also mentioned the work of organizing the Cambodian election to the French side. Overall, during the visit to France of the Cambodian delegation, all the programs were planned and went well.
As for the results, Mr. Tep Nytha highlighted three main points, including:
First, we learned about the electoral system in France, and Cambodia also informed the relevant institutions of France about the operation of its electoral system. We have strengthened good relations with the institutions involved in the French election.
Second, the election in France compared to the Cambodian electoral system is not the same, but there are some good technical points that we observe that France has already prepared each election procedure, and when the election was slightly modified as a decision. Basically, the application is different from our Cambodia, where we make new procedures for each election. The French election forms for their provinces or communes come in a variety of colors that are easy to spot.
