(Svay Rieng): Vietnamese traders are collecting bamboo, ping pong and acacia trees from local people in Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province, crossing the border to Vietnam through the border checkpoint.
Residents in Koki village, Tros commune, Romeas Hek district, say that a group of Vietnamese traders collect bamboo, sponges and acacia trees from people crossing the border to Vietnam every morning. Cross the border from Vietnam into the Romeas Hek district administration through the wire corridor.
Vietnamese traders have confirmed that ping pong bamboo is collected and supplied to furniture makers in Tay Ninh province, Vietnam. As for the Akasya tree, there are Cambodian chiefs who are plantation contractors from the people and high-ranking officials to sell to Vietnamese traders to collect, buy and cut directly on the plantation (contract price based on small and large plantations). These acacia trees are also sold to furniture processing handicrafts.
Tomorrow, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit will hold a press conference on "Success of the past 5 years of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of March 21, 2023, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit will hold a press conference on "Success of the past 5 years of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration" at the Office of the Council of Ministers, Freedom Hall, Ground Floor.
The speakers at the press conference were representatives of the Oddar Meanchey provincial administration. Conservationist: The Cardamom Forest is a battery for Cambodia and a source of global climate balance.
This confirmation was made during the program of "Wildlife Tour" which arrived in Phnom Penh at Aeon Mall Sen Sok on the evening of March 19, 2023, after being organized in the Cardamom Mountains: O'Som Commune Veal Veng district, Pursat province, in Khemarak Phoumin city, Koh Kong province, and in Thma Bang district, Koh Kong province, to raise awareness of the benefits of Cardamom forest.
The wildlife tour has linked the Cardamom Mountains forest protection campaign to a sustainable end to wildlife trapping (zero traps) and the restoration of large tigers, while the REDD + project, which maintains a standing forest, generates revenue. From the sale of carbon credits directly into the national economy and community.
Dr. Sou Vanna said, "The forests of the Cardamom Mountains are like a huge pump motor for Cambodia, which draws clouds from the oceans to irrigate the land, as well as Cambodia's battery chargers because of the Cardamom Mountains. "There are up to 22 big rivers and hundreds of small streams and lakes, which are the source of water and have created a lot of dams with a total capacity of about 20 percent of the country's total electricity generation."
According to Sok Kheng Vin, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Environment, the Cardamom Mountains are currently protected by border posts, patrols, and the participation of nearby communities.
It should be noted that most of the forest cover in the Cardamom Mountains is covered by dense forest, semi-dense forest, which is an important storehouse for carbon storage and mixed forest, which is suitable for rare species to value the conservation and development of the national economy. Period of development of the energy sector, sales of carbon credits and eco-tourism.
