Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the implementation of the fourth phase of the Public Financial Management Reform Program
(Phnom Penh): On Monday morning, March 20, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the launch of the fourth phase of the Public Financial Management Reform Program 2023 to 2027. The ceremony took place at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for more than 40 minutes, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia does not wait for complete peace to reform. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia's survival now is due to reform.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his life was very fragile on this reform. There are two types of Samdech's reforms: the first is political reform, which is to resolve the Cambodian conflict through negotiations, and the second is economic reform.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there were three pressures affecting political life and reforms, including: First: Disagreements within the party after the overthrow of the Khmer Rouge; Second: Wrong market regime. Between Vietnam and Cambodia, and third, sanctions from liberal countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia's reforms were carried out continuously, without waiting for foreign aid.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reform of public financial management in the past 20 years has made many historic achievements in Cambodia, both in terms of improving the governance of public financial management and in Aspects of Cambodia's socio-economic development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that, in fact, economic and social progress is closely linked to the achievements of public financial management or the national budget. In 2003, before the implementation of this reform program, the total national budget revenue was only 1,821 billion riels, while the national budget expenditure was about 2,994 billion riels.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that the Public Financial Management Reform Program has reached its fourth and final phase after being implemented for nearly 20 years, which he once presided over. Announced the launch of the first phase of this reform program during December 2004.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the cause of independence and national sovereignty, good achievements of the public financial management reform program have strengthened the ownership and role of the Royal Government of Cambodia in taking responsibility for the fate The country has reduced its dependence on foreign borrowing, which now accounts for less than 20 percent of the total national budget.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reform work has made the expectations of nation-building enshrined in the preamble of the 1993 Constitution come true: "High responsibility for The destiny of the future of the nation to reach growth, prosperity and prosperity forever "and turn Cambodia into a real" island of peace ".
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to continue to push for the successful implementation of the final phase of this reform program as planned, Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends eight key points for leaders and civil servants of all ministries and institutions. As a facilitator and operator of the Public Financial Management Reform Program.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech is very proud of the implementation of the public financial management reform program over the past 20 years, through which we can build the foundation at each stage and can reach This last stage has been very successful.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, I would like to reiterate and urge all relevant ministries and institutions to continue to actively participate in the implementation of their mission, function, program and accountability with ownership and willingness to change. The format for this reform program is set out in the "Vision and Strategy for Public Financial Management Reform Program Phase IV" document.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen hopes that the fourth phase will be successfully implemented with excerpts from good lessons and experiments, as well as continuous monitoring and evaluation to jointly address challenges and overcome obstacles. All with a spirit of solidarity, cooperation and high coordination in order to achieve the vision of building a public financial management system in Cambodia to meet international standards and excellence.
A Chinese navy ship carrying military equipment docks in Cambodia to participate in the Golden Dragon exercise between the two armies
The arrival of the Navy is to organize the 2023 Golden Dragon Exercise jointly between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army from March 23 to April 5, 2023.
The ship was led by Major General Jin Minh Tian, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Southern People's Army of the Chinese People's Liberation Army.
According to the plan, all the equipment is planned to be transported from Sihanoukville to the training ground in Phnom Chum Reak Reay, Kampong Chhnang province, the venue for the 2023 Golden Dragon joint exercise between the two armies.
It should be noted that the Cambodian and Chinese armies will hold joint exercises on a large scale in order to provide security for major events and how to help people affected by any catastrophic events. The two agreed to hold a joint exercise at the Gendarmerie Training Center (Phnom Chum Reak Reay) in Peam commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province.
