Understand the business: Exporters of processed products show procedures for exporting goods to Japan, a potential market for Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Exporters of processed foods from Cambodia to the Japanese market see that this market still has potential for the export of Cambodian goods, especially processed foods or confectionery, which is an opportunity for Cambodian producers who want to expand their market. Hold the international market.
Establishing exports to international markets has not only greatly benefited the Cambodian economy, but also helped farmers who are growing agricultural products, while the government has encouraged exporters through exemptions. 10% VAT.
He said exporting goods to Japan may not be easy, especially the type of food that requires quality production, hygiene standards and food safety. For your company, before it can be exported to Japan, it takes one year to be able to export.
As a company exporting processed fruits or dried fruits to Japan for 3 years, he explained some procedures that exporters need to know in order to be able to export to Japan:
First. First of all, we need to set a goal of what kind of goods to export, because the export of each product has different conditions, strict or light depending on the type of product. Exports of processed or dried foods are less complicated than those of fresh produce.
Speaking at the Cambodia-Japan Business and Investment Association (CJBI) Business Network Conference on March 17, Ieng Sotheara, president of the Cambodia-Japan Business and Investment Association, said that the Japanese market is a stable market if producers Cambodia can capture this market.
"Comparing the food we export to other countries and Japan is more detailed, but if the Japanese market is strong and durable," he said. "But first we have to fight and strengthen production to meet other standards."
He said that through the Cambodia-Japan Trade and Investment Association has been establishing a network between Cambodian and Japanese producers to promote more agricultural exports from Cambodia.
