Information Minister: On the day of the National Assembly vote to overthrow Sihanouk 53 years ago, soldiers surrounded the National Assembly building
(Phnom Penh): March 18, 53 years ago, was the day when the group of Prince Sisowath Sirimat, Lon Nol Intam and Cheng Heng, staged a joint coup to oust Samdech Norodom Sihanouk from the glorious Sangkum Reastr Niyum state.
The event was considered a coup, but coup plotters defended it, saying it was not a coup, but a vote of no confidence in the leadership of Norodom Sihanouk. These two perspectives are still in conflict in the Khmer view.
On the 53rd anniversary of the coup, Information Minister Khieu Kanharith recalled that on the afternoon of March 18, 1970, while sitting and talking in the corner of Mr. Kurun's house (opposite the current Tuol Kork Heavenly Restaurant). ) It is said that the head of state has been ousted because of the problem of selling land to Yeak Kong and corruption.
The Minister continued to remind that until the morning of March 19, 1970, at Indra Devi High School, a microphone was broadcast on the national radio about the discussion on overthrowing the Head of State in the National Assembly.
The Minister pointed out that it was not until 1971, when he was the personal secretary of Ung Sim, President of the Royal Council of Thrones (then the Republican Senate), that he realized that on the day of the discussion on the removal of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, the soldiers surrounded the National Assembly. And it is forbidden to speak in defense of the head of state.
According to the news, the election to remove Samdech Norodom Sihanouk from the head of state by about 86 to 3 members of parliament. According to the minister, the current parliamentary elections are under threat from the army led by Lon Nol. So this is a clear demonstration of the plot of the coup by the traitors.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith also pointed out that that day was the day that Cambodian blood was prepared to become a river because Cambodian politicians only looked at the tip of their noses and did not look at political developments outside at all.
Please be reminded that March 18, 53 years ago, was the development of a major political event in Cambodia and led to the flames of war and tragedy until December 29, 1998, when Cambodia was able to completely end the flames of war and division. Through the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. From the day of the flames of war until the day of extinction lasted almost 30 years.
"Let there be protests to take back our country," Tram added. However, Tram did not provide any official notice or provide evidence of a leak from the local law firm.
A spokesman for the Manhattan District Attorney's Office declined to comment on the matter, and Trump, who is seeking a Republican presidential candidate for the 2024 election, said he would continue to campaign. Propaganda even though he was charged with a crime.
Mr. Hun Many: Two lessons that all generations of Cambodians must remember from the historical event 53 years ago of the coup d'etat to overthrow His Majesty the King
(Phnom Penh): March 18, 2023, this is the 53rd anniversary of the coup d'etat (March 18, 1970) to oust Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk from the post of head of state and to the forefront of Cambodia. The flames of civil war spread throughout the country, leading to the killing field regime.
Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, as the next generation of young Cambodians, expressed the view that this historic event of the coup was the starting point of bringing Cambodia into the flames of civil war, continuing to bring misery to the people. Cambodia falls under the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime of 3 years, 8 months and 20 days.
Mr. Hun Many emphasized that what all generations of Cambodian children must remember from this historical event are two lessons, including:
* First: Foreign interference can lead Cambodia through uncertainty and can also create tragedy like in the past, which provides a bitter lesson for all Cambodians.
* Second, foreign interference will also be able to bring about the disintegration of the unity of the nation and the entire Cambodian people, which our society has gone through for decades, until we fully achieve national unity and solidarity after Successfully implemented the win-win policy on December 29, 1998.
