He added that the participation of new members now provides justice, trust and support for the correct leadership of the Cambodian People's Party. Through these new members, the strength and spirit of the Cambodian People's Party will be greatly enhanced and the party will be able to fulfill its duties to serve the nation, the people and the development of the country.
He recalled the history of the Cambodian People's Party, which had been active since 1951 as a country under French colonial rule. The party has changed its name following the evolving political situation in Cambodia.
He further advised that new members must pay high attention and understand each other. If we have strong unity, we will survive. The old and the new members must keep in mind that the unscrupulous always find a way to break the internal unity in order to cause us to die by division.
