What crimes has Putin been charged with?
According to the ICC, Putin's arrest warrant is for war crimes charges involving the illegal deportation of children from Ukraine, which has been under Russian control since the war of aggression began. In addition to Putin, Lvova-Belova, Russia's commissioner for children's rights, has also been charged with war crimes.
The International Criminal Court (ICC) was established in 2002 by the Rome Statute to prosecute those who commit war crimes, crimes against humanity, genocide and aggression when any member state is unwilling or unable to do so on its own. . The International Court of Justice, based in The Hague, the Netherlands, has 123 members and a budget of $ 180 million for 2023.
According to the Rome Statute, which has 123 member states, or two-thirds of the entire international community, the ICC has jurisdiction over crimes committed on the territory of a member state or a recognized or recognized state. Jurisdiction of this court. In this case, Ukraine accepted the jurisdiction or authority of the ICC twice, in 2014 and 2015.
