The Governor continued that the presence of General Thai Technology (Cambodia) in Sihanoukville is really contributing to the economic growth of the province as well as job creation for people, increase in export volume. Development of physical infrastructure, growth of tax revenue and non-tax revenue increase and maintain macroeconomic stability and opportunities for national and international investment.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun claimed that Sihanoukville is currently designated by the Royal Government of Cambodia as a "multi-purpose model special economic zone" and nicknamed the "Star of the Southwest" in accordance with the Cambodian Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 to promote growth. The national economy is a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
