Ministry of Environment brings 2,000 mangrove trees to be planted in Samrong commune, Prey Nup district to increase Cambodia's marine biodiversity and help the planet
(Preah Sihanouk): The working group of the Ministry of Environment on Saturday morning, March 18, 2023, planted 2,000 mangrove trees in the community area in Samrong commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province to increase Cambodia's marine biodiversity and Helps to balance the atmosphere.
Ms. Mom Thany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, said that the planting of mangrove trees was organized by the Ministry of Environment in collaboration with the Sihanoukville Provincial Prosecutor, relevant units, as well as local communities and is very important in the management of natural resources. Conserve biodiversity as well as improve the livelihoods of local communities and help protect the planet's environment.
Ms. Mom Thany also stated that this campaign is organized in conjunction with the celebration of the 112nd anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8, 2023 under the theme: "Women together to keep the peace for development in the digital age." With the planting of this mangrove tree, the women of the Ministry of Environment participated in creating a memorial in Sihanoukville to leave the next generation as well as improve the lives of local communities and help the planet.
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, will pay an official visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and co-chair the 20th meeting of the Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission on Economic, Cultural and Scientific Cooperation. And Technology on March 20-22, 2023. The visit is at the invitation of Vietnamese Foreign Minister Bui Thanh Son.
