(Phnom Penh): The Union of 22 Civil Society Organizations on March 18, 2023, issued a statement expressing regret over the European Union's decision to restrict the Royal Government of Cambodia to further cut the EBA. This decision is tantamount to interfering in Cambodia's internal affairs, unlike what the EU has vowed.
The Union of 22 civil society organizations believes that this restriction will not bring any benefits to the Cambodian people, instead it will bring difficulties to the Cambodian people, such as job loss and loss of income. Moreover, that decision violated the sovereignty of Cambodia, an independent country.
The decision to withdraw the EBA is a real threat to the Cambodian government, which is contrary to the promise that the EU will not interfere in Cambodia's internal affairs and that the EU is committed to helping Cambodia get out of poverty as soon as possible.
The Union of Civil Society Organizations calls on the European Union to take a long-term view of Cambodia's sovereignty and independence and call on the European Union not to cut off the EBA or the preferential treatment to continue to help Cambodians improve their lives.
The Union of Civil Society Organizations regrets that Sam Rainsy has repeatedly urged the EU to secede from the EBA from Cambodia. In the name of Mr. Sam Rainsy, who pretended to be a patriot, but he always acted to make foreigners hate Khmer and destroy the interests of their own country. The Union of Civil Society Organizations expresses despair over Sam Rainsy, an extremist politician who does not consider the common national interest.
