(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Norng Narith, a farmer who started to raise Australian lobsters or red lobster lobsters from a small size of only 3 to 4 ponds. But now he has become a farmer with the skills and experience to raise Australian lobsters, expanding his pond and ponds, as well as growing aquaculture and other livestock.
Mr. Nong Narith, 37 years old, living in Chamkar Khlai village, Svay Chrum commune, Rolea Bier district, confirmed that he currently has 5 lobster ponds and more than 20 lobster ponds that are operating and successful before and after his success. Has suffered many failures many times until today.
He is currently expanding his plantations to raise more animals to increase his family's income. In addition, he added to the business of raising shrimp by raising frogs, raising fish, raising flies and growing vegetables on the water.
Farm owner Chet Srey Oun said that in addition to raising shrimp, which is currently on the market, he is also harvesting vegetables on the water, which is technically called (hydroponic) to sell in the market, which is the first harvest. His second since increasing the business of growing vegetables on the water.
As for growing vegetables on the water, he grows from the shrimp and fish ponds, which can save space and can make the water from fish to fertilizer for vegetables. His frog farming has been similarly successful, harvesting many crops and currently hatching more.
Separately, Ms. Touch Vanny, alias Srey Oun, 36 years old, the wife of Mr. Nong Narith, also said that today her family pumped a pond to catch more than 50 kg of lobsters for customers to bring home, some will be packed and sent to distribute. Some provinces. His family has been engaged in this farming business for more than 5 years, and now his farm is named (Srey Oun Lobster Farm), which sells small and large lobsters, lobsters, meat and broilers.
