These tariffs were imposed by the Trump administration under Article 301 of the 1974 Trade Law from 2018, citing allegations that China infringed on intellectual property and technology transfer.
Imports of affected products from China will fall to about $ 265 billion in 2021 from $ 311 billion in 2017, the year before tariffs were lifted, the report said.
