ICC issues arrest warrant for Putin over war crimes in Ukraine (Video inside) (The Hague): The International Criminal Court (ICC) on Friday issued an arrest warrant for Russian President Vladimir Putin. Accusations of committing war crimes in Ukraine. This was released by the AFP news agency on Saturday, March 18, 2023.
According to the ICC, Putin was arrested on charges of war crimes related to the illegal deportation of children from Ukraine, which has been under Russian control since the war of aggression began. The president of the International Court of Justice added that the implementation of the arrest warrant will depend on international cooperation.
Moscow has denied allegations that its forces committed atrocities during the war in Ukraine. Ukraine, meanwhile, has welcomed the ICC ruling, saying Putin's arrest warrant is just the beginning. According to Kiev, more than 16,000 Ukrainian children have been deported to Russia since the war broke out on February 24, 2022.
