Immediately after receiving the complaint from the villagers, at midnight on the same day, the local police officers went to search for the above suspects, but could not find them and extracted the records from the people to complete the case file and send it to the specialized office to ask for a warrant. Arrested.
After receiving the case, the court issued two summonses and one arrest warrant, but the person refused to comply until March 13, 2023, the authorities received a warrant from the investigating judge of the trial court. Prey Veng province ordered the authorities to bring this person away.
Pursuant to Order No. 72 dated 13 March 2023 of Mr. Huot Heang, Investigating Judge of Prey Veng Provincial Court ordered the arrest of Bo Saran, 36 years old, resident of Svay Chek Village, Russey Commune, Peam Chor District, Prey Veng Province. Placed under investigation for "attempted murder, trespassing, and unauthorized possession of firearms, ammunition of any kind."
To comply with the order, Prey Veng Provincial Police immediately went to the base, but Bo Saran escaped and fled to Vietnam. Upon learning that the suspect had escaped, Cambodian police immediately contacted the Vietnamese side, sending pictures of the suspect along with the vehicle so that Vietnamese authorities could easily identify the target.
Immediately after receiving the pictures from the Cambodian police, the Vietnamese side targeted Bo Saran and arrested him for drugs. Currently, the suspect has been sent to the Prey Veng Provincial Police for legal action.
