Minister of Health urges relevant officials and partner organizations to work together to solve the shortage to end TB by 2030
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, encouraged the relevant officials and partner organizations to continue to work together to overcome the shortcomings and strengthen the strengths to better end TB. In 2030.
This statement was made by the professor at the closing ceremony of the 26th National Conference on TB Control, which was held at the Phnom Penh Hotel on March 17, 2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
The Minister of Health said that in 2023, more efforts must be made to find at least 33,000 cases of all types of TB and to maintain a cure rate of more than 90%.
Prof. Mam Bunheng urged TB research and treatment for high-risk groups, including TB, HIV, prison prisons, children's tuberculosis, tuberculosis among diabetics and tuberculosis among the elderly. Further expand the fight against drug-resistant TB by working with stakeholders, especially to encourage patients to use TB drugs properly and to the end.
In particular, it is important to maintain TB-fighting activities at hospitals, health centers and further expand the Dodgers community, which is active in the care of patients closest to their homes, and to further strengthen cooperation with classification and promotion partners. Mobilization of resources to achieve the program's goals for 2023 and beyond, including existing donors, and efforts to mobilize resources from new donors.
According to a new ranking of countries with the highest TB incidence in the world announced by the World Health Organization in the second quarter of 2021, Cambodia is not among the 30 countries with the highest incidence of TB. No more serious TB in the world for the period from 2021 to 2025.
