Prison officials: In 2022, 1,233 prisoners were pardoned and pardoned
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the officials of the General Department of Prisons, in 2022, 1,233 prisoners were commuted and pardoned.
This report was presented on March 17, 2022 at the meeting to disseminate the 2023 work direction of the Ministry of Interior and the work results in 2022 and the 2023 work direction of the General Department of Prisons.
His Excellency General Superintendent No. 1 Mao Sophearom, Deputy Director General and Director of the Department of General Administration, said that the policy of mitigation and amnesty was to review and evaluate the list of prisoners commuting and pardoning a total of 1,957 prisoners. (188 women) As a result, the meeting decided to pardon and commute 1,233 people (96 women) on the occasion of various national holidays for 2022, including:
According to the Royal Decree on Mitigation and Pardon 2021 in Chapter 2, Article 3, it is stated that the ceremonies that can request the commutation and pardon of prisoners are five times a year, including:
1: Victory Day on the genocidal regime 2: National New Year 3: Vesak festival 4: National Independence Day 5: Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon Ok Ambok.
The article added that commutations and pardons could also be made at major national festivals or events. In addition, mitigation and pardon can also be made for each of the above ceremonies, either separately or together. Regulators, Governance, Outreach and Training Capacity Building on Credit Processes and Procedures under ACSEP
This outreach workshop was chaired by Mr. Mey Van, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Project Director, with the participation of Mr. Sok Dara, Director General of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. ACSEP Project Manager, Component 1, Mr. Yun Linne, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap, Ms. Min Theary, Deputy Governor of Oddar Meanchey.
Please note that ACSEP is a project of the Royal Government that will contribute to strengthening the value chain of some competitive agricultural products, such as cassava, mangoes, cashew nuts, vegetables and domestic chickens in six target provinces, including: Siem Reap. Oddor Meanchey, Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Tbong Khmum and Preah Vihear.
This project will help:
* Facilitate access to credit for agro-industrial enterprises and agricultural communities.
* Promote market relations among agro-industrial enterprises and agricultural communities and improve food safety and quality.
* Improve the connection of the transport network from the production farm to the market.
