Ministry of Commerce: During Khmer New Year, Gasoline prices are likely to increase slightly due to international market trends
(Phnom Penh): A spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce said that during the upcoming Khmer New Year, the price of gasoline in Cambodia may have some trend, but the Royal Government will try to make the oil affordable and ensure the amount of oil. Enough to serve the needs of the people during the New Year with a lot of travel.
Pen Sovicheat, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, said the slight increase in oil prices was due to a slight increase in oil prices over the last 10 days to about 50 riel per liter. International oil prices have also started to rise slightly.
"As for the question of whether oil will rise until April, it will affect the travel or the happiness of the people," he explained. I would suggest that based on the current oil trend, it may increase slightly but not much, and we are trying to keep the amount of oil sufficient to serve the general consumption of the people, especially during the dry season. Travel a lot.
At the same time, the Ministry of Commerce and importers have been working together to ensure that the amount of oil will be sufficient for sale and keep the retail price of oil (regular gasoline and diesel) at a reasonable price, not to rise too much. Importers also have stockpiles of oil to supply the ministry's requirements.
