(Phnom Penh): Japan has decided to provide a grant of $ 145,692 for the construction of a community technology center in Bati district, Takeo province, under a grant for the Small-Scale Human Security Project (Kusanoni Grant).
This grant agreement was signed on March 17, 2023 by Mr. Ou Noo Atsushi, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia and a representative of the Recipient Institution at the Embassy of Japan with the participation of Dr. Chea Van Det, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications.
Recipient: Department of Post and Telecommunication, Takeo Province.
In this project, a community technology center will be built at a public school in Bati district, Takeo province. Despite the growing demand for IT-savvy employees in Cambodia, many young people in rural communities do not have many opportunities to study information and communication technology and digital technologies due to lack of infrastructure and programs. Study information and communication technology.
As a result, their low IT and IT skills and knowledge become part of the barrier to getting a job. The project aims to improve the situation, and we expect it to benefit approximately 8,000 people as well as about 1,000 students in the area through the establishment of the first Community Technology Center, which will provide opportunities More in the study of information and communication technology and digital technology.
Japan's Kusanoni Grant began in Cambodia in 1991 to support Cambodia's efforts to develop and rebuild the country at the grassroots level. The grant aims to protect vulnerable people from a number of factors, such as poverty and / or misfortune, that could directly threaten their lives, livelihoods and dignity, as well as promote their self-reliance. Communities.
Since 1991, the Government of Japan has provided more than $ 66 million to local authorities and NGOs to implement 707 Kusanoni projects throughout Cambodia.
