(Phnom Penh): Through the public forum in the special live program on income tax for 2022 of the General Department of Taxation, Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, responded to some complaints about Pay value added tax (VAT) and withholding tax.
Mr. Kong Vibol explained that the value-added tax does not require all members of the public to pay taxes, but requires enterprises to collect from customers who are consumers and pay taxes to the state. Therefore, when an enterprise collects VAT and considers it as its income without declaring or falsifying invoices, it is illegal. Taxes cannot tolerate such illegal acts.
He stressed that tax obligations do not require all taxpayers to pay taxes, but follow the law.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, explained the procedure for filing a tax complaint to all taxpayers if they do not agree with the General Taxation. The tax department can file a complaint.
An explanation of the procedure for filing a complaint was made during a special live broadcast on the 2022 Income Tax of the General Department of Taxation on March 16, 2023.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that according to the law, it takes 30 days to file a complaint against a tax official if the taxpayers find that the tax officer is incorrect Complain to the tax litigation commission or court. He stated that for filing a complaint, there must be testimonial documents to acquit.
He also said that if the legal deadline of 30 days is exceeded, the General Department of Taxation will not allow the appeal because it has expired the statute of limitations.
