Long live peace, bring the soul of national culture back to the motherland! Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen receives Cambodian jewels demanded from abroad
After Cambodia achieved national peace, its lost treasures, some of which had been lost for hundreds of years, were reunited. On the morning of Friday, March 17, 2023, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, will receive some Cambodian jewels that have just been reclaimed from abroad. The ceremony will take place at the Peace Palace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen held this event on March 17, 2023, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the reception of some Cambodian jewels that have just been reclaimed from abroad, which was held at the Peace Palace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that this work is the result of the joint cooperation of relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Seventh Committee of the National Assembly and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, led by Mr. Hun Many, who went to the UK twice directly. To bring ancient Khmer jewelry back to the country, which is also a model of the contribution of Cambodian youth in the preservation of national cultural heritage.
Among the reclaimed Khmer cultural treasures are some important statues of Hinduism and Buddhism, as well as ancient jewelry from the pre-Angkorian and Angkorian periods, especially large stone statues such as: Iso and Preah Skant, Preah Skant Sitting on a peacock and Preah Kanes, which originated from the resort of Koh Ker, the former capital of the Khmer Empire in the 10th century AD. Which had been the target of large-scale thefts for many years during the civil war.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia supports the transfer of cultural heritage to the host country for the benefit of humanity (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, expressed his support for the transfer and return of cultural heritage to the country. Ownership for the benefit of all mankind and to be a prime example of the understanding that "the heritage of any country should return to its homeland."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this statement on the occasion of receiving some Cambodian jewels that had just been reclaimed from abroad on the morning of March 17, 2023.
Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is a small country that went through war and suffered great devastation, but now has rapidly integrated itself in the region and internationally and is also playing an active role with the international community in the global affairs of Preserve the cultural heritage and civilization of mankind.
On behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen commended the governments of various countries and stakeholders for their contribution to these great achievements.
The Prime Minister also thanked the United States Government, including the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Department of Homeland Security, the Ministry of Justice, and the US Embassy in Cambodia, especially US Ambassador Patrick Murphy for their cooperation. Good operation combined with legal and technical support to prevent and repatriate Cambodian cultural heritage.
Samdech Techo expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the Royal Government of the United Kingdom, relevant authorities and the Embassy of the United Kingdom for Cambodia, which recently cooperated well and facilitated the return of Cambodian ancient statues and jewelry to Cambodia. .
The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia considers international cooperation with UNESCO-led partners on the protection, cooperation and preservation of human heritage as an important example of positive change in public opinion as well as global moral and ethical trends. "The heritage of any country should be returned to its homeland."
