Ministry of Mines and ADB Disseminate Energy Sector Development Master Plan and National Energy Efficiency Policy of Cambodia
The PDP is Cambodia's first long-term plan for its energy sector, which includes several scenarios for a 20-year plan that includes growing electricity demand, expanding power generation and developing transmission and distribution networks.
NEEP is Cambodia's first energy efficiency policy and provides a supportive framework for future development of the sector. NEEP sets ambitious national goals for reducing energy consumption by at least 19% by 2023 compared to the energy efficiency scenario. The NEEP also identifies measures and tools that the government will prioritize and develop to support the broader adoption of energy efficiency.
The forum was attended by representatives of government institutions, international development organizations, non-governmental organizations (NGOs) and the private sector. About 80 officials attended the event, which was held at the Sofitel Phnom Penh Phokitra Hotel on March 16, 2023.
The forum was officially opened by Minister of Mines and Energy Suy Sem, who highlighted the importance of these policies in promoting Cambodia's energy interaction and responding to international commitments under the Paris Agreement.
Mr. Suy Sem stated that Cambodia is committed to increasing the use of renewable energy and energy efficiency, which will support the Royal Government's efforts to provide energy with reliability, stability and affordability.
ADB's ongoing projects support the strengthening of the national grid, the expansion of solar PV through public-private partnerships, and the acceleration of adoption of emerging technologies such as battery storage systems.
