ISLAMABAD: A Pakistani Supreme Court on Thursday ordered police to postpone the arrest of Imran Khan for another day to stem the escalation of violence by supporters of the former prime minister. This clashed with security forces at his home. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Thursday, March 16, 2023.
On Tuesday and Wednesday this week, dozens of Khan supporters, armed with sticks and chains, rallied to prevent Khan's arrest as he failed to appear in court over the indictment. Illegal sale of state property given to him during his tenure as prime minister. But Khan has denied the allegations.
An arrest warrant was issued for Khan on Tuesday this week, sparking clashes between supporters and security forces in the Lahore area where the former prime minister resides, raising fears. On the issue of political stability in the country as Pakistan is facing an economic crisis.
The legal process against Khan began after he was ousted in the early 2022 parliamentary elections. Since then, he has been demanding opposition to the election results and organizing nationwide protests that have resulted in deaths and injuries.
