Addressing his compatriots recently, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, stated that in the future, Samdech wants to make Cambodia a cashew emperor, the largest exporter of cashew nuts in Cambodia. The world.
Samdech Techo emphasized, "I want to make Cambodia a cashew emperor, because now cashew has produced the most of all, we just do not have processing. I went to the exhibition to Kampong Thom the day before, Ivory Coast had only 1.1 million tons, but Cambodia has 1.1 million tons. This does not take into account the growing crop, which is about 700,000 hectares.
According to data from the Cambodian Cashew Association, Cambodia is the largest producer and producer of cashews in ASEAN and in the world. But the challenge is that Cambodia exports more raw cashew nuts than processed nuts, with annual exports of around 600,000 to 1 million tonnes. Therefore, Cambodia needs to invest in processing to export more processed cashew nuts and reduce the export of raw cashew nuts to get more value.
A senior official at the Ministry of Commerce and a national cashew policymaker has expressed optimism that the goal of turning Cambodia into a cashew export empire will be achieved in the near future.
"How fast it takes to achieve this goal depends on the joint efforts of all stakeholders, including state institutions, the private sector and stakeholders, but in the past, both the public sector And the private sector as well as development partners are strongly committed to the development of the Cambodian cashew sector. "I am confident that we will be able to achieve this goal in the near future."
He added that if the government wants to accelerate the cashew sector, the government must encourage local investors with more capital to invest in processing for export rather than waiting for foreign investors.
In addition, he sees some work that the Royal Government must intervene to achieve the cashew export ambitions, including:
1: Cashew Association wants the Royal Government to help establish a special economic zone or agro-industrial park with a factory processing only agro-industrial crops to help farmers become grain processors to sell to companies or factories in the special economic zone. Process export standards.
2. Provide special interest rate loans to the agricultural sector so that the agricultural sector can grow faster.
"Providing all special tax exemptions to factories, enterprises or handicrafts that process cashew nuts and agro-industrial crops is also necessary."
4. Ask the Agricultural Authority, especially the Ministry of Agriculture, to provide technical advice to local farmers so that they can spend less and help them cope with climate change.
The Rural Development and Agriculture Bank (ARDB), which serves the Royal Government's agricultural policy, has also adopted credit policies and procedures aimed at intervening in the procurement, construction, warehousing, processing and export of cashew products to boost the cashew sector. Get better and raise more funds for the sector.
According to the association, in the world, the countries that grow and produce cashews include Brazil, Senegal, Guinea-Bissau, Guinea-Bissau, Ivory Coast, Benin, Burkina Faso, Tanzania, Nigeria, Cambodia, India, Vietnam, Indonesia and the Philippines.
