(Svay Rieng): The Anti-Drug Bureau of Svay Rieng Provincial Police arrested a Vietnamese national with 16 packets of ketamine powder, which was intended to cross the border into Vietnam through Prey Vally International Border Crossing in Prey Vally Village, Thmey Commune, Kampong Ror District.
After the arrest, the suspect, 35-year-old Nguyen Khanh, was sent to Svay Rieng Provincial Court and remanded in custody by an investigating judge on the afternoon of March 15, 2023.
Brigadier General Keo Sotha, Deputy Commissioner for Narcotics Suppression, confirmed that the suspect was arrested on March 12, 2023, when he intended to cross the border into Vietnam. The arrest was made by the Anti-Drug Task Force of Svay Rieng Provincial Police in collaboration with the Prey Virey International Gate Police Force and the Kampong Ror District Police Inspectorate.
He confirmed that after the crackdown, the police sent the suspects and exhibits to the Svay Rieng Provincial Police for inspection and then sent the samples to the Anti-Drug Department of the National Police to check the weight of the packaging and the drugs. For the suspects, the judge has already issued a temporary detention order at Svay Rieng Provincial Prison.
