Ministry of Education instructs educational institutions to promote the study of Khmer culture and civilization to cultivate and strengthen the spirit of patriotism
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has instructed both public and private educational institutions to promote the study of Khmer culture and civilization in order to cultivate and strengthen the spirit of patriotism, as well as to participate in the preservation and promotion of Khmer culture and survival. Grow more.
The Ministry of Education's instruction comes after a lack of awareness of Cambodian children about their culture and civilization. Dr. Hun Manet in the past has also expressed concern about this deficit. He proposed to strengthen the education of Khmer culture, civilization and morality in educational institutions, especially the level of general knowledge.
In order to raise awareness of Cambodian culture and civilization, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has instructed all public and private educational institutions to implement the following guidelines:
1. All public and private educational institutions shall prepare and find documents related to the expansion of knowledge on culture and civilization, as listed in the appendix below, in the school library in response to the students' studies.
2: Establish a mechanism for accessing reading and study in the library by dividing shifts or scheduling clearly and making it easy to read, study and research.
3. Encourage students to read, study and research on these documents, with the guidance and coordination of the class teacher or teacher specializing in Khmer language, Khmer literature and social studies, as well as providing good and accurate services from the librarian.
4: Encourage students to borrow and inspire students to buy these books to read at home by the teacher to ask questions such as questions or exercises and check the improvement later.
5: Relevant units, school management and those in charge of technology must promote, monitor and evaluate the implementation of the study of the content of Khmer culture-civilization thoroughly and effectively.
6: Organize monthly exam subjects, semester exams and national exams in Khmer language and Khmer literature and social studies.
7. The Curriculum Development Department must prepare a budget for the treatment or copying to be placed in the library in response to the actual needs of some public educational institutions that are not able to serve in a timely and effective manner.
8. The Department of Curriculum Development must cooperate with relevant units and institutions, development partners by raising funds to support and serve the quality and sustainability of Khmer culture and civilization.
