This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Distributes Diplomas to Over 4,000 Build Bright University Students
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, March 16, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the graduation ceremony for 4,566 students of Build Bright University, 2,032 females. The graduation ceremony took place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
Dr. Diep Seiha, Rector of Build Bright University, said that the graduates have associate degrees, bachelor's degrees, master's degrees and doctoral degrees. They graduated in the academic year 2019-2020, academic year 2020-2021, and academic year 2021-2022 from the main location of Phnom Penh, Takeo, Stung Treng, and Ratanakkiri. These graduates also include 46 indigenous students, 18 of whom are female.
According to the survey, Dr. Diep Seiha said that 95.88 percent of the students who received this degree were employed, of which 76.36 percent were employed and 12.84 were non-academic. Percentage and employment as self-employed equal to 10.81%.
Build Bright University is one of the oldest higher education institutions in Cambodia. The university has been involved in human resource training since the 2000-2001 academic year.
