Spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court: Statement by Co-Lawyer Kem Sokha is a misrepresentation and misleading to the public (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Spokesman On the night of March 15, 2023, the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court issued a statement stating that the statement of Mr. Kem Sokha, Co-Lawyer for Human Rights, is a false statement and misleading. Public.
On 14 March 2023, the Co-Lawyers for the Defense of the Defendant Kem Sokha issued a statement on "Violation of Kem Sokha's Right to Assist Lawyers", stating that there was obstruction and barriers to entry Seek legal advice with the client, which makes it impossible for the co-lawyers to exercise their rights and obligations to the client.
A spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court confirmed that so far the prosecution has not received any request from the Co-Lawyers to meet with Kem Sokha. On the other hand, the statement of the co-lawyers defending the rights of the above convicts is a misrepresentation and misleading to the public because:
In the section of the decision of the Criminal Judgment No. 182 "M" dated March 3, 2023, in point 3, it was decided: to put the accused under judicial supervision, requiring the following obligations: Below:
1. Do not leave the premises of the house No. 97, Street 313, Village 7, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, unless authorized by the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
2. Do not meet any person, both Khmer or foreign, directly or indirectly through the technology system other than family members, except with the permission of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, according to the necessary requirements only.
