Ministry of Labor issues guidelines on suspension of employment contracts for factory workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags sectors affected by the global economic crisis
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a directive on the suspension of employment contracts for factory workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags sectors affected by the global economic crisis.
* US $ 20 from the Royal Government and US $ 15 from the employer for the suspension of the employment contract for 7 to 14 days * US $ 40 from the Royal Government and US $ 30 from the employer for the suspension of the employment contract for 15 days Days to 1 month.
To receive this allowance, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training recommends the following:
1: The owner or director of a factory in the field of textiles, garments, footwear and travel products and bags must:
Disseminate and inform widely and openly to the workers who have to suspend their employment contract about the obligation to provide (1) Khmer ID card number and (2) personal phone number (or telephone number of spouses, children, parents). Or siblings) for the Ministry to use as a basis for transfer of benefits through Wing Specialized Bank in accordance with the period of suspension of employment contract
- Prepare a list of workers who have been suspended from work properly in the form attached in Appendix 3 of this instruction, requiring workers to put their thumbprints on their name to confirm the Khmer ID card number and number. This factory-made phone is absolutely right.
In case of termination of the suspension of employment contract (return to work) before the deadline specified in the permit to suspend the employment contract, a letter must be notified to the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training for at least 2 days (of Work) before the return day in the form of a letter as in Appendix 4 of this instruction.
- Responsible before the law in force for all information provided to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and must be reimbursed to the Royal Government for any conspiracy to falsify information in order to obtain permission to suspend employment contracts and receive payment. Sponsored by the Royal Government.
The owner or director of the factory who fails to openly disclose to the workers the above information requirements or fails to give the workers a thumbprint to recognize the Khmer ID card number and the telephone number they have compiled shall receive Responsible for paying the workers the allowance of the Royal Government.
Within 2 working days after receiving the letter requesting the suspension of the employment contract with sufficient references, the Labor Inspector may visit and verify at the factory.
The Ministry would like to remind the workers to cooperate in providing the Khmer Nationality Identity Card and the telephone number that can be contacted to the factory, as well as to check the Khmer Nationality Identity Card and the phone number in the list of workers to suspend the employment contract. Properly before the thumbprint confirms the accuracy of these two pieces of information.
Any worker who fails to provide the Khmer identity card and telephone number to the factory means that he / she has volunteered not to accept the government subsidy.
3. Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training After granting permission to suspend an employment contract, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training shall make a copy of the suspension contract in the form of a letter as in Appendix 5 of this instruction to the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Ministry of Industry and Science. Technology and Innovation, Ministry of Commerce and relevant provincial / municipal administrations.
The Ministry would like to confirm that the contract suspension allowance will be applied for factories in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags industries that have been granted a contract suspension from April 1, 2023 onwards. In particular, the suspension of employment contracts implemented before April 1, 2023 must be followed by an agreement between the employer and the workers.
During the suspension of this employment contract, in order to ensure the harmony of professional relations and enhance labor productivity, the Ministry encourages factory owners or directors to discuss with the Garment Training Institute of Cambodia (CGTI) or other training institutes to provide training in legal skills. Involved in the field of labor, soft skills and necessary technical skills in the factory to workers, especially administrative leaders and department heads.
Chamkarmon District Administration Instructs Colrimix Owners to Apply for Tourism Licenses, Location Opening Permits and Other Permits for Doing Business Legally
(Phnom Penh): With the permission of Mr. Kieng Leak, Governor of Chamkar Mon District, the Chamkar Mon District Administration Working Group led by Mr. Mao Boneth, Deputy Governor of Chamkar Mon District, on March 15, 2023, inspected the location of Cool Remix at B&C booth in China Market, Street 78, Village 14, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
The team visited the site and found that there were 10 patents, patent tax certificates, business registration certificates and snooker boxes and 66 gaming machines in operation, and no illegal gambling was found.
The team then advised the owners to apply for a tourism license and location permit and other permits from the relevant institutions and not to allow any kind of illegal gambling and drug trafficking in the location.
