"The Danish government has agreed to set up a fund for Ukraine with a total budget of $ 1 billion by 2023," the Danish Ministry of Finance said in a statement. Of the 179 members of the Danish parliament.
The aid fund will be divided into three sections, with the largest amount going to military aid of nearly $ 800 million. Civilian assistance for humanitarian and long-term reconstruction efforts will receive $ 170 million, and $ 57 million will focus on business assistance.
In addition, the Danish government also plans to allocate funds for 2024-2027 to cover the cost of replenishing military aid to Ukraine both in 2022 and in 2023. This.
