Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng reminded the authorities at all levels to take care of some other work at the local level, such as taking care of the people by protecting them by providing them with clothes and money to protect the security and order at the local level, even though he does not have a framework. Despite the state, he has helped a lot with local security, in collaboration with the commune police administration.
Preventing drug problems is much more important than helping to crack down on drug-related crimes at the grassroots level. As for traffic accidents, we have a new law, and for drivers who have drugs in their body, which must be checked and the driver's license must be revoked.
In that, Samdech emphasized that all the people whose names are on the voter list, because the election day is approaching, each time, our citizens can not avoid the expired ID card, but the commune chief can confirm if there is a name. In the existing voter list.
Management of security, order, entry and exit in the border area, the municipal administration must prevent the maintenance of border posts and the legal crossing of people. Move the people to stop illegal logging and continue to resolve land disputes out of court more effectively, reducing the number of disputes and reducing the number of disputes to a minimum.
Increase the frequency of holding public forums at the grassroots level with the people to grasp their requests and resolve them in a timely manner. Solutions and Public Services: Through the OWSOs in cities, districts, communes, sangkats, registrations, identity cards, and other areas, to citizens, senior officials of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia urge electricity service providers to improve the quality of electricity supply. To the people
(Phnom Penh): Senior officials of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia urge all electricity service providers in Cambodia to improve the quality of their services by cleaning the network, repairing the network and maintaining the network regularly to provide Convenience to users.
Dr. Teng Sokhomal, Executive Director of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, said this at the meeting to review the work results of 2022 of the Rural Electricity Association on March 15, 2023.
"The issue of stability and quality of supply is something that has been around for a long time, not just now, and it is not going well yet, so we just need your continued involvement to make it happen," he said. Providing better quality services by cleaning the network, such as cutting branches, cutting things, etc., repairing the network and maintaining the network, etc. "
At the same time, he reminded all electricity license holders to abide by the 14 conditions to improve the electricity supply to the people and not to violate the service area specified in the license issued by Electricite du Cambodge (EDC). Some licensees have supplied electricity in violation of areas occupied by others, leading to problems.
Mr. Try Chhun Heng, President of the Rural Electricity Association, said that to date, there are 427 licensed electricity providers operating in 25 provinces, including 123 active members.
He added that the electricity providers have worked hard and budgeted to expand the distribution network in their licenses to meet the needs of consumers and contribute to the development of sufficient electricity supply in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, March 16, 2023, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the graduation ceremony for a total of 4,566 Build Bright University students, 2,032 of whom are female. The graduation ceremony took place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
Dr. Diep Seiha, Rector of Build Bright University, said that the graduates have associate degrees, bachelor's degrees, master's degrees and doctoral degrees. They graduated in the academic year 2019-2020, academic year 2020-2021, and academic year 2021-2022 from the main location of Phnom Penh, Takeo, Stung Treng, and Ratanakkiri. The graduates also include 46 indigenous students, 18 of whom are female.
Preah Vihear Provincial Administration Closes the Meeting to Summarize the Work Results for 2022, Senior Minister Meas Sophea Introduces 8 Points for Successful Implementation in 2023
