Kem Sokha's lawyers issued a statement on March 14 alleging that Kem Sokha's right to legal aid was violated. The statement came after a group of lawyers were guarded outside Kem Sokha's home, barring them from meeting with him, demanding the prosecutor's permission.
Through a telegram on March 15, 2023, Mr. Jean Malin considered that the authorities' obstruction was not a violation of Mr. Kem Sokha's right to receive legal aid.
"Just asking for a little bit of permission does not seem wrong, because it is required by the terms of the court ruling," he said. "If the prosecutor does not allow it, it is a violation of the right of the lawyer to meet with the client."
The Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Justice reminded Kem Sokha's defense counsel that even a visit to a client in prison requires the permission of the prison authorities.
Mr. Chin Malin suspected that if Mr. Kem Sokha's defense lawyer intended to meet with his client, he would just ask the prosecutor as if it were okay, unless there were other intentions?
(Takhmao): Honorary General Dr. Hing Bun Heang, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Commander of the Bodyguard Command, stated that officers and soldiers of the Bodyguard Command made great sacrifices National, territorial integrity and the people of Cambodia in the country and along the border of the temples of Preah Vihear and Ta Moan in the past.
