A statement from the Syrian president on Telegram said that Assad would meet with Russian President Vladimir Putin during his visit, along with a large delegation of Syrian ministers. The Kremlin said the two leaders planned to discuss political, trade and humanitarian cooperation, as well as expectations for a common solution to the situation in and around Syria.
The visit coincides with the 12th anniversary of the Syrian uprising, which began with peaceful protests in March 2011. The protests turned into an armed uprising after Assad used military force to crush the opposition. It later plunged into a multilateral conflict that drew neighbors and world powers to intervene and caused the largest displacement crisis since World War II.
Russia has intervened in Syria by launching a military campaign in 2015 with bombings of opposition-held areas. The campaign has helped Assad recapture much of the territory lost to rebels trying to overthrow him.
