This was stated by Mr. Chuon Dara, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce on the occasion of his participation in the opening ceremony of the 20th China-ASEAN Expo Forum held on March 15, 2023.
Mr. Chuon Dara stated that Cambodia and China have established diplomatic relations for 65 years, and through this diplomatic relationship, the two sides have strengthened and deepened bilateral ties year by year. Years and has become an inseparable steel friendship to jointly build progress, prosperity and mutual understanding.
Cambodia-China has been a strategic and cooperative partner since 2010, and this relationship has doubled and benefited both sides.
"The vision of the two governments of Cambodia and China in the framework of the Silk Road Economic Belt and the 21st Century Maritime Silk Road is committed to working together to promote the building of a single Cambodian-Chinese community and to increase the scale," he said. "Bilateral trade to exceed 12 billion US dollars by 2023."
He highlighted Cambodia's potential products for export to China, such as rice, cashews, bananas, mangoes and many other potential products.
Mr. Chuon Dara confirmed the 20th China-ASEAN Expo 2023, in which the Ministry of Commerce will cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to organize business, investment and tourism forums during the exhibition, requesting the Chinese side to co-organize to ensure results. Better.
Ou Quoc Qian, Economic and Trade Adviser at the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, said that the China-ASEAN Expo is an important forum for open cooperation between China and ASEAN.
Every year, the China-ASEAN Expo invites Chinese and ASEAN leaders, guest ministers and business leaders to come together to build consensus, enhance mutual trust and deepen cooperation.
He added that the 20th China-ASEAN Expo will create more business opportunities for Cambodian enterprises.
