(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, on March 14, 2023, presented a Certificate of Appreciation to Mr. Seang Chenda, Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Documentation Center, on behalf of the Documentation Center of Cambodia at the 2022 Annual Meeting. 2023 of Kampong Cham Provincial Administration.
On that occasion, Mr. Un Chanda also recalled the people who worked in the fields, dams and canals without time to rest during the Khmer Rouge regime, which caused the people to be weak, which we must remember.
Kampong Cham Documentation Center is one of the five branches of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, including 1) Prey Veng Provincial Document Center, 2) Anlong Veng Peace Center, 3) Takeo Provincial Document Center, 4) Koh Thmor Documentation Center, and 5) Kampong Cham Provincial Documentation Center.
Kampong Cham Provincial Documentation Center continues to carry out its core work at the grassroots level in compiling educational and disseminating documents on the history of the Democratic Kampuchea regime that ruled Cambodia from April 17, 1975 to January 6, 1979.
Since the Kampong Cham Provincial Documentation Center was officially established on July 1, 2021, the center has been open to the public, survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime, delegations, teachers, students and thousands of young people who have visited and studied. Kampong Thom Provincial Governor Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for a 2,000-Meter DBST Road in Sangkat Damrey Choan Khla, Stung Sen City (Video inside)
