(Phnom Penh): Joint Working Group to inspect the duty to close the new type of tax stamp for cigarettes (Joint Working Group) of the General Department of Taxation (OPD) and the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia (AEC) on March 13. 2023 organized a workshop to promote the implementation of the duty to close the new type of tax stamp for cigarettes.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Ming Ban Kosal, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Taxation and Co-Chair of the Joint Working Group.
Dr. Ming Ban Kosal pointed out that in the past, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has issued a number of prakas and regulations related to the implementation of the duty to close the tax stamp for cigarettes, and the Ministry of Economy and Finance has been continuously updated in accordance with the situation. Doing business and the development of the national economy.
He also asked all cigarette businesses to participate in declaring income tax properly and in a timely manner to avoid tax re-assessment by auditing or investigating tax offenses. Serious fines or penalties. In addition, it can also lead to charges of money laundering offenses that are subject to criminal penalties.
Please be informed that the dissemination workshop on "Implementing the duty to close the new type of tax stamp for cigarettes" focuses on three main topics, including:
First, Laws and Regulations Related to the Obligation to Seal New Tax Stamps for Cigarettes and the Rules for Supervising the Implementation of New Tax Stamps for Cigarettes by Mr. Moeng Soklao, Deputy Director of the General Taxpayer Management Department of the General Department of Taxation and Deputy Chairman of the Working Group
Second: Provisions related to the import of cigarettes by Mr. Hor Sinath, Assistant of the Excise Department of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia
Thirdly, the publication of health warning message on tobacco product package by Dr. Ray Rany, Director of Tobacco or Health of the National Center for Health Promotion, Representative of the Ministry of Health.
