(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, March 15, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the opening ceremony of the 5th Asia-Pacific Conference on Persons with Disabilities 2023, which was held at Sokha Hotel in Phnom Penh.
Four Asia-Pacific Disability Conferences have already been held, the first in Thailand in 2009, the second in the Philippines in 2012, the third in Japan in 2015 and the third in Japan. Fourth, in Mongolia in 2019, when the conference agreed to ask Cambodia to host the fifth conference in collaboration with the Asia-Pacific Rehabilitation Network.
The conference will discuss in detail the challenges and opportunities in the field of disability that have been encountered in the past to address together through the sharing of good experiences of speakers from different countries to build a confident and inclusive future plan. Sustainability.
The 5th Asia-Pacific Conference on Persons with Disabilities on Environmental Development was organized under the theme “Strengthening the Social and Economic Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities During and After Outbreaks. "Kovid-19 through community-based environmental development."
The conference aims to promote the economic environment of people with disabilities in the region, promote social welfare and social protection for people with disabilities, strengthen cooperation and all-party partnerships to enhance the effectiveness of development in Environmental communities, share good experiences, testimonials and innovations in community development during and after the Kovid-19 outbreak.
The conference runs for three days from Wednesday the 15th until Friday the 17th of March. The conference was attended by about 700 dignitaries, national and international dignitaries, senators, members of the National Assembly, the Deputy Prime Minister, Senior Ministers, Senior Ministers and relevant officials from various ministries and institutions.
