Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Opening Ceremony of the 5th Asia-Pacific Conference on Persons with Disabilities
(Phnom Penh): This morning, Wednesday, March 15, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening ceremony of the 5th Asia-Pacific Conference on Persons with Disabilities 2023, which was held at Sokha Hotel in Phnom Penh.
Four Asia-Pacific Disability Conferences have already been held, the first in Thailand in 2009, the second in the Philippines in 2012, the third in Japan in 2015 and the third in Japan. Fourth, in Mongolia in 2019, when the conference agreed to ask Cambodia to host the fifth conference in collaboration with the Asia-Pacific Rehabilitation Network.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on the national and international community to continue to work together to implement the Sustainable Development Goals on Persons with Disabilities, the United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and the Incheon Strategy to provide real rights to people. Have a disability.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that at present, the challenges of public health, economy, society and geopolitics have been seriously affecting the lives of the general population, especially the disabled and other vulnerable people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that on the issue of the Cambodian war, there is enough bitter experience that can be documented as history, and in fact "war can not end with war". In this sense, only a peaceful settlement of disputes through dialogue, negotiation and consultation can achieve lasting peace.
* In order to contribute to the promotion of people with disabilities in the community and in the process of socio-economic development as much as possible, Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages and offers the following four views:
First, all development activities, including social, economic, political and cultural activities, must encourage and promote the maximum participation of people with disabilities at the community level in order to achieve inclusive development in both aspects and roles. Of development.
Second, increasing cooperation between the people, government, development partners and civil society is encouraged to share experiences, exchange of information technology and practical excellence, especially the good ideas of the three-day discussion of this conference. An entry into the deepening of disability development plans at the community level.
Third, I would like to encourage more cooperation in organizing specialized skills training and using appropriate techniques for the education of people with disabilities to improve the ability and access to high-paying jobs, as well as make people with disabilities more involved. More complete and equal rights in the labor market in both the private and public sectors.
Fourth, I would like to encourage you to continue to strengthen, implement and expand community development in an effective and comprehensive environment, and call for joint participation in the spirit of the one-person system in implementing the Jakarta Declaration on Asia-Pacific Disability Decade 2023-2032 for the benefit of people with disabilities both nationally, regionally and globally.
