MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin said on Tuesday that what was happening in Ukraine was to justify Russia's existence as a nation. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, March 14, 2023.
In a statement to workers at an airline factory, Putin reiterated his claim that the West was trying to divide Russia.
"For us, this is not a geopolitical task, but the task of the survival of the Russian state, creating the conditions for the future development of our country and our descendants," he said.
Putin also accused the West of using Ukraine as a tool to wage war against Russia and cause the country to fail strategically.
The United States and its allies have said they are helping Ukraine defend itself from imperial aggression that has devastated Ukrainian cities, killed thousands of civilians and forced millions to flee their homes.
After obtaining the right to build and invest in 2019, the company sought to find sources of investment and construction partners with high experience, choosing Power China from China, which has experience in the construction of hydropower projects. Electricity in Cambodia in the past.
The construction of Stung Pursat 1 hydropower project started in February 2022. Until now, the company has paid attention to the construction and achieved some results, including demining of unexploded ordnance on 566 hectares, clearing forest in The main location of the project covers an area of 566 hectares, as well as the construction of access roads to the dam and the main location of the project, a total of nearly 36 km.
The project is in the process of building some important infrastructure, including the construction of a dam. The project is scheduled to be completed and commissioned in 2026.
On the morning of March 14, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen personally inspected the construction process of this dam. The Prime Minister welcomed the investment and construction of the dam.
According to Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the President of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), the hydropower was built under the BOT (construction, operation and transfer to the Royal Government). Mr. Keo Rattanak emphasized that after the construction is completed, the company will operate with the hydropower for 37 years and will hand over to the Royal Government of Cambodia.
In an interview with the press, Mr. Keo Rattanak welcomed with great pleasure the construction of this dam. Mr. Keo Rattanak emphasized that this hydropower has high value for the national economy and the consumption of the people.
Mr. Keo Rattanak claimed that this hydropower project, in addition to providing hundreds of jobs to the people, also helps provide additional electricity for Pursat province as well as the framework across the country. In addition, this project also helps prevent floods in the rainy months to flood some areas such as Pursat, Kandeang and Bakan.
In addition, the Stung Pursat 1 hydropower project also provides water for people to use and irrigate in the dry season.
According to Mr. Keo Rattanak, in addition to the benefits mentioned above, the Stung Pursat 1 hydropower project also provides benefits for the tourism sector.
According to Keo Rattanak, Cambodia currently has a total of nine hydropower sources. At the same time, Cambodia has a total capacity of about 4,000 megawatts, which makes Cambodia have enough electricity for the people to use and serve the industry. Economic, Social and Cultural Council holds a meeting to review its work in 2022 and raise the direction for implementation
