Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "Some people have spoken out against the use of hydropower, but they also demanded a solution for them." How to solve? Oil is too expensive, coal is said to pollute the environment, hydropower is being destroyed, and some areas are being flooded. "So do we have to go back and burn the kerosene lamp and burn it again?"
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that electricity not only meets the needs of the people, but also meets the needs of industry and tourism.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the 1990s, Cambodia used only about 30 megawatts of electricity, but now it uses up to 2,200 megawatts. Currently, Phnom Penh only needs up to 1,000 megawatts of electricity, while in the past it needed only 30 megawatts.
Due to the epidemic of Kovid 19 and the war between Russia and Ukraine, which has increased the amount of raw materials for electricity generation for 2022, the government has issued a loss of about 200 million US dollars on electricity. This was confirmed by Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia.
Today, Cambodia has the capacity to generate 3,400 megawatts of domestic energy from solar, hydropower, biomass, coal and oil, and the current demand is only about 2,200 megawatts. That means we have the ability to produce more energy, no problem.
