In a televised speech, Males said the Australian government had called more than 60 leaders, including those in the Pacific and Southeast Asia, to inform them. Agreement on nuclear-powered submarines with the United States and the United Kingdom under the framework of the AUKUS Tripartite Security Agreement.
The leaders of the United States, Britain and Australia on Monday announced further details on how Australia should purchase nuclear-powered submarines under the AUKUS tripartite security agreement, which was established more than once. 18 months ago.
Under the AUKUS agreement, which aims to block China's growing influence by maintaining "free and open Indo-Pacific", Australia will buy three nuclear-powered submarines from the United States for more than 368,000 US dollars. Million dollars with the option to buy two more units after the first phase of the agreement, which will be done in the early 2030s.
The three countries also pledged to cooperate on AI capabilities, supersonic weapons and other advanced technologies, and the United States will increase the deployment of nuclear submarines to visit the country's ports. Australia in the coming years.
