(Pursat): In the morning of Tuesday, March 14, 2023, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, inspects the progress of the construction of Stung Pursat 1 hydropower plant and talks with people affected by the project.
After obtaining the right to build and invest, the company sought to find sources of investment and construction partners with high experience, choosing Power China from China, which has experience in the construction of hydropower projects in Cambodia. In the past.
The project is in the process of building some important infrastructure. The project is scheduled to be completed and commissioned in 2026.
Pursat provincial governor Khoch Rida said the project would affect 347 families. Of these, about 342 families, equivalent to 98 percent, have already resolved the compensation policy.
For impact management and compensation is divided into three conditions. The first condition is for 12 families with houses and land in the project area. Each family received 80 square meters of house and 5 hectares of cleared agricultural land in Taing Yor village, Bramoy commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
The second condition for 60 families affected by agricultural land and homelessness in the project area. Each family received 5 hectares of cleared agricultural land in Tuol Krous village, Bramoy commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
The third condition is for families with only huts and land in the project area, 218 families. The 218 families agreed to receive cash compensation. Compensation fees are settled according to the study, which is determined by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Separately, about 43 families after the actual study, 37 families were not affected and 6 families lost their owners.
The Stung Pursat 1 hydropower project is the second hydropower project in Pursat province after the Atai hydropower plant. Stung Pursat 1 hydropower is highly studied and evaluated for economic benefits.
Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and a representative of the Royal Government in charge of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), said that in addition to providing hundreds of jobs to the people, this project also provides additional electricity for Pursat province as well as the framework. Nationwide. In addition, this project also helps prevent floods in the rainy months to flood some areas such as Pursat, Kandeang and Bakan.
According to Mr. Keo Rattanak, in addition to the benefits mentioned above, the Stung Pursat 1 hydropower project also provides benefits for tourism.
