(Phnom Penh): The Supreme Court on March 13, 2023, upheld the sentence of a defendant who was sentenced by the court to 30 years imprisonment in a previous murder case.
Recall that the victim was killed by her boyfriend, tied to an electric wire, tied with a rope, tied with her hands and feet, then wrapped the body in a blanket and tied with a rope from the outside, entered into a large bag, and then dropped in a pile. Garbage to rob the victim's motorcycle and mobile phone in Borey Peng Huoth, 42c, Tumnup Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok on November 15, 2016.
The verdict was announced by Mr. Khim Ponn, Chief Judge of the Supreme Court. The victim in this case is Keo Kanha, 19 years old, an employee of Club 55, living at 1147, National Road 2, Group 12, Prek Tanou Village, Sangkat Chak Angre Leu, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
In this case, Yen Sopanha was sentenced by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on August 8, 2017 to 30 years in prison for "premeditated murder" under Article 199 of the Criminal Code.
At that time, the accused appealed, but the Phnom Penh Municipal Court of Appeal upheld the verdict of the lower court. Defendants continued to appeal to the Supreme Court. It should be noted that the accused was arrested on November 17, 2016 in Koh Thom district, Kandal province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this while Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen officially inaugurated the screening of the movie "Son Under the Full Moon" on Monday evening, March 13, 2023.
The film "Son under the full moon", which is a historical film and reflects the life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen in the cause of the motherland, has been completed.
This is a film about the real life of Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit during the Lon Nol War, the coup d'état of Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King, the escape into the Mackie forest during the Pol Pot genocidal regime, the crossing into Vietnam to Seeking the strength of patriots to liberate the country from the Pol Pot regime, the reunion of the wife of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen after the liberation on January 7, 1979.
This film shows the life story of Samdech Techo from his childhood, having to leave his parents and siblings in his hometown to study in Phnom Penh, living with monks in Wat Neak Voan.
This historical film is about 52 episodes and took more than a year to shoot. The production team selected 103 key actors, at least 500 characters and 500 other troops to perform in the big scenes.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that the film related to this national historical event cost about 6 million US dollars to produce. The budget for this film is not the national budget.
In the premiere of Son Under the Full Moon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the organizing committee led by Ms. Hun Mana and the staff of Bayon TV to organize this program. Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his gratitude and appreciation to all the actors who participated well.
