Angry over indebtedness, creditors break into a house, kill a dog, cut down a tree, dismantle property, destroy property, insult and threaten to imprison a debtor
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hul Setha, who lives on Lum Road, Anlong Kgan Village, Khmuonh Commune, Sen Sok District, Phnom Penh, said that recently, his creditors broke into the house, killed the dog, cut down the tree and dismantled the rubble. No one took his property, insulted him and threatened to imprison him because his creditors were angry that he did not pay the full amount owed.
For these matters, Mr. Hul Setha described that he actually borrowed money from the creditors of Cambodian-American citizens to invest in the business, and he also repaid a large number of creditors under the contract, but Unfortunately, when Kovid outbreak broke out, there were closures almost everywhere, making the economy not functioning properly, resulting in erratic payments, slowing down, at which time creditors multiplied interest plus large sums of money.
After learning that the creditors were transferring the title without the debtor's consent, he decided to file a lawsuit to protect his legal interests. On December 9, 2022, the President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Taing Sunlay, issued a protection order to him.
However, on March 2, 2023, at 14:15, the creditors came to break into the house unilaterally without the presence of the landlord or any authorities. Then, they killed two dogs and cut down trees, looted and stole household items at will, which seemed like a robbery. .
Mr. Hul Setha said that he was shocked when he came home to see the dog as a beloved pet trapped in a cage and was strangled to death, ruthlessly dismantled luggage in the house arbitrarily. There is no doubt about the law.
Seeing such a situation, he also filed a complaint to the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior to prevent illegal activities on February 3, 2023, and on February 4, 2023 at 2 pm, criminal police officers came down. They were detained for questioning at the ministry, but were later released on bail.
Finally, he or she is a party to the debtor's request and request to the creditor to repay the money he received and the interest set by law and to arrange legal proceedings. For the offenses committed by the creditors with their parties, they also ask the court to handle the procedure according to the law.
