Chinese shoe factory relocates from Myanmar to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Due to the political crisis in Myanmar, a Chinese shoe factory based there has now decided to move back to invest in Cambodia due to Cambodia's peace, political stability, rapid development as well as goals. More policies to encourage investors to come to Cambodia.
Mr. Hu Chao Huy, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Alvin Su Shoe Company, confirmed this to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training on the morning of March 13, 2023, on the occasion of seeking support for the establishment of a shoe factory in Cambodia, located in Samrong Tong commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province, is scheduled to open in June 2023.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng thanked the President of the company for his trust in Cambodia, and Cambodia also welcomes all investors who have invested here, including Cambodia's export market for footwear, bags and travel products. To major markets such as the European Union, the United States, Japan and so on.
On that occasion, the president of the company told some of the history of the company to the Minister, the company needs nearly a thousand employees to produce 700,000 pairs of shoes per month to export to Europe and the United States. He wants the minister's additional guidance on law enforcement in Cambodia, as his factories, which operate in China and Myanmar, are well involved in law enforcement.
In response, Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that Cambodia has a very clear strategic plan for the development of this sector, if something goes wrong, there will be a mechanism to solve it. The Minister also advised Alvin Su to join any association to receive legal training and protection from the association.
He also asked companies to comply with Cambodian laws, especially the Labor Law, the Social Security Law, the Law on Trade Unions, the Better Factories Project in Cambodia (ILO-BFC) and other labor-related regulations.
