Ha ha! RFA really needs a diesel engine! This is their independent newspaper, brothers and sisters! " Declaring Kandal Province as a Mine-Free Province, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth Urges to Continue Educating People on Mine Dangers
(Kandal): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on March 13, 2023, presided over the ceremony to "Celebrate the Declaration of Mines in Kandal Province." "
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, Dr. Mao Phirun, Chairman of Kandal Provincial Council, Mr. Kong Sophorn, Governor of Kandal Province and Mr. Heng Ratana, Royal Government Delegate in charge. Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) and many other stakeholders.
He said that the enforcement of relevant laws and regulations, combined with education and training aimed at reducing mine risk, has also contributed to the steady decline in mine casualties and explosive remnants of war. In fact, the number of victims has dropped sharply from 4,320 in 1996 to 41 in 2022.
In Kandal province, operators cleared minefields and explosive remnants of war in a total area of 9,780,210 square meters, finding and destroying 2,873 anti-personnel mines, 49 anti-tank mines and remnants. 94,289 other explosives and a total of 11,733 people.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth requested the Mine Authority, all national and international operators to continue to provide close cooperation with local authorities at all levels to increase their active participation in education and awareness raising. Landmines and explosive remnants of war to communities, students and boys and girls living near minefields and explosive remnants of war.
