The award ceremony for the winners of medals and coaches from the 11th ASEAN Para Games 2022 was held this morning, March 13, 2023, with the participation of Dr. Prof. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and other stakeholders at the Ministry of National Defense.
There were 29 gold, silver and bronze medal winners, as well as coaches and assistant coaches who received incentives from the Royal Government. According to the Royal Government sub-decree, one gold medal (one discipline) received 40 million riels, one silver medal received 30 million riels and one bronze medal received 16 million riels.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh thanked Mr. Hun Many, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, for leading the delegation of the 11th ASEAN Para Games with great success to bring honor to our motherland. These results really show the strong will of the Royal Government under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to promote sports for the disabled in Cambodia on an equal footing, both regionally and internationally.
According to documents obtained by Reuters, the Indian Ministry of Law believes that despite various forms of social relations, the legal recognition of marriage must be granted only to heterosexual relations and that the state has a legitimate interest in custody. This discipline.
The Ministry of Law notes that "living as a partner of the same sex is not a substitute for an Indian family with a spouse and children." "Courts should not accept requests for a change in the entire legislative policy that is deeply rooted in India's religious and social norms."
In a historic verdict in 2018, India's Supreme Court upheld a law banning homosexuality. Currently, more significant developments are being seen on LGBT rights. Same-sex marriage is a sensitive issue because openly talking about homosexuality is taboo for many in this socially conservative country of 1.4 billion people.
