A fire burns more than 20 houses in Kampong Chhnang city
(Kampong Chhnang): A fire broke out along the riverside of Phsar Krom in Kampong Chhnang city on the morning of March 12, 2023, causing damage to many houses.
Hing Phop Meena, Governor of Kampong Chhnang City, said by telephone that the fire broke out in the house of a fishmonger and then spread to 27 houses with more than 30 families. A total of 42 houses were affected in the incident, which is still preliminary information.
Brigadier General Ear Bunthoeun, Deputy Commissioner and Spokesman of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police, said that in the case of the house fire, the fire brigade of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police used 10 fire trucks and intervened. Extinguished with water using nearly 100 cars to control the situation.
As for the extent of property damage in the case of the fire, the authorities and local authorities are conducting a total research is not yet clear.
According to local sources, the fire was started by a homeowner who had a fish grill for sale in the backyard, which caused the fire to burn and spread to nearby houses. In a row.
