Four institutions jointly support SMEs in Cambodia to have the ability to manage business expansion and seek partners from Japanese investors
(Phnom Penh): Four institutions have collaborated to support small and medium enterprises in Cambodia to have the ability to manage and expand their business, as well as have a higher ability to attract partners with Japanese investors.
Mr. Khim Leang, Vice President of the Cambodia-Japan Trade and Investment Association, said that the cooperation will create capacity building courses for business owners to strengthen their business management capacity to more effectively ensure the sustainability of their business.
In addition, through the coordination of the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center and the Cambodia-Japan Trade and Investment Association, will help expand the network of Cambodian entrepreneurs to have the opportunity to cooperate with Japanese investors to help sustain their business. The number of Japanese seeking investment opportunities has increased significantly.
Mr. Taing Nguon Ly, Executive Director of the New Business Training Center "Techo" said that the purpose of signing the MoU is to attract foreign investors, especially Japanese investors to cooperate or support businesses, especially start-ups. Meet the challenges of doing business.
Dr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Cambodian Entrepreneurs, said that Cambodian entrepreneurs will provide funding for potential businesses to organize their businesses, as well as help establish and expand their network with successful business owners and potential investors.
Mr. Mar Yarith: The information may be the same, but information experts can find the most attractive angle.
