(Svay Rieng): Mr. Lim Seang Heng, Governor of Bavet City, on the morning of March 11, 2023, attended the official inauguration of the gate of the pagoda and other achievements in Wat Po Thmey called Wat Bavet in Chrak Leav Village, Sangkat Bavet, Bavet City. Svay Rieng province, which cost about $ 200,000 to build.
Venerable Sek Phanith, Chief Bishop of Wat Po Thmey, also known as Wat Bavet, said that the achievements, including the three gates of the pagoda and the statue of the Buddha, which has been officially inaugurated, have now begun construction. From 2020 until the end of 2022, it has been completed with a total construction budget of nearly 200,000 dollars, with the participation and support of Buddhists near and far, both in the country and abroad.
The Chief Bishop would also like to thank all the philanthropists who have donated materials and suffixes to build many achievements to be used as relics of the pagoda for Buddhists to worship in the future in the form of Buddhism, the state religion. Most people worship and practice from the beginning to the present.
Mr. Lim Seang Heng said that all these achievements came from the initiative of Venerable Chao Chao Athikar Wat, Lok Ta Achar, many other Buddhist pagoda committees who have mobilized philanthropists both near and far to help build. It bears fruit in many achievements to be kept in the pagoda so that the Buddhists can perform rituals and keep the precepts according to the Buddhist tradition.
"Obviously, today we all celebrated together and also participated in the official inauguration ceremony for the benefit of all Buddhists in the future," he said.
(Koh Kong): To promote the health sector, two health post buildings donated by Dr. Hun Manet and Ms. Pech Chanmony were officially inaugurated on March 10, 2023 in Kandol Commune, Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province. And in Toul Korkir commune, Mondul Seima district, Koh Kong province.
The inauguration of the health post was presided over by Mrs. Mithona Phuthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province and attended by Mr. Hak Leng, Deputy Governor, Mr. Toa Moeng, Director of Provincial Health Department, Mr. Krouch Borey Seiha, Governor of Botum Sakor District and all government officials. Monks, teachers, students, many people as well.
Mr. Hak Leng said that the health post building to be inaugurated is 14 meters by 8.5 meters, has 4 rooms, 4 bathrooms, equipped with solar lights, fences around the total budget of $ 85,900. He also urged doctors to follow professional ethics and serve the people well according to their role in providing medical services to the people.
Speaking on the occasion, Ms. Mithona Phu Thong said that the country is peaceful, stable, developed due to the efforts under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen for the nation and people. Therefore, the people must keep the peace together, unite to keep the peace, so please go and vote for the CPP in the future.
The Provincial Governor, on behalf of the local authorities and representatives of the people of Koh Kong Province, would like to thank Dr. HUN Manet and Ms. Pech Chanmony for spending their own money to build two more health posts and equip them. Doctors, wells, roads and other materials, as well as donated to the people some food budget.
