Raimondo was quoted by Reuters as saying that the two countries would map the electronics supply chain to the joint venture and identify opportunities for joint ventures and technology partners.
India has been looking to attract more big investments under a $ 10 billion incentive plan for chip and screen manufacturing, aiming to become a major player in the global supply chain.
Last year, the South Asian country stepped up fiscal support for new domestic semiconductor plants to cover 50 percent of project costs. According to Reuters.
Vietnam's exports fall 10% as global demand slows
HANOI: Vietnam's exports fell 10 percent in the first two months of this year from the same period last year as declining global demand continued, Vietnamese government data showed on Thursday. Affect the country's exports. According to Reuters.
Exports from January to February fell to 49.64 billion US dollars due to a drop in exports of clothing, footwear and electronics, Reuters reported, citing a report released by the Vietnam Customs Department. The country supplies some of the world's largest companies.
January-February garment exports fell 19.6 percent from a year earlier to $ 4.55 billion, while footwear exports fell 16 percent to 2 percent. $ 76 billion.
Vietnam reported strong economic growth of 8% last year, but economists have warned that the country faces problems with declining global demand.
In February, Vietnam's total exports rose 10.3 percent year on year to 26.05 billion US dollars, while imports rose 1 percent, according to a report released by the Customs Department on Thursday. , 3 percent to $ 23.25 billion. According to Reuters.
