Minister Thong Khon: Cambodia's World Heritage Tourism Network is really special, not easy to have any country like (Video inside) (Kampong Thom): The World Heritage Tourism Network in Cambodia is very special for Tourist travel is associated with providing a wealth of knowledge on history, culture, religion, architecture, environment and education, which is not easy for any country to have, according to Minister of Tourism Thong Khon.
Addressing the closing ceremony of the 7th River Festival on the night of March 10, 2023 in Kampong Thom province, Minister Thong Khon said that Cambodia has a lot of cultural potential in terms of tangible, intangible culture, history, heritage and other diversity. Of Khmer culture.
The World Heritage sites that Minister Thong Khon is referring to include the Angkor site in Siem Reap, the Preah Vihear temple area in Preah Vihear province, and the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site in Kampong Thom province, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, as well as the Koh Ker temple site in Preah Vihear province. Request more World Heritage Sites
Angkor is the ancient Khmer capital of the Angkorian period for more than 600 years from the beginning of the 9th century to the middle of the 15th century, which is widely known to international tourists. The site was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1992.
The Temple of Preah Vihear is a cultural, historical and religious heritage site with a fine design, accompanied by a magnificent climate on the top of the Temple of Preah Vihear. It is a large Hindu shrine of the ancient Khmer Empire and is still a sacred place of the modern Khmer people. The site was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 2008.
Sambor Prei Kuk is the site of the ancient Khmer capital of the Chenla period from the 7th to the 8th century, a cultural and historical heritage site and a major Brahmin site for the Khmer people since ancient times. The site was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 2017.
Mr. Thong Khon added that the friendliness of Cambodians is not like others, other foreigners, if they smile, smile from the eyes, but Cambodians are smiling from the heart.
Minister Thong Khon also called on inter-ministerial institutions, all stakeholders and all people to strive to build a more prosperous nation both now and in the future, especially to maintain peace, because peace is the most important factor. Attract more national and international tourists to visit our country.
NEC to Observe French Electoral System from March 13-19
(Phnom Penh): According to the Notification of the French Embassy dated March 6, 2023, Ms. At Sophie, Director of the Department of International Security Cooperation of the Ministry of Interior and Overseas Territories, invited a high-level Cambodian delegation to visit Official observation of the French electoral system in Paris from 13 to 19 March 2023, while Cambodia is preparing for the upcoming parliamentary elections in July 2023.
