Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Meets Women International Police Day on March 8
(Preah Sihanouk): On the afternoon of March 10, 2023, Major General Chuon Narin, Police Commissioner of Preah Sihanouk Province, presided over the 112nd International Women's Day March 8, 2023. "Let's keep the peace for development in the digital age."
On that occasion, Major General Chuon Narin instructed the female police force to pay attention to discipline, role, duty, social peacekeeping, strengthen self-development for additional knowledge, skills and abilities in line with the digital age to be more equal. Equal to work and hold high positions as a male police force.
The Commissioner General also gave a bouquet of flowers to each woman and a budget of 80,000 Riels each, as well as organized a solidarity meal for the female police force.
During the closing ceremony of the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that although the FATF had removed Cambodia from the gray list, the Royal Government of Cambodia was not satisfied with what it had achieved. That is to say, the next step is to make sure that Cambodia does not fall into the gray list again.
"Even though Ang Fat decided to leave the gray list, we must not be satisfied with the results we have achieved," said Sar Kheng. "We need to continue to work harder to build trust from all walks of life, including domestic and foreign investment and relevant tourists."
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that the Anti-Money Laundering Commission is preparing a summary report and will then hold a meeting to gather opinions or input and set out further implementation measures to ensure that Gray or black banks can not come back and we should not be proud to forget that doing something harmful may fall on the gray list as before, because we have fallen once.
At this point, the Prince stressed that this work can not be done by any individual or unit alone, but must be together with the Royal Government and the people involved. At the same time, the fight against human trafficking and other non-traditional crimes remains an issue that we can not reduce because it also affects money laundering or other issues.
The leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia has shown continued commitment to the fight against money laundering and terrorist financing and the financing of genocide.
In July 2020, Cambodia also issued a law on anti-money laundering and terrorist financing. The law aims to guarantee anti-money laundering and terrorist financing by setting measures to control, prevent, suppress and eliminate money laundering and terrorist financing. Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Urges Health Department Leaders to Introduce Its Officials to Ban Discrimination Against CED Card Holders
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, urged the leaders of the Provincial Health Department to advise their officials not to discriminate against cardholders to access medical services because medical expenses are the cost of Government.
The provincial governor said so on the afternoon of March 10, 2023 at the closing ceremony of the meeting to review health work in 2022 and set the direction for 2023 at Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department.
Mr. Un Chanda continued that the current cardholders are facing challenges because in the past, the cardholders went to the hospital for medical treatment, but were avoided by the medical staff, especially the accounting office. .
At this point, they may not yet understand that the treatment for the cardholders is a government budget, that is, all medical accounting services must be recorded, then the cost of treatment is paid by the government. Replacement money.
The provincial governor added that in relation to the above cases, the leaders of the Department of Health should advise their officials, such as health centers, referral hospitals, not to be discriminated against and to take care to serve them. It is especially good for those who hold the ID card, regardless of the color, please serve them equally.
At the same time, the Governor of Kampong Cham Province also commended and thanked all the leaders and health officials of Kampong Cham Provincial Administration for their hard work and responsibility on the development of the health sector in the province. 2022, which has contributed to sustainable economic and social development.
On that occasion, the provincial governor instructed health officials to pay attention to inspect the quality of food hygiene in restaurants to increase confidence to avoid problems that affect people's health.
On the other hand, if selling unhygienic food, it can also affect their business, so our team of doctors to explain to restaurant owners on a regular basis, including in the factories.
