(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Police has released a short educational video related to the benefits of obeying all traffic laws to help protect both their own lives and the lives of others who travel on the streets through knowledge. Obey traffic signs, traffic lights, drive safely and wear the right seat belt for safe travel.
Speaking at the first National Assessment of the Economic Development Cooperation Fund (EDCF) National Assessment Workshop jointly conducted by the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Export-Import Bank of Korea, Ms. Kim Kyung-hee noted that Cambodia Is EDCF's second largest partner.
This workshop aims to share the results of the national assessment of EDCF's involvement in Cambodia over the past 20 years. The Ministry of Economy and Finance of Korea has been tasked with evaluating the implementation of the EDCF project in Cambodia in order to gain lessons learned and expand future EDCF interventions in Cambodia.
A day before the workshop, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, and Ms. Kim Kyung-hee, Director General of the General Department of Financial Development of the Ministry of Economy and Finance of Korea, met and discussed ways to enhance their role. EDCF in the long run as one of Cambodia's key development partners based on the strategic priorities of both governments.
At the March 9, 2023 Policy Dialogue, representatives of both sides agreed to focus on key areas: digital health and green development, the three operating strategies of the EDCF Medium-Term Strategy 2023-2025. Continue to support the transport, water resources and health sector, which accounts for about 81% of total EDCF loans in Cambodia.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth expressed his pride in Cambodia as the second country among the 10 countries that cooperate with EDCF, and from 2001 to the end of 2022, the Korean side promised Concessional loans totaling approximately US $ 1.8 billion.
As a result of this commitment, 32 concessional loan agreements between the Ministry of Economy and Finance of Cambodia and EDCF were signed, totaling approximately US $ 1.6 billion to finance 28 development projects and 1 program in accordance with the development strategy. Of Cambodia based on key priority sectors including: transportation (roads and bridges), education, health, energy, irrigation, clean water and wastewater treatment systems.
The policy dialogue and seminar reaffirmed the strong bilateral development cooperation between the two countries and the two governments agreed to continue to work closely to identify and respond more effectively to the challenges facing the two countries. Development in Cambodia.
