The General Confederation of Trade Unions of Cambodia (CGCU) organizes a workshop on "Labor Dispute Resolution Procedures Sponsored by the Arbitration Council Foundation" to contribute to the development of knowledge and skills
(Phnom Penh): The General Confederation of Trade Unions of Cambodia (CGCU) on March 10, 2023 organized a workshop on "Labor Dispute Resolution Procedures Sponsored by the Arbitration Council" to contribute to improving the knowledge and skills of workers. The participating employees are 80 members representing unions, unions, federations, associations, organizations.
During the workshop, Mr. Men Nimmith, Acting Executive Director of the Arbitration Council Foundation, stated that the purpose of this workshop was to provide workers with a better understanding of labor dispute resolution procedures provided by the Out-of-Court Arbitration Council. Peace in its enterprise and increase productivity, increase the stability and competitiveness of factories.
Mr. Men Nimmith said that according to the law, we have only 15 days to resolve the Arbitration Council, and the court does not set a time limit, it can be months or years. However, the Arbitration Council stipulates that the dispute must be resolved within 15 days, unless both parties to the dispute agree to an adjournment due to the complexity of the dispute.
At the same time, Ms. Tep Kim Vannary, President of the General Confederation of Unions of Cambodia, added that 2023 is a year that the Arbitration Council has co-organized a seminar for the Board of Directors of the General Confederation of Unions of Cambodia in all fields to promote. Knowledge and skills of workplace dispute resolution procedures and provide workers with legal knowledge that is tailored to specific activities, such as joint dispute resolution in arbitration.
She added that the resolution of individual disputes in court, so the Royal Government also amended in cooperation with the arbitrator and the court to seek justice for workers, also amended some articles to raise awareness and resolve effectively. And transparency.
Once again, Mr. Men Nimmith would like to call on the trade unions to review and resolve peacefully, not to bring it to the Arbitration Council, but to resolve it through their own enterprises, factories and the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. In accordance with the law, a spokesman for the General Commission: 174 more vehicles were inspected and fined on March 10, 2023
