Senior Minister Sun Chanthol praised the company's rapid construction process. Minister Sun Chanthol welcomed and welcomed the investment in the construction of ports and logistics centers in the area as part of improving transportation, especially the connectivity of the inland waterway system, which is the government's ambition. Cambodia.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized, "Ask what is the benefit of this port? It is very profitable, we encourage more water transport. If transported by road, it damages the road and costs a lot of money. We strive to build many satellite ports along our rivers, including the Tonle Sap, Bassac, Mekong, Sekong, Sesan, Sre Pok, etc. How to transport by water to sell abroad to create jobs for people.
The senior minister also saw that the multi-purpose port and logistics center are a good strategic area for transportation, as it is the center of the country and a good place to distribute goods from the provinces around the Tonle Sap Lake and other provinces. More towards the international market.
Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, said that Kampong Leng District has a population of more than 10,000 families and is heavily dependent on farming. As Kampong Leng district is cut off by the Tonle Sap River and the Tonle Sap Lake, it is difficult to transport agricultural products to the market. If traders come to transport, the selling price is not high because it costs a lot of shipping.
The Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province welcomed the investment to establish a port and a logistics center. Through this port, not only provide jobs for the people in the area, but also facilitate the transportation of agricultural products of the people, which contributes to the high prices of agricultural products.
Kampong Hav commune, Kampong Leng district, is an area that is flooded during the rainy season and is also a place for migratory fish. Therefore, the construction of the port and logistics center also takes into account the environment and ecosystem.
Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, emphasized that the Ministry has already studied and evaluated the construction of the port and logistics center without any impact on the environment.
