(VOVworld) - Cambodia and Vietnam have agreed to speed up the process of amending the Cambodia-Vietnam Transit Agreement to include the Men Chey (Prey Veng) -Ten Nam (Tai Ninh) international border gate, which facilitates exports and imports. Import goods between the two countries.
In a meeting with Tran Quoc Khanh, Deputy Minister of Industry and Trade of Vietnam, Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, discussed the expansion of trade cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam to promote bilateral economic and trade sectors. More progress.
He asked the Vietnamese side to examine the possibility of speeding up the process of amending the Cambodia-Vietnam Transit Agreement to include the Men Chey (Prey Veng) -Ten Nam (Tai Ninh) international border gate, with the two sides currently awaiting the official inauguration. Of this international port by the heads of government of both countries only.
At the same time, he agreed to expedite the process of amending the Cambodia-Vietnam Transit Agreement to include the Men Chey (Prey Veng) -Ten Nam (Tai Ninh) international border gate as possible, as the two top leaders plan to Will inaugurate this international gate in the near future.
During the meeting, the two sides also discussed procedures and mechanisms to facilitate the export of Cambodian sugar to the Vietnamese market to avoid paying taxes under anti-diversion measures.
