(Doha, Qatar): On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, led a Cambodian delegation to the 5th United Nations Conference on Least Developed Countries (LDC5). Summit of the Group of Least Developed Countries in Doha, Qatar, March 4-9, 2023.
As the Co-Chair of the Meeting, Minister Pan Sosak welcomed the Speakers and Member States to the High-Level Roundtable and noted the strong reliance on public resources to finance the response. The need for sustainable development and response to the crisis that the least developed countries and the world are facing.
The Minister and the Co-Chair then handed over the forum to the speakers to discuss and discuss the mobilization of resources and the strengthening of global partnerships for sustainable development in less developed countries.
The speakers had a lively discussion focusing on some of the LDCs' challenges, including limited domestic resources, increased debt burden and the ability to take advantage of financial markets. The solution to this problem is to strengthen the capacity of LDCs in the areas of tax administration, efficient and effective use of local resources, combating illegal financial flows, mobility, savings and local financial institutions.
The meeting was a success and provided important input for LDCs and development partners to support mobility and efficient use of resources for sustainable development.
