Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Opening Ceremony of the 7th River Festival in Kampong Thom Province
(Phnom Penh): On Thursday, March 9, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening ceremony of the 7th River Festival, which was held at Stung Sen Park in Kampong Thom province.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen gave a 40-minute speech, the following are the main contents of Samdech:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very pleased to be invited to open the river festival under the theme "Our river for the present and the future".
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the Inter-Ministerial Commission of the Ministry of Tourism, relevant ministries, institutions of Kampong Thom administration and the private sector for jointly organizing the 7th River Festival after a three-year absence due to Kovid-19 disease.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the spirit of pre-promotion, the Royal Government has set out a number of policies to support the economy to leave negative growth in the short term, making the Cambodian economy recover quickly with 3% growth in 2021. In 2022 it will grow by 5.2 percent and in 2023 it is expected to grow by 5.6 percent.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has considered tourism as a priority sector and a "green gold" contributing to the socio-economic development of the country through the creation of employment opportunities to increase income for the people directly and indirectly promote Export on the spot, increase national income, support economic growth, contribute to the preservation of our culture and protect our environment and natural resources effectively and responsibly.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia will continue to receive further growth from the potential of resources, including natural resources, cultural heritage and history. But do not forget about the preconditions that ensure all these growths, including ensuring peace, political stability, security and full social order under a win-win policy, which is conducive to sustainable tourism development over time. Long.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has always supported and prioritized development that supports and considers the conservation of valuable resources.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has divided the Tonle Sap Lake land into three areas to facilitate management. Zone 3 is land that can not be enjoyed and can not be owned, Zone 2 is land that can be enjoyed but can not be owned and Zone 1 is land that can be enjoyed and can be owned - Owned.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the management of the Tonle Sap Lake must consider two important tasks: conservation and consideration for the living and enjoyment of the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia needs to maintain a permanent presence of peace, which is one of the biggest points related to the development of the people of the world.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that without peace, without development, without peace, there would be no respect for human rights and democracy, and without peace there would be nothing.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on people all over the country to unite to preserve the hard-won peace and not to allow any country or group to destroy peace in this country at any cost. We must all maintain this peace to ensure development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that no matter what, whoever intends to destroy the peace is not afraid to take action at any cost. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there is no peace, not to mention rights, freedoms and democracy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that in the past, Kampong Thom could not organize a meeting like now, if it is organized, there will be shelling.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects Cambodia to become the largest exporter of cashew nuts in the future.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara and relevant authorities for their efforts in demarcating land around the Tonle Sap Lake.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to continue to pay high attention to maintaining security and order, especially to promote the implementation of the village-commune safety policy thoroughly and consistently.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the relevant ministries, institutions and provincial administrations around the Tonle Sap Lake to continue to complete the survey and clearing of land from the second and third areas of the Tonle Sap Lake area to complete and quickly to give ownership to the people. People in area 1 and enjoy in area 2 and continue to enjoy in area 3.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the state has purchased all pumping stations in Kampong Thom province for a total of about $ 2 million to reduce the cost of water bags from the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen The Mekong and Tonle Sap rivers are no longer far apart through the project of connecting infrastructure between Kratie and Kampong Thom and Kampong Thom to Kampong Chhnang. Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirms that the road and bridge connecting Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Thom will start construction in 2024
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that for Kampong Thom, investing in a hotel is difficult but can be good for a restaurant.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs Kampong Thom provincial authorities to find food products to attract tourists.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed relevant ministries and institutions to continue to give priority to the development of riverine areas, especially the provinces around the Tonle Sap Lake, on the construction of necessary infrastructure to serve tourism, connectivity and transportation. In particular, examine the possibility of constructing bridges across the Tonle Sap and the Tonle Sap Lake, connecting bridges and roads from Kampong Chhnang to Kampong Thom.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia will continue its efforts to protect and conserve the environment and natural resources based on the principle of "development serves and conservation" and conservation serves development "together. "Think together, act together, take responsibility" to make the river area an attractive tourist destination for tourists.
