BEIJING: After China's major national event, the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China in late 2022, in early March 2023, another important event was held in Beijing, the National People's Congress. Across China and the General Assembly of the National People's Political Consultative Conference, often referred to by the Chinese people as the "General Assembly of the two parliaments."
The two conventions marked the beginning of a Chinese-style modernization process launched at the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China, as well as a change in the mandate of Chinese state and government leaders. Therefore, it can be said that this is an event related to determining the destiny as well as the direction of the development of the nation in the future.
Indeed, the epidemic crisis has hit the world economy hard, including China. Although China maintained positive growth during the crisis, the Chinese economy was also affected. After all, what keeps the Chinese economy resilient and vibrant is China's national policy of adhering to multilateralism and win-win cooperation with global trading partners.
In addition, China's huge domestic market, with a population of more than 1.4 billion, is an irreplaceable advantage in stabilizing its economy. This potential market is a strong impetus for China's economic growth and a capital for China to conduct trade cooperation with countries around the world.
Setting an annual GDP growth target of 5% is not an indirect one. We see that at the beginning of 2023, China reopened the country, which is a positive sign for the resumption of cross-border trade and communication between the Chinese people and the people of the countries in all aspects. China's big businessmen are also seizing the opportunity to seek direct business opportunities abroad, including raising capital, investing and investing.
The private economy is important for China's socio-economic development, employment opportunities, fiscal revenue and China's technological innovation. According to the data, the private economy contributes more than 50% of taxes, contributes more than 60% of GDP, contributes more than 70% of technological innovation and contributes more than 80% of urban employment opportunities.
Xi Jinping reiterated China's unwavering adherence to the "two fundamental national policies": unwavering adherence to strengthening and developing the economy, public property and adherence to the promotion. Encouraged to support and guide the development of the private economy. In the past, Chinese leaders have repeatedly emphasized these two basic national policies under various circumstances to encourage the private economy.
