Samdech Techo Hun Sen also pointed out that before buying this pumping station, people have to pay 1,200,000 Riels for water pumping per hectare, but after the state buys all the pumping stations, farmers only pay Only 600,000 riel per hectare, so the Royal Government has facilitated the expenses of half the people.
According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, in addition to reducing the cost of water bags for growing crops, the Royal Government also facilitates the cost of electricity, with the state charging only 480 riels per kilowatt hour.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "We have purchased all the pumping stations worth nearly 2 million US dollars. Previously, farmers in Kampong Thom province used water because the private sector used to charge 1,200,000 riel per hectare, now we have reduced the water charge to 600,000 riel, enough to pay for water. While the price of electricity for water bags for farmers is only 480 riel per kilowatt hour.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his strong hope that by reducing the cost of production, the people will get more benefits, especially profits. At this point, the prince encouraged to do this work as well as possible, both the land owned by the state and the land used to enjoy the people to really benefit from the efforts of the Royal Government.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, added that all that the Royal Government has done is not to put in place a democratic policy, but to go through the practical implementation that we have been doing and will continue to do. .
Samdech considered that peace is more valuable than anything, and if there is no peace, please do not talk about human rights and democracy, only the right to life.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the 7th River Festival in Kampong Thom province on the evening of March 9, 2023. Samdech continues to prioritize peacekeeping efforts in Cambodia.
"Whoever intends or acts to destroy the peace in our country, we are not intimidated with the use of all means and measures at all costs to maintain peace and ensure the development of our country." This is according to Samdech Techo.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that peace must come before everything, and if there is no peace, not to mention democracy and human rights, which must consider the right to life first. Samdech expects that the Cambodian people who went through the war and the genocidal regime of Pol Pot clearly understand what the Royal Government is doing for peace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalls the situation in Cambodia during the war, which could not even meet. "At all costs, we are not afraid to act to destroy the forces that wish to destroy the peace for our country."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on people across the country to unite to maintain the hard-won peace and not to allow any country or group to destroy peace in this country.
