Dr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, confirmed that the opening of this new branch will not only provide services to farmers in Battambang, but also to farmers in Banteay Meanchey, Pailin, Pursat and Siem Reap. Services here as well.
According to Dr. for Battambang, ARDB has provided nearly 30% of total loans, assisting farmers in rice cultivation, warehousing, rice milling, processing, agricultural products, animal husbandry, aquaculture and small and medium enterprises. Original.
Dr. Kao Thach continued that with the support of the Royal Government through the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which is the guardian of ARDB Bank, it has expanded its network of operations to 15 mobile offices in the provinces to provide banking services to farmers, farming communities. Rice mills, small and medium enterprises in agriculture and agro-industry.
Dr. Vong Sandab, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Representative of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, expressed his support and congratulations for the efforts of the Board of Directors, Management and all staff of ARDB Bank. Expand the scope of the bank's operations in the provinces, cities and rural areas.
He urged farmers, agricultural communities, mill owners, agricultural production and processing enterprises to continue to support and use ARDB banking services to expand their business base in order to contribute to the restoration and promotion of national economic growth in accordance with the policy of Royal Government.
Please be informed that ARDB Bank is a policy bank of the Royal Government, which was established in 1998 as a specialized bank, with the main operations focusing on providing loans to customers and wholesale loans to microfinance institutions to provide loans to the people. Farmers and farming communities.
