Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Announces Operation to Clear Mine and War Remnants in Siem Reap Province with Chinese Aid
(Siem Reap): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and WANG Wentian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, on March 9, 2023, announced the groundbreaking ceremony for a demining operation. And remnants of war equipment under the Chinese Mine Action Assistance Project in Cambodia in Siem Reap.
Heng Ratana, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), said that the Chinese government grant project has already provided CMAC units in two phases from 2018 to 2022. Total budget of 10 million US dollars.
Mr. Heng Ratana added that as a result of these two phases, CMAC has cleared a total of 74,922,784 square meters of minefields and minefields, discovered and destroyed a total of 71,558 mines and unexploded ordnance. Nuts. The project also contributes to the development of communities, providing safety and improving the lives of a total of 214,661 families.
It should be noted that for the achievements in Siem Reap, CMAC has started to clear mines and remnants of war by the end of 2022, achieving results such as clearing a total of 51,790,865 meters of minefields and minefields. A total of 29,185 mines and all kinds of unexploded ordnance were found.
