Minister Mao Ha Vannal Urges Siem Reap Angkor Thmey Airport Development Company to Accept Staff from Old Airport on Volunteer Principles
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Mao Ha Vannal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, on March 9, 2023, received a delegation from Yunnan Investment Company, the new developer of Siem Reap Angkor Thmey International Airport. Exchange Comments.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson for Civil Aviation, said that in this meeting, Dr. Mao Havanal informed about some concerns when closing the old Siem Reap Angkor Airport: how to use human resources, staff and equipment. Taken from the old airport to be smooth, and the recruitment of this staff is based on a voluntary principle.
On that occasion, Yunnan Investment Company also informed about the efforts to show the ability to manage the new Siem Reap Angkor International Airport to become a standard airport like some developed countries in ASEAN.
He said Yunnan Investment is one of the TOP 10 companies in the world with an annual turnover of $ 300 billion, with 40,000 individuals and more than 500 subsidiaries. A major shareholder in the development of Siem Reap Airport.
At the same time, Yunnan Investment Company also unveiled a satellite development project with more than 1,000 hectares of reserve land to attract investors to build special economic zones, as well as activities to support domestic production and exports.
Separately, Siem Reap Airport is currently operating as an investment by the French Airport Concession Company (SCA), which has the right to manage the three airports (Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Sihanoukville) until 2040. For Siem Reap Airport, the Royal Government of Cambodia has set up a negotiating committee with SCA to facilitate early termination of contracts.
