Russey Keo District Police Inspector: From January to March 7, 2751 Khmer Nationality Cards Distributed to Citizens
(Phnom Penh): The 7 Police Administration Stations in collaboration with the Sangkat Administration in Russey Keo District distributed Khmer Nationality ID cards to nearly 3,000 local people from January 2023 to the 7th. March. According to Colonel Heang Tharet, Russey Keo district police inspector.
Khan Police Inspector continued, “From January 1, 2023 to March 7, 2023, Khan Police Officers and Police Officers at the posts in cooperation with the 7 Sangkat Administrations distributed 2751 Cambodian Nationality Cards (Male). 1380 people).
Please be reminded that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, once said that 2020 is the fourth year of implementing the National Strategic Plan on Identification after being approved by the Royal Government in June 2016.
In that regard, Samdech Krala Hom stated that the National Strategic Plan on Identification is an important plan of the Royal Government of Cambodia with a long-term strategic vision to guide the management of identity data through modern technology and use. Identification data to improve the efficiency of providing public services to citizens.
Samdech Krala Hom stated that the reform of the identity management system is still a high priority for the Royal Government, because the identity management system is the backbone of all service systems, both public and private, and that Cambodia must contribute to Implement sustainable development goals.
Identification work focuses on two main tasks: managing identity identity and providing services to citizens. In particular, the provision of administrative services to citizens refers to the use of personal identity data to provide services to citizens, such as the issuance of birth certificates, identity cards, residence books, family books, passports, enrollment, land ownership, housing, vehicles and registration. Business list and so on.
Please be informed that 2021 is the fifth year of the implementation of the National Strategic Plan on Identification (2017-2026). In 2021, Cambodia was affected by the 19 19 Kovid Crisis, which caused a number of challenges. However, the General Department of Identification has worked hard to achieve its duties and achieved significant progress.
Major General Sithy Lod talks with 215 female police officers on the occasion of the 112th International Women's Day, March 8, 2023
(Banteay Meanchey): On March 8, 2023, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Sithi Loh presided over a gathering to celebrate the 112th International Women's Day on March 8, 2023 under the theme "Women Keep the Peace." For development in the digital age.
The celebration of International Women's Day under this theme aims to continue to highlight the invaluable value of women's participation in peacekeeping, as well as to be actively involved in accelerating development in all areas.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. and Mrs. General, Colonel, Deputy Commissioner, Chief, Deputy Chief of Specialized Bureau, Inspectors of all cities and districts, the Commander of the four mainland border police battalions and a total of 215 female police officers throughout the province.
On that occasion, Major General Sithi Loh also urged the female police force to pay attention to discipline, role, duty, social peace, strengthen self-development in terms of knowledge, skills and additional capabilities in line with the digital age to be more There is equality in the performance of duties and high positions as a male police force.
During the ceremony, the Major General, Commissioner and leaders of all relevant departments also presented a bouquet of sarongs, 20,000 Riels and a solidarity meal to the female police force.
